var tafsirData_3 = {
  "1": "Alif, Lam, Mim. The surah opens the same way al-Baqarah opened — with letters read one by one. Twenty-nine surahs begin like this, and the most honest thing the first generation said about them still stands: Allah knows best what He meant. The Prophet, peace be upon him, did not explain them, and neither Abu Bakr nor Ibn Abbas claimed certainty.\n\nThat silence at the very start of a surah that will go deep into argument about Isa, about Tawrat and Injil, is teaching. Faith includes being at peace with knowledge that belongs to Allah alone — which is exactly what verse 7 will call the muhkam and mutashabih.\n\nScholars offered reflections without claiming finality. These are the raw letters of the Arabic tongue that the poets of Quraysh used for their finest odes. Out of these same letters comes a Book they could not imitate, though challenged repeatedly. Reciting them slowly — Alif... Lam... Mim — also makes the ear sit up. A strange, distinct sound at the opening gathers attention, and into that gathered quiet comes the greatest testimony that follows.",
  "2": "Allah — there is no god worthy of worship except Him — the Ever-Living, the All-Sustaining. After the three letters comes the foundation. La ilaha illa Hu — negation then affirmation — no deity in any heaven or earth deserves love, fear, hope, dua, except Him.\n\nThen two names that hold everything else: al-Hayy, the One whose life has no beginning, no gap, no end; and al-Qayyum, the One who stands by Himself and makes everything else stand. Every heart that beats, every throne that claims power, every provision that arrives, stands only because He sustains it. If He dozed — and He does not — the heavens would collapse.\n\nThis is the same opening as Ayat al-Kursi in the previous surah, and for good reason. Al-Imran will discuss those who took Isa as god, who claimed Uzayr as son, who said Allah is poor and they are rich. Before any of those claims is entertained, the criterion is set: can your claimed god be described as Hayy Qayyum, ever-living without death, sustaining without need? If not, he is not Allah. Isa slept, ate food, grew tired. Uzayr died for a hundred years. Angels are sustained. Only the One described here remains.\n\nTo begin with this after Alif Lam Mim is to say: whatever ambiguity comes later, rope it to this clarity. The Living Sustainer does not die, does not beget, does not need partner.",
  "3": "He revealed to you the Book in truth, confirming what came before it, and He revealed the Torah and the Gospel before. The Book spoken of is the Quran, sent down to Muhammad, peace be upon him, bit by bit — nazzala — gradually, over twenty-three years, carried by Jibril.\n\nIn truth — bil-haqq — in origin truthful, in content truthful, for purpose of making truth triumph. Confirming what came before it — musaddiqan lima bayna yadayhi — not cancelling the original Tawrat given to Musa and Injil given to Isa, but bearing witness that they were truly from Him. The Quran does not introduce a new god; it confirms the same Oneness those books taught before additions and deletions entered.\n\nAnd He revealed the Torah and the Gospel — not as human biographies but as revelation — al-Tawrat wal-Injil — before, as huda lil-nas — guidance for people of their times. Same root as huda for muttaqin in al-Baqarah. Each was true guidance for its era.\n\nPlacing all three together in one verse dismantles two extremes: those who reject earlier scriptures entirely, and those who cling to them and reject the last. Believer says: all from Allah, but final Book confirms and stands as criterion over what remains. It is family resemblance: same light, final lamp brightest so earlier lamps are recognized by it, not denied.",
  "4": "Before — as guidance for people — and He revealed the Criterion. That is the second half of same sentence. The Torah and Gospel were guidance before, and then Allah revealed al-Furqan — the separator between right and wrong, truth and falsehood.\n\nFurqan here can mean the Quran itself — its title — or every criterion sent with prophets that allows people to tell halal from haram, sincere from pretender. Both meanings hold. Revelation not only informs; it separates. It cuts between pure and mixed.\n\nThen warning: those who reject Allah's revelations — after they came as Furqan — will have severe punishment — adhab shadid. After guidance that distinguishes, rejection is not ignorance but preference for darkness after light was offered.\n\nAnd Allah is Mighty — Aziz — no one overcomes Him or prevents recompense, not Nimrud with kingship, not Romans who destroyed Temple, not Quraysh who blocked Ka'bah — and Owner of retribution — dhu intiqam — Who answers oppression, not quickly out of anger but surely out of perfect justice.\n\nSo verses 2-4 encapsulate entire surah: who Allah is (Hayy Qayyum), what He sent (Book confirming, Torah Gospel before, Furqan distinguishing), and what awaits after distinction — severe recompense if rejected, mercy if followed.",
  "5": "Nothing on earth or in the heavens is hidden from Allah. After describing revelation coming down, Allah describes His sight reaching up and down, covering everything revelation will judge.\n\nMa fil-ard wa la fis-sama — nothing. Not leaf falling, not tear at night, not whisper in council that plotted against Prophet in Madinah, not funds withheld from orphans, not pride hidden behind humble speech of those who pleased people in worldly life (2:204). All makhfi becomes makshuf before Him.\n\nThis is both awe and relief. Awe for concealer mentioned in previous surah — those who hid Book for small price, those who concealed testimony, those who hid true feelings while calling Allah to witness heart. Relief for concealer who repented and corrected and clarified — and Allah turned.\n\nIt also prepares for verse 6 about wombs. If nothing hidden in heavens and earth, then certainly nothing hidden in dark womb where no eye sees embryology is fully seen.\n\nFor believer, to know nothing hidden from Allah turns vigilance into closeness. He does not police after; He sees while. You remember Him somewhere low — market, home — and He remembers you in better assembly, because He saw remembrance already.",
  "6": "He is the One who forms you in the wombs as He wills. There is no god worthy of worship except Him — the Mighty, All-Wise. From general unseen to most intimate unseen: womb. Huwa alladhi yusawwirukum fil-arham kayfa yasha — He shapes, images, colours — yusawwir — you in wombs as He wills.\n\nNot as parents will exclusively. Genetics is cause, but shaper is He. Male female, tall short, single twin, healthy test — kayfa yasha — as He wills, with wisdom. Two brothers from same parents utterly different.\n\nIf He shapes unseen child without partner, then creating Isa without father is not strange — same verb yasaawwir used. Maryam's astonishment later — how can I have child when no man touched — answered by same principle: same Shaper who forms in wombs as He wills does not need usual means.\n\nLa ilaha illa Hu — repeated from verse 2, now tied to womb-shaping. The One who shapes offspring is only deity worthy of mother calling upon for righteous child, as wife of Imran will call and Zakariya will call.\n\nAl-Aziz al-Hakim — Mighty none can overrule shaping, Wise shaping placed perfectly — not random. Even what appears as disability contains hikmah beyond first glance, which reveals later.\n\nA mother feeling child move, an expecting father anxious, both are addressed. The Artist of that image already knows child and is already worthy of trust.",
  "7": "It is He who sent down to you the Book — some verses precise, foundation of Book, others unspecific. As for those in whose hearts is deviation, they follow the unspecific seeking discord and seeking its interpretation, but none knows its true interpretation except Allah. And those firm in knowledge say, 'We believe in it, all is from our Lord.' But none will remember except people of understanding.\n\nThis verse gives method for reading Quran. Muhkamat — precise, mother of Book — umm al-kitab — clear commands, beliefs, halal haram, stories with moral. Mutashabihat — unspecific — descriptions of Allah's attributes, reality of unseen, Alif Lam Mim, details of Hour, some descriptions of Isa.\n\nHearts with deviation — zaygh — already inclined to bend, hunt through mutashabih to support desire, to twist Isa verses to claim divinity, to torture with Alif Lam Mim. They seek fitna — discord — and ta'wil — forcing interpretation aligning with desire.\n\nWhat is proper? Those rasikhuna fil-ilm — firmly grounded in knowledge — say amanna bihi kullun min indi Rabbina — we believe in it, all from our Lord. They return mutashabih to muhkam, not vice versa. They do not pretend not to think; they think deeply, then submit where limit reached.\n\nWa ma yadhdhakkaru illa ulu al-albab — only people of inner core remember. Core intellect knows when to reason and when to submit. That core is cultivated by humility, not argument.\n\nThis verse humbles all interpreters: return unclear to clear — clear is Hayy Qayyum لا إله إلا هو, Isa is servant messenger, Tawrat Injil guidance, Furqan distinguishing. Keep that in centre.",
  "8": "Our Lord — do not let our hearts deviate after You guided us, and grant us mercy from Yourself. Indeed You are the Giver. This is first dua of rasikhun. After describing firm knowledge as saying we believe, Quran gives their actual whispered words.\n\nRabbana la tuzigh qulubana ba'da idh hadaytana — Our Lord do not make hearts deviate after You guided. They know heart — qalb — turns — taqallub — and deviation can happen even after guidance, even after knowledge, as seen in scholars who hid Book for price. They do not trust own firmness; they ask Firm One to keep firm.\n\nWahab lana min ladunka rahmah — grant mercy from Yourself — min ladunka — from Your own nearness, special mercy, not just general. Mercy that keeps guidance, mercy that makes patient at Uhud, mercy that makes spend despite love of wealth.\n\nInnaka anta al-Wahhab — Indeed You are Giver — al-Wahhab — form of intensive giving again and again without payment. Only One who gives without depleted store.\n\nThis dua companion reading muhkam mutashabih. After debate about Isa, after encountering confusing things online, after feeling heart swayed — sincere believer says this. It is not long, but Prophet, peace be upon him, often said Ya muqallib al-qulub thabbit qalbi ala dinik — O Turner of hearts make firm my heart on Your religion, mother of believers saying do you fear? He said hearts between two fingers of Rahman. So they ask Giver of mercy, not achievement.",
  "9": "Our Lord, You will gather humanity for a Day about which there is no doubt. Indeed Allah never breaks promise. Second dua continues. After worrying about hearts deviating, they anchor to final gathering.\n\nRabbana innaka jami'u an-nas li-yawmin la rayba fih — You will gather humanity for Day no doubt about. Same la rayba as opening of al-Baqarah — no doubt in this Book — la rayba fih about that Day. Both connected: Book without doubt points to Day without doubt.\n\nWhy mention gathering now? Because when hearts incline to argue over mutashabih, to seek worldly desires, reminder of gathering that will settle all disputes — Allah will judge between you concerning wherein you differed (2:113) — brings sobriety. All horses that dazzled, gardens that seduced, arguments that entertained will be lined same plain.\n\nInnAllaha la yukhlifu al-mi'ad — Allah never breaks promise. Mi'ad — appointed meeting. He promised to send Furqan, to gather. Those who kept promises of spending, prayer, trust — will find promise kept.\n\nThis closes opening: Book from Hayy Qayyum revealed truth confirming before, criterion distinguishing, nothing hidden, shapes wombs as wills, some verses precise foundation others tested, firm ones respond believing and praying not to deviate and gathering. Theology set before stories of Imran family.",
  "10": "Indeed those who disbelieved — neither their wealth nor their children will avail them against Allah at all — and those are fuel for the Fire. From duas of firm knowledge to fate of those who refused.\n\nNeither amwal nor awlad — wealth nor children — two things people rely most when truth calls: money that buys influence, children that give support network. On Day gathering no doubt, currency different.\n\nWa ula'ika hum waqud an-nar — they are fuel of Fire. Waqud — fuel that keeps Fire burning, as earlier fuel of Fire is people and stones (2:24). Image horrifying. They thought wealth would ransom, children would intercede, like monsters thinking can overpower. Instead themselves become what keeps punishment alight.\n\nConnects to earlier: If nothing hidden from Allah (5), shapes wombs (6), then wealth children also from Him formation — cannot shield against Him by using what He gave against Him.\n\nModern: wealth portfolio, followers count, will not avail. Fuel metaphor asks: what are you fuelling today? If wealth spent seeking Allah pleasure (2:261 grain), it becomes garden. If hoarded to deny Furqan, its owner becomes fuel.\n\nVerse ends bookkeeping worldly assets vs akhirah assets; next verse gives historical example of those who trusted wealth children — Pharaoh people.",
  "11": "Like the way of Pharaoh's people and those before them. They denied Our signs, so Allah seized them for their sins, and Allah is severe in punishment. Ka-da'b — like habit, like custom, like way. Way of Pharaoh's people — who had wealth, armies, monuments, children heirs, claimed high lord — and those before them — Ad, Thamud, who also trusted buildings.\n\nKadhdhabu bi-ayatina — denied Our signs — same verb as those who reject revelations (4) after Furqan came. Signs included staff to snake, white hand, but they called magic. Allah seized them for sins — akhadhahum Allahu bi-dhunubihim — not random; due to sins.\n\nWallahu shadid al-iqab — Allah severe in punishment — same closing as earlier warning for concealers (2:211). Severe not hasty; punishment severe when after clear signs denial persists.\n\nPattern: wealth children not avail in akhirah, nor did in dunya when seizure came — Pharaoh's wealth did not prevent drowning, children did not help.\n\nFor listeners in Madinah — Quraysh who trusted wealth at Badr and People of Book who trusted children lineage — this precedent personal. You are walking same da'b.\n\nRemedy opposite da'b: believers who owned wealth but spent, had children but dedicated as wife of Imran did — will see different seizure — mercy reaches before punishment.",
  "12": "Say to those who disbelieved, \"You will be overcome and gathered to Hell — and evil resting place.\" Qul lilladhina kafaru satughlabuna wa tuhsharuna ila Jahannam — direct prophecy, especially to Quraysh after Badr and Jews in Madinah who doubted.\n\nSatughlabuna — you will be overcome — in this world, not only next. History confirms: Quraysh overcome at Badr, then Fath Makkah; Jewish tribes who broke treaty overcome. Tuhsharuna ila Jahannam — and gathered to Hell — verb signifies herding unwilling. Same gathering that believers prayed for earlier — He will gather humanity — but now gathering to destination evil: bi'sa al-mihad — evil resting place. Earlier earth made bed (firash) comfortable (2:22), here mihad miserable.\n\nVerse gives timeline: defeat in dunya then herd. For disbelievers threat, for believers comfort — no need despair when mocked for lack wealth; overcoming promised by Hayy Qayyum who shapes wombs and sees hidden.\n\nProphet, peace be upon him, recited this in market of Banu Qaynuqa. It happened.\n\nAnd it asks listener today: what gathering are you preparing for? If wealth children fuel Fire, overcoming in dunya leads to mihad terrible. If spent seeking mercy, overcoming leads to gardens under which rivers flow described soon (15).",
  "13": "There was certainly a sign for you in two groups that met — one fighting in Allah's path and other disbelieving. They saw them double their number with their eyes. And Allah supports with His help whom He wills. Indeed in that is a lesson for those with vision.\n\nTwo groups — fi'atayn — one fighting fi sabili Allah — Prophet and companions 313 at Badr hungry fasting — other disbelieving — Quraysh ~1000 well-equipped, fed, claiming protection of House.\n\n\"They saw them double their number with their eyes.\" Interpretation debated: believers saw disbelievers twice their size yet still fought? Or disbelievers saw believers double actual, struck terror? Both demonstrate Allah control of perception — forms in wombs as wills (6), shapes sights as wills. Psychology battlefield.\n\n\"Allah supports with His help whom He wills.\" Nasr not numbers.\n\nIndeed in that is ibrah — lesson crossing over — for ulu al-absar — those with vision, inner sight not just eyes. Those with vision see Badr not just historical clash but sign of principle: little with tawhid can overcome many with shirk when Hayy Qayyum permits; heart deviated seeking mutashabih misses sign, heart firm sees.\n\nThis verse links to testimony earlier: wealth children fuel Fire, Pharaoh seized; now eyes saw. After general precedent, concrete recent sign you witnessed. So argument not abstract; you were there.\n\nFor Uhud coming later surah, this will be prelude: Badr victory not because invincible but because supported; same support conditional on obedience.",
  "14": "Beautified for people is love of desires — women, children, heaped treasures gold silver, branded horses, cattle, and tilled land — but those are enjoyment of worldly life, and Allah has with Him excellent return.\n\nZuyyina lin-nas hubb ash-shahawat — desires made beloved, beautified — by Creator as test, or by Satan decorating? Both: Allah created love natural for spouses, children, wealth, horses (today cars), cattle (business), tilth (property). Shahawat — cravings. Not condemned as evil but as adornment — makes life continue, but when made ultimate, enslaves.\n\nList covers spectrum ancient Arabian pride then still modern: nisa — spouses, banin — children lineage, qanatin muqantarah gold silver — hoarded wealth investments, khayl musawwamah — branded fine horses — today luxury vehicles branded, an'am — cattle — business herds, harth — tilled land — real estate.\n\nDhalika mata' al-hayat dunya — that is enjoyment worldly life — mata' — temporary provision, like traveller's kit not home. Brief, fading.\n\nWallahu indahu husn al-ma'ab — with Allah excellent return — better than all listed combined. Gardens... (next verse details).\n\nThis verse honest about human love; does not say have no love, but says recognize beautification and remember better return. If love leads to disobedience, then share of those whose wealth children fuel Fire. If love disciplined seeking Allah pleasure, spending from what you love (3:92), then love becomes vehicle to excellent return.",
  "15": "Say, shall I inform you of what is better than all that? For those mindful of Allah are Gardens with their Lord beneath which rivers flow, abiding eternally, and pure spouses, and pleasure from Allah. And Allah is Seeing of servants.\n\nQul a-unabbi'ukum bi-khayrin min dhalikum — Shall inform you of better than all that beautified? Question arouses.\n\nLilladhina ittaqaw — for those mindful — muttaqin — same as al-Baqarah opening guidance for muttaqin — at Rabbهم gardens under rivers flow — not just water but rivers beneath — khalidina fiha — eternally — no expiry like worldly tilth.\n\nWa azwajun mutahharah — pure spouses — mutahhar — purified from physical defects, from jealousy spite, from menstrual harm (22). Companionship free imperfections that worldly spouses, even beloved, still have due to humanity.\n\nWa ridwanun min Allah — and pleasure from Allah — greater than gardens and spouses. Gardens delight body, pure spouses delight heart, ridwan delights soul knowing Lord pleased. Prophet said most excellent reward Allah will say to people Paradise, I have granted you pleasure so I never angry after.\n\nWallahu Basirun bil-ibad — Allah Seeing servants — sees who prefers better over beautified, who chooses gardened eternal over brief mata'.\n\nNote verse does not say leave world: world allowed as provision, but inform better. Decision becomes rational once knowing extent — trade lower brief for higher lasting — wisdom earlier defined (2:269).",
  "16": "Those who say, Our Lord, we have believed so forgive our sins and protect us from torment of Fire. This is first audible example of muttaqin voices. Not boastful claim but du'a.\n\nRabbana innana amanna faghfir lana dhunubana wa qina adhaba an-nar — Our Lord we have believed, so forgive... and protect.\n\nThey start with amanna — we believed — not we did many deeds. Faith itself presented as plea. Then ask two things: forgiveness of past sins — dhunubana — and protection from Fire — adhaba nar — future.\n\nConnection: earlier those who disbelieved neither wealth children avail, fuel Fire. These say opposite: iman, seeking forgiveness fuelled by tawhid, asking protection from Fire.\n\nSimplicity du'a teaches tawassul — seeking closeness via iman itself, not via other. We believed — so forgive — using faith as means.\n\nAnd it echoes duas of rasikhun (8-9): mercy and gathering. Muttaqin here same as rasikhun.\n\nFor us, this du'a short enough daily after acknowledging faith. After being told better than worldly desires is Gardens, immediate response believers not \"we want gardens\" but \"forgive sins protect from Fire\" — because entry depends on forgiveness more than performance.\n\nIt leads to description how they live that makes du'a sincere.",
  "17": "The patient, the truthful, the obedient, the spenders, and those who seek forgiveness before dawn. Now description of those who said du'a. Five qualities.\n\nAs-sabirin — patient — sabr at obedience when tired, from sin when tempted, in calamity when struck. Foundation.\n\nAs-sadiqin — truthful — sidq in speech, intention, covenant; opposite those who said about Allah what they do not know.\n\nAl-qanitin — obedient, devout — qunut — standing long in prayer with humility, as earlier three bowing, prostrating.\n\nAl-munfiqin — spenders — from beautified wealth earlier but now directed seeking Allah pleasure, not hoarded fuel Fire; spend from what love (92).\n\nWal-mustaghfirin bil-ashar — those seeking forgiveness before dawn — ashar — last part night before Fajr, when sleep sweetest and world quietest. At that time they ask forgiveness, as Prophet said Lord descends nearest heaven last third. Choosing that time shows sincerity, consistency.\n\nFive qualities cover heart (sabr, sidq), body (qunut), wealth (infaq), and time (istighfar at dawn). Comprehensive muttaqin.\n\nNote order: patience first, because without it other qualities fleeting. Istighfar last, because even after patience truth obedience spending, they still see need to seek forgiveness — humility caps piety.\n\nThis portrait answers what better return looked like — not only gardens but character that qualifies for ridwan.",
  "18": "Allah witnesses that there is no god except Him — and the angels and those of knowledge — standing with justice — there is no god except Him — the Mighty, All-Wise. Greatest testimony in Quran.\n\nShahidAllahu annahu la ilaha illa Hu — Allah Himself testifies to His own Oneness. If Allah testifies, what testimony greater? Then angels — pure beings worship constantly — testify. Then ulu al-ilm — people who possess knowledge — not necessarily degrees but those firm in knowledge earlier (7) who say we believe — their testimony joins divine and angelic.\n\nQa'iman bil-qist — standing with justice — qist — He maintains justice while being witness; universe ordered justly, not random.\n\nLa ilaha illa Hu — repeated twice for emphasis — closure.\n\nAl-Aziz al-Hakim — Mighty none can challenge testimony, Wise testimony placed perfectly.\n\nThis verse elevates knowledge bearers: their witness paired with Allah's and angels'. Not tribal chiefs paired, but scholars. Why? Because knowledge that returns mutashabih to muhkam, that knows shaping in wombs, that knows nothing hidden, culminates in recognizing tawhid.\n\nFor those arguing Isa divinity, this testimony demolishes. Isa was among those who needed to testify tawhid himself; he said Allah my Lord your Lord worship Him alone (51). How could he be object of testimony?\n\nAnd for believer seeking better than beautified desires, best possession is to be among ulu al-ilm who stand with Allah in this testimony.",
  "19": "Indeed the Way with Allah is Islam. Those given Scripture did not differ except after knowledge came to them out of jealousy among themselves. And whoever disbelieves in Allah's signs — Allah is swift in reckoning.\n\nInna ad-dina indAllahi al-Islam — Indeed religion with Allah is Islam — submission — same as submission of Ibrahim and all prophets earlier. Not one of many ways equal; complete system for all times: to submit face to Allah while doing good (2:112). This is Way — deen — adina — indebtedness, allegiance.\n\nWhy did People of Book differ despite knowing? After knowledge came — min ba'di ma ja'ahum al-ilm — after Torah Injil, after descriptions of final Prophet. Not out of ignorance but baghyan baynahum — jealousy, transgression between them, seeking superiority.\n\nExample: Jews knew description Muhammad but envied not from them; Christians knew tawhid but claimed Trinity to distinguish; some among People Book believed morning rejected evening to confuse (72).\n\nWa man yakfur bi-ayatillah fa inna Allaha sari'u al-hisab — whoever disbelieves in signs — swift in reckoning. Sari' al-hisab — quick account — no long bureaucracy. As earlier swift return Day no doubt, recompense rapid when comes.\n\nThis verse is both anchoring and warning. Anchoring for believer lost in many faiths talk: Way with Allah is Islam. Warning for scholar: knowledge does not prevent envy causing difference; envy can make knowledgeable differ after knowledge came. Cure: submit, not compete.\n\nIt prepares for Prophet instructed what to say if they argue (next verse).",
  "20": "If they argue with you, say, I have submitted my face to Allah and those who follow me. And say to People of Book and the unlettered, Have you submitted? If they submit, they are guided, but if they turn away, your duty is only to convey. And Allah is Seeing of servants. Fa-in hajjuka — if argue — argument after clear testimony tawhid and Islam.\n\nSay — qul — I have submitted my face — wajhi — whole self face noblest — to Allah, and those who follow me. Not just claim but following alongside.\n\nSay to People given Scripture and ummiyyin — unlettered Arabs who had no book — a-aslamtum — have you submitted? Question not rhetorical mocking but invitation as earlier (2:108) or guidance?\n\nIf they submit guided; if turn away — tawallaw — your duty balagh — convey. Not compulsion, not control hearts. Hayy Qayyum does not sleep watching; your job not to make them submit but to invite.\n\nWallahu Basirun bil-ibad — Allah Seeing servants — sees who argues sincerely seeking truth versus arguing seeking envy, sees your submission, sees their turning.\n\nThis verse balances firmness simplicity: I have submitted; have you? Choice theirs but sight His. As earlier deen is Islam (19), messenger not responsible residents Hellfire (2:119). Same here: duty convey.\n\nModel for dawah today: submit yourself first, invite with question not hurling insult, leave result to Seeing of servants.\n\nAnd it transitions to some who not only argue but kill prophets (next).",
  "21": "Those who disbelieve in Allah's signs, kill prophets unjustly, and kill those who order justice among people — give them tidings of painful punishment. After inviting to submit, Quran shows extreme opposite. Three crimes escalating: disbelieve in ayat — reject signs after they came (19), kill prophets unjustly — bi-ghayri haqq — though prophets came with clarity, and kill those who order justice among people — qist — ordinary believers who stand for fairness.\n\nHistorical it happened: Children of Israel killed many prophets, Jews in Madinah mocked and wished elimination, Quraysh attempted kill Muhammad, peace be upon him.\n\nFa-bashshirhum — give tidings — sarcasm, painful punishment — not good news. Tidings usually joy; using for pain shows irony.\n\nThese are not distant past crimes. Every age has versions: denying clear aya when it costs, assassinating voice calling to tawhid, silencing person ordering justice when community prefers corruption. The pattern repeats.\n\nThe verse says their deeds wasted world and hereafter next — because hospitality towards truth killed at root.\n\nFor believer, opposite qualities: believing signs, protecting prophets legacy, ordering justice — as earlier ulu al-ilm witnessing standing with justice (18). That is salvation.",
  "22": "They are ones whose deeds are wasted in this world and Hereafter, and they have no helpers. Habitia a'maluhum — wasted — like dust rock earlier (2:264). Deeds may include charity, building, but after killing prophets and justice-orderers, foundation collapses. In world wasted because no barakah, no lasting good; in hereafter weighed zero.\n\nWa ma lahum min nasirin — no helpers — no children wealth that earlier thought avail, no allies Taghut that promised help. On Day they will look for intercessor, protector, none.\n\nLinks to earlier: though they thought wealth children avail fuel Fire (10), now confirmed. And those who took Taghut guardians brought from light to darkness (2:257) end without helper.\n\nThe severity teaches minority who orders justice matters to Allah greatly. Killing one such person equal to threatening prophetic mission. So supporting such person — speaking truth to power quietly — also weighty.\n\nBeliever reads and fears participating even by silence in killing justice voices.",
  "23": "Have you not seen those given portion of Scripture? When invited to Book of Allah to judge between them, a group turns away. Portion — nasib — not whole; they had part of knowledge but acted as if had all. When invited to Book Allah — kitab Allah — to judge — li-yahkuma baynahum — between them, some turn away — mu'ridun.\n\nSituation in Madinah: two Jewish tribes conflict, or Jew and Muslim dispute brought to Prophet to judge by Torah, they turn away when judgment against interest. They accepted Book when supported claim.\n\nThis mirrors earlier (2:113) Jews say Christians nothing and vice versa while reciting Book. Invitation to let Book judge exposes preference for desire.\n\nFar from ancient, same today: invited to Quran Sunnah to settle marriage, inheritance, business, person turns away if not in favour, shops for lenient fatwa concealing testimony.\n\nThumma tawalla fariq — then group turns — shows depth: not ignorance then turning, but after invitation. Knowledge plus turning worse.\n\nNext verse gives excuse they invented.",
  "24": "They say, Fire will not touch us except few days — wishful lies deceived them about religion. Lan tamassana an-nar illa ayyaman ma'dudat — Fire not touch except counted days. Same as Jews in 2:80 claimed few days. Counted days invented: perhaps days worshipped calf, or forty days, etc. Idea lineage ensures limited punishment then Paradise ours.\n\nWa gharrahum fi dinihim ma kanu yaftarun — deceived in religion what they invented. Ghurur — deception. They forged, then believed own forgery. Wishful thinking — amaniyyuhum as earlier (2:111) — became doctrine.\n\nThis is dangerous mechanism: sin, then to ease conscience invent doctrine limiting consequences, then after repetition think doctrine true. Polytheists said idols intercede; some Muslims today say \"Allah Ghafur will forgive\" as license persisting while concealing, forgetting severe punishment also real.\n\nVerse says their iftira — fabrication — deceived them, not others primarily. Self-deception most harmful.\n\nReply coming verses 25 — how horrible when gathered Day no doubt — shows few days claim collapses at gathering.",
  "25": "How will it be when We gather them for a Day about which no doubt — and every soul paid in full what it earned and they will not be wronged? Fa-kayfa idha jama'nahum li-yawmin la rayba fih — How will it be when... The question leaves answer to imagination. Scene: those who said few days now gathered, no doubt Day.\n\nWa wuffiyat kullu nafsin ma kasabat — every soul paid in full what it earned — tuwaffa — as earlier about full recompense (2:281). Not days counted arbitrarily but exact earning. And they not wronged — la yuzlamun — no injustice, so few days claim injustice to victims whose rights denied.\n\nEarlier supplication rasikhun mentioned gathering Day no doubt (9) as comfort; same gathering for this group becomes horror. Same Day two faces: for muttaqin mercy, for deceived horror. Difference root — sincerity vs wishful lying.\n\nVerse forces reader imagine standing with earned, not inherited guarantee. If claim \"Fire few days\" were true, payment would not be full, would be discount. But divine justice full.\n\nNext verse teaches Prophet to say ownership and honour power to counter such false security.",
  "26": "Say, O Allah Owner of all dominion, You give dominion to whom You will and take it from whom You will, You honour whom You will and humiliate whom You will — in Your hand is all good — indeed You have power over all. Qul Allahumma Malika al-mulk — O Allah Owner of kingship. Mulk includes kingdom, authority, wealth, lineage honour they relied on.\n\nTu'ti al-mulka man tasha wa tanzi'u — give to whom You will and strip from whom You will — history sees: gives to Talut simple farmer though not wealthy (2:247), gives to Dawud young shepherd after Jalut, gives to Muhammad unlettered orphan though Quraysh chiefs richer. And takes from Pharaoh, Namrud, Quraysh.\n\nTu'izzu man tasha wa tudhillu — honour whom You will humiliate whom... Honour not traced to tribe; honour through Islam.\n\nBi-yadika al-khayr — in Your hand is all good — all khayr. Not in family, not in few days guarantee. Good includes guidance, ridwan, forgiveness — better than beautified desires (14-15).\n\nInnaka ala kulli shay'in qadir — power over all. Repeats from 2:106 capability foundation abrogation and law.\n\nThis dua Prophet taught. Purpose: after warning those who said Fire few days because think lineage protects, remind dominion Owner gives and takes. Believer reciting fears no tyrant, hopes no lineage; all in His hand.\n\nSeeds of next verse about life death.",
  "27": "You merge night into day and merge day into night, bring living from dead and dead from living, and provide for whom You will without account. Tuliju — you cause enter — night into day, day into night — alternation not sudden clash but gradual entry, light into darkness, darkness into light, seasons lengthening — visible power.\n\nTukhriju al-hayya min al-mayyit wa... — bring living from dead and dead from living — seed from soil dead, plant living; egg from chicken dead matter? Human from nutfa seemingly lifeless; believer from disbeliever household, disbeliever from believer household; sincere heart from heedless.\n\nTarzuqu man tasha bi-ghayri hisab — provide for whom You will without account — limitless, without calculation, without asking. Similar to better provision vs brief enjoyment. Rizq includes guidance.\n\nThese processes testify that Giver of dominion also controller daily cosmos, and thus dominion shift not strange. If He can bring night from day, He can bring honour from humiliation, life after death, provision without account though person seems poor.\n\nIt also connects to shaping in wombs (6) — same power forms brings living dead.\n\nFor believer anxious over sustenance after leaving riba (2:278) or after spending beloved, this verse reassurance: Rizq without account — His hand full of good.\n\nSets stage for loyalty — not take disbelievers as guardians instead of believers — because Provider is He.",
  "28": "Believers should not take disbelievers as allies instead of believers — whoever does will have nothing to do with Allah — except when fearing them with precaution — and Allah warns you about Himself — and to Allah is destination.\n\nLa yattakhidh al-mu'minun al-kafirin awliya min duni al-mu'minin — believers not take disbelievers as intimate guardians protectors instead of believers. Awliya more than casual friendship; inner alliance loyalty that puts their interests ahead of faithful. Ummah was new, facing threat; some wanted shield by siding with Jewish tribes or Quraysh secretly.\n\nWa man yaf'al dhalika fa-laysa minAllahi fi shay — whoever does so has nothing to do with Allah — disavowal severe. Not just sin but loyalty severed, unless fearing taqiyyah — precaution when under severe persecution — allow outward display while heart believing, as Ammar did.\n\nWa yuhadhdhirukum Allahu nafsah — Allah warns you about Himself — terrifying phrase: He warns you about Himself — His punishment, His watch, His taking account nothing hidden (5). So precaution allowed but no casual alliances.\n\nWa ila Allahi al-masir — to Allah destination — final return where loyalties tested. Who was your wali? That matters at masir.\n\nBalance: not hostility to all non-Muslims — Quran permits kind just treatment (60:8), marriage, business — but inner protective alliance shaping identity should not be with those who disbelieve after guidance purely for worldly gain.\n\nForeshadows Uhud when some wanted return to disbelievers after setback.",
  "29": "Say, whether you conceal what is in your hearts or reveal it — Allah knows it — and He knows what is in heavens and what on earth — Allah has power over all. Same sentence as near end of al-Baqarah (2:284). Whether conceal in hearts or reveal — t'khfu or tubdu — Allah knows. Earlier nothing hidden from Allah (5) generic; here specifically what in صدور — chests.\n\nWa ya'lamu ma fis-samawati wa ma fil-ard — knows heavens earth — as before.\n\nWallahu ala kulli shay'in qadir — power over all — capable to bring concealed to light for accounting, forgive or punish.\n\nContext of alliances: you may conceal loyalty to disbelievers outwardly showing loyalty to believers, or taqiyyah case outward opposite; Allah knows difference. Heart earning matters (2:225).\n\nComfort for believers suppressing fear, grief after Uhud, not expressing.\n\nWarning following Day when every soul presented good done and wishes misdeeds far.\n\nLink: if you truly know He knows hearts and has power, you will fear Him (next — warns you about Himself).",
  "30": "On a Day every soul will find whatever good it did present, and whatever evil it did it will wish there was great distance between it and it. And Allah warns you about Himself — Allah is Kind to servants. Yawma tajidu kullu nafsin ma 'amilat min khayr muhdaran — Day each soul finds good present — muhdar — ready, not lost. Even tiny dawn istighfar (17), patience grain (2:261) present. That encourages.\n\nWa ma 'amilat min suu' tawaddu law anna baynaha wa baynahu amadan ba'idan — for evil, wish great distance — amad ba'id — long span — between self and sin, so sin not attached. Person sees film adultery, lying, killing prophets legacy — wishes far.\n\nWa yuhadhdhirukum Allahu nafsah — repeats warning about Himself second time in two verses — emphasis severe. Yet closes mercy: Wallahu Ra'ufun bil-ibad — Allah Kind to servants — Ra'uf — tender, gentle. Warns because kind. Warning itself mercy, to avoid Day of wishing distance.\n\nWord muhdar — present — suggests good not abstract reward but deed itself transformed into something pleasant present. Evil also present as burden.\n\nSo after verses about alliances hidden hearts, picture Day where all hidden revealed present forces choice: which deeds you want present near?\n\nIt paves for love follow condition next verse.",
  "31": "Say, if you love Allah, then follow me — Allah will love you and forgive your sins — and Allah is Forgiving, Merciful. Qul in kuntum tuhibbuna Allaha fattabi'uni — if you sincerely love Allah. Hubb — claim many made: People of Book said we are children of Allah His beloved. Muslims could claim love without proof. Criterion: follow me — Prophet Muhammad.\n\nIttiba' not just admiration but walking behind: follow in creed (Hayy Qayyum no compulsion), in patience dawn forgiveness, in spending despite love, in leniency (159). If claim love but turn away from his teachings about alliances, riba, prayer, claim false.\n\nReward double: yuhbibkum Allah — Allah will love you — beyond you loving Him, He loving you greater — and yaghfir lakum dhunubakum — forgive sins. Love brings forgiveness, forgiveness returns to love.\n\nWallahu Ghafur Rahim — Forgiving Merciful — fitting because followers will slip.\n\nThis verse called ayat al-mihnah — test verse, criterion love. Some said: product love obedience. If love true, feet follow beloved path.\n\nAfter warning self, Allah Kind to servants (30), path to kind is follow messenger He sent as mercy.",
  "32": "Say, obey Allah and the Messenger. But if they turn away — Allah does not love the disbelievers. Brief, final. After love follow (31), obedience command.\n\nAti'u Allaha war-Rasul — obey Allah and Messenger — pairing always together; obeying Messenger obeying Allah because he recites verses purifies teaches Book wisdom (3:164 echo).\n\nFa-in tawallaw — if turn away — same tawalli used for group turning away when invited to Book judge (23), for alliances turning to disbelievers. If turn away after love claimed and invitation given, fa-inna Allaha la yuhibbu al-kafirin — Allah does not love disbelievers. Does not love — opposite of yuhbibkum Allah in previous verse for followers. Love withdrawn.\n\nSo two loves contrast: Allah loves followers who follow, forgives; Allah does not love disbelievers turn away after clarity.\n\nCloses early section about Book, alliances, knowledge.\n\nNext begins chosen families — Adam, Nuh, Ibrahim, Imran — connecting obedience chain.",
  "33": "Indeed Allah chose Adam and Nuh and the family of Ibrahim and family of Imran over the worlds. Istafa — chose, purified, selected — as earlier Ibrahim chosen (2:130). Four examples: Adam — first human chosen to be khalifah though earth corruption feared; Nuh — chosen after humanity drowned; family of Ibrahim — includes Isma'il Ishaq Ya'qub, wide; family of Imran — includes Maryam, Isa, Yahya — pious household.\n\nOver worlds — al-alamin — of their times. Not racial supremacy but selected for mission, purified for worship.\n\nWhy these four? They link Quranic lineage: Adam origin, Nuh second origin after flood, Ibrahim father of both Israelite and Ismaelite lines, Imran leading to Isa whose divinity debated — yet lineage chosen not divine. Choosing shows honour bestowed not innate divinity.\n\nChooses whom He wills for mercy as earlier (2:105). Honour from Allah, not self.\n\nNext verse clarifies they descendants of one another — chain.\n\nIf Allah chose families, He can choose individual Maryam beyond sisters.",
  "34": "Descendants of one another — And Allah is Hearing, Knowing. Dhurriyyatan ba'duha min ba'd — offspring some from others — same faith chain, not scattered different religions — millah of Ibrahim single. Adam to Nuh to Ibrahim to Imran one light passed.\n\nWallahu Sami'un Alim — Hearing Knowing — as earlier hearing knowing appears around sensitive family matters (2:224, 227). Here He heard du'aa of wife of Imran, knows what in womb (6). He heard Zakariya whispered dua for offspring.\n\nIt emphasises not ancestry alone but continuity. Dhurriyyah implies shared concern.\n\nFor People of Book claiming exclusive rights — best nation — Quran says true bestness by following chosen chain's faith, not blood alone.\n\nIt also prepares detailed story Imran family chosen — wife dedicating child.",
  "35": "When wife of Imran said, My Lord I have dedicated what is in my womb purely for Your service — so accept from me — indeed You are the Hearing, All-Knowing. Imrat Imran — wife of Imran — named traditionally Hannah — pregnant hoping male serve Temple — Beit al-Maqdis — as was custom dedicate boys.\n\nInni nadhartu laka ma fi batni muharraran — I vowed to You what in belly freed — muharrar — liberated from worldly tasks solely for Your service — temple servant.\n\nFa-taqabbal minni — accept from me — same du'a Ibrahim and Isma'il raised foundations (2:127) — taqabbal minna. Dedication without acceptance incomplete.\n\nInnaka anta Sami' al-Alim — Hearing Knowing — she knows Allah heard her private vow in pregnancy, Knows what in womb already mentioned shaping as wills (6).\n\nShe expects male, as female not custom serve temple dwelling constantly due to menstruation etc. But dedication sincere; acceptance will come different than expected. This teaches rizq: offer best, leave form to Allah.\n\nEcho earlier spend from what love (3:92) — she spends beloved child before birth.\n\nNext verse shows delivery girl.",
  "36": "And when she delivered her, she said, My Lord I have delivered a female — and Allah knew better what she delivered — and male is not like female — I have named her Maryam and I seek protection for her and her offspring from Satan the outcast.\n\nShe delivered girl, said \"Rabbi inni wada'tuha untha\" — voice perhaps disappointment not in girl but in vow expectation — boys serve temple full-time; girl? Yet Allah knew better what she delivered — He knew girl better than she imagined.\n\nWa laysa adh-dhakaru kal-untha — male not like female — in this context not general superiority but: this female not like any male they imagined; she surpasses. Maryam will surpass many males in devotion.\n\n\"I named her Maryam\" — Maryam — meaning worshiper, devoted. Naming is first education: gives identity.\n\n\"And I seek refuge for her and her offspring from Satan rajim.\" Ta'wid — protection — from shaytan rajim — same enemy who made Adam slip. Seeker is mother. Prophet said no child born except Satan pricks, except Maryam and her son — due to this dua.\n\nAllah accepted despite expectation mismatch, and made Maryam best among women chosen over women worlds (42). Lessons: sincere vow accepted even if form changes; daughter can be greater than son hoped; dua of mother potent protection — seek refuge for offspring.\n\nZakariya now becomes guardian.",
  "37": "So her Lord accepted her beautifully and made her grow nicely, entrusting her to Zakariya's care. Whenever Zakariya entered upon her in the prayer chamber, he found provision with her. He said, O Maryam, from where is this for you? She said, It is from Allah — Allah provides for whom He wills without account.\n\nFa-taqabbalaha Rabbuha bi-qaboolin hasan — accepted beautifully — qabool hasan — not merely accepted but with beauty — makes her upbringing pleasant.\n\nAnbataha nabatan hasanan — made her grow nicely — like plant — nabat — same root growth mentioned earlier life from dead.\n\nKafala Zakariya — entrusted to Zakariya — prophet her maternal uncle — guardian. To decide guardian they cast pens — aqlam — lots — story next verse 44.\n\nKullama dakhala alayha Zakariya al-mihrab wajada indaha rizqan — whenever entered prayer chamber mihrab found rizq — summer fruits winter, winter fruits summer, said provision without account (27) same phrase.\n\nShe said huwa min indi Allah — from Allah — tawhid simple — Allah provides whom wills without account.\n\nThis scene taught Zakariya to ask for child despite old age, because One who provides fruit out season provides son out season. Zakariya's dua follows immediately after seeing rizq.\n\nAlso for us: Maryam alone in mihrab, yet rizq reaches — true tawakkul plus devotion brings unexpected provision without account. And fanatical material accounting fails before divine bounty.",
  "38": "There Zakariya called upon his Lord, saying, My Lord grant me from Yourself good offspring — You are indeed Hearer of prayer. Hunalika da'a Zakariya Rabbahu — there — at that moment, that place mihrab where he saw provision without account, old man with barren wife dared ask.\n\nRabbi hab li min ladunka dhurriyyatan tayyibah — grant me from Yourself good offspring — min ladunka — from Your special nearness as earlier mercy from ladunka (8). Tayyibah — good, wholesome — not just child but righteous.\n\nInnaka Sami' ad-du'a — Hearer of prayer — Sami' ad-du'a higher than Sami al-Alim — specific hearing that answers.\n\nZakariya elderly, wife barren, but seeing Maryam's miraculous rizq he reasoned: if seasonal impossible rizq possible, offspring impossible also possible. His du'a sincere, private, in mihrab — best place du'a after seeing sign.\n\nProphet Zakariya model for old parents, for those told impossible biologically. He did not ask for any offspring to continue lineage pride; asked tayyibah — good — which answers later Yahya confirm word from Allah, noble, chaste, prophet.\n\nConnection earlier wife Imran dedicated what in womb for service; Zakariya now dedicates request for offspring triy — continuation righteous families chosen.",
  "39": "So angels called him while he was standing praying in the prayer chamber, Allah gives you good news of Yahya — confirming a Word from Allah — and a chief, chaste, and prophet among righteous.\n\nAngels called — while standing praying — qaim yusalli fil-mihrab — same mihrab where Maryam received rizq, where he prayed. Answer comes during worship, not after years waiting.\n\nGood news — Yahya — John son — confirming Word from Allah — musaddiqan bi-kalimatin min Allah — that Word is Isa — Kalimatu Allah — because Yahya first to believe Isa, or confirms Isa as Word. Name Yahya means lives — Yahya — because heart alive, or Allah gave life to barren womb.\n\nLeadership qualities: sayyid — chief, noble, leader his people respected; hasur — chaste, restraining from women, fully devoted not distracted by desires earlier beautified (14); prophet among righteous — salihin — joins chosen families.\n\nZakariya had asked tayyib offspring — answer exceeds: not just child but prophet chief.\n\nThis demonstrates Allah gives better than what asked — min ladunka — when asked sincerely. Also parallels later Maryam child Isa even more miraculous — Yahya birth to old barren wife prelude to Isa birth to virgin.\n\nNote angels calling — multiple — plural — glorifies moment.\n\nNext his astonishment shows humanity remains even after du'a.",
  "40": "He said, My Lord how can I have a boy when old age reached me and my wife barren? He said, So it will be — Allah does what He wills. Qala Rabbi anna yakunu li ghulam — same astonishment earlier — old age reached me — balaghani al-kibar — Wife barren — aqir — double impossibility biological.\n\nAnswer: Kadhālika Allahu yaf'alu ma yasha — So will be — Allah does what He wills. Yaf'alu — does — active. In Maryam case later says Yakhluqu ma yasha — creates what wills (47) — distinction: Yahya from old barren still within usual creation via parents but unusual timing; Isa created without father outright creation, so yakhluqu stronger.\n\nAllah does what He wills — verse earlier dominion gives to whom wills (26), provides without account (37). So doing what Wills includes giving child to old.\n\nHis age said ~100 plus? Yet will of Allah overrides cause.\n\nBeliever fearing provision, child, healing often reasons via cause only; this teaches Creator of cause free to bypass.\n\nAfter astonishing promise, Zakariya asks sign to thank, not doubt.",
  "41": "He said, My Lord grant me a sign — He said, Your sign is you will not speak to people three days except by gestures, and remember your Lord much and glorify evening and morning.\n\nZakariya asked sign not out of doubt but gratitude — to know when to increase remembrance, to thank. Sign given: not to speak to people three days except ramzan — gestures, not muteness from illness but holding tongue from people while tongue free for remembrance.\n\nAyatuka alla tukallima an-nasa thalathata ayyamin illa ramzan — three days only gesturing. Why silence from people? To isolate for dhikr, to feel bounty, to prevent babbling about miracle before time, to learn thanksgiving concentration.\n\nWadhkur Rabbaka kathiran wa sabbih bil-ashiyyi wal-ibkar — remember Lord much, glorify evening morning — the silence from people replaced with chatter with Lord. Ashiyyi — evening, ibkar — early morning, two ends day when gratitude overflows.\n\nThis pattern later for Maryam also silence: but different.\n\nFor us: when Allah grants unexpected rizq — child after despair, provision without account — response prescribed is not party but increased remembrance morning evening, tongue withheld from people chatter saved for glorification. Sign of gratitude is dhikr kathir.\n\nZakariya remained in mihrab, fasting speech to people while praising. The child Yahya would be given wisdom as boy.\n\nNext angels turn to Maryam selection.",
  "42": "And when angels said, O Maryam Allah has chosen you and purified you and chosen you over women of worlds.\n\nIsfa — chosen — twice: chosen first for dedication, purified — tahharaki — purified spiritually from sins and physically, and chosen over nisa al-alamin — women of worlds. Double choosing emphasises honour.\n\nIbn Abbas said Maryam best of women world at her time, as Khadija best time, Fatima best etc. Chosen over women worlds in two senses: purity and role.\n\nPurified from what earlier impurity alleged by Jews? Also from menstruation? Actually some said she never menstruated? But mainstream purified from shirk, from bad suspicion, made suitable carrying Word.\n\nAngels addressing her directly — not prophet but honour — as angels spoke to Ibrahim's wife. Shows karamah of righteous woman.\n\nChosen status not because male not like female deficiency, but female in this instance surpasses. Male is not like this female — earlier verse (36) used same phrase.\n\nHer selection linked to mother dua seeking protection from Satan — accepted.\n\nFor every girl feeling less because cultural male preference, Maryam chosen over worlds.\n\nNext command devout prayer.",
  "43": "O Maryam, be devout to your Lord, prostrate and bow with those bowing. Ya Maryam uqnutī li-Rabbiki — be devout — qunut — obedience devotion standing long prayer. Then usjudi — prostrate — war-ka'i — bow — with those bowing — ma'a ar-raki'in — join congregation, though worship mostly private mihrab, still join.\n\nQunut, sujud, ruku — three postures mentioned — cover prayer.\n\nRaki'in generally men? But she joins row? Means worship with worshippers in Temple, community.\n\nMessage: high status does not exempt from worship; chosen second time, then commanded increase devotion. Chosen status increases responsibility, not indulgence.\n\nFemale worshipper told join community not isolation only. Though Maryam secluded, community ties needed.\n\nAfter honour and command, story of lots for guardian enters as unseen news.",
  "44": "That is from news of unseen We reveal to you. You were not with them when they cast pens deciding who should take care of Maryam, nor when they disputed.\n\nDhalika min anba al-ghayb nuhihi ilayk — that from news unseen We reveal to you — i.e., Prophet Muhammad who never attended Temple lots. He was not present when they cast pens — aqlam — throwing pens into water to see whose floats, to decide guardian of Maryam after Imran died — nor when they disputed — yakhtasimun — argued each wanting honour caring for chosen girl.\n\nYou were not with them — wa ma kunta ladayhim — yet you narrate precisely as Torah sources confirm. Proof prophethood — revelation from Hayy who nothing hidden (5).\n\nThe casting lot method described elsewhere: each scholar threw pen carved name into river; all sank except Zakariya's floated. So Allah chose Zakariya via qura — lawful lot for competing equal rights.\n\nThis story comforts Prophet experiencing dispute among People of Book in Madinah casting arguments: same disputes existed around Maryam. Revelation that knows hidden disputes can guide present disputes.\n\nIt also shows protecting Maryam involved dispute because honour — caring righteous woman considered privilege. For community, befriending and sheltering faithful woman is competition.\n\nNow second angelic address about Isa.",
  "45": "When angels said, O Maryam Allah gives you good news of a Word from Him — his name Messiah Isa son of Maryam — honoured in this world and next and among those close to Allah.\n\nGood news — Word from Him — Kalimah — Isa called Kalimatu Allah — not Word as Allah attribute but Word Be — kun — created by Word, or good news word.\n\nHis name Messiah Isa son of Maryam — Messiah — al-Masih — meaning anointed, blessed, wipes away blindness from birth, or anointed with blessing. Isa ibn Maryam — son of Maryam — refutation divinity claim: son of woman, not son of Allah, ascribed to mother because no father.\n\nWajihan fid-dunya wal-akhirah — honoured in this world and next — in world with prophethood, miracles, followers loving, in next with high station intercession, near. Wa min al-muqarrabin — among those close — muqarrabin — elite angels.\n\nAngels giving news mirror earlier angels gave Zakariya Yahya. Maryam's news greater — not just righteous son but Messiah.\n\nShe in seclusion, virgin, hears such news of child who honoured both worlds — test heavy.\n\nPrestige description sets stage for her question how possible.",
  "46": "And he will speak to people in the cradle and maturity, and be among righteous. Wa yukallimu an-nasa fil-mahd wa kahlan — speak in cradle — mahd — and maturity — kahlan — about 30-50 years age strength.\n\nSpeaking in cradle miracle: Isa defended mother accusation, said inni Abdullah — I am servant Allah. Speaking in maturity indicates he will not die as child but live to maturity — refuting claim crucified as youth; rather raised and will return adult speaking to people.\n\nWa min as-salihin — among righteous — salihin — same as Yahya described righteous, joining chain chosen families.\n\nThis promise gives Maryam reassurance: child not shame but righteous speaking early and late.\n\nCradle speech also mercy to Maryam who will face people carrying baby. How to answer accusation? Her fasting silence, baby speaks.\n\nFor us: honoured in world next requires righteousness; Isa honoured because among salihin despite divinity claims later.\n\nNext her natural question.",
  "47": "She said, My Lord how can I have a child when no man touched me? He said, So it will be — Allah creates what He wills — when He decrees matter He says Be and it is.\n\nMaryam wonders — Qalat Rabbi anna yakunu li walad wa lam yamsasni bashar — how with no man touched — physical impossibility known.\n\nAnswer: Kadhāliki Allahu yakhluqu ma yasha — Allah creates what wills — yakhluqu — creates, stronger than yaf'alu for Yahya — because Yahya from parents old, Isa without father genuine creation from nothing paternal. When decrees matter says Be — kun — and it is — fayakūn — same phrase used for heavens earth originator (2:117).\n\nSame Kun for Adam from dust then Be he was (59) — example Isa like Adam — both with kun, Adam without mother father, Isa without father less strange.\n\nAllah's will does not need cause as He shapes wombs as He wills (6) earlier, provides without account (37). So Maryam's virginity preserved, purity remains.\n\nHer question not doubt but seeking understanding how — unlike Zakariya also asked how but seeking process.\n\nResponse teaches: Be and is sufficient. No need father, no need mother? Actually mother needed as tilth but not father.\n\nFor believer facing impossible situation — provision, health, marriage — same answer active: yakhluqu ma yasha, Kun.\n\nNext list of what He teaches him.",
  "48": "And He will teach him writing and wisdom and Torah and Gospel. Wa yu'allimuhu al-kitaba wal-hikmata wat-Tawrata wal-Injil — taught by Allah directly.\n\nKitab — writing? Some say actual scripture writing, or Book — al-kitab generic revelation writing skill. Hikmah — wisdom — understanding placing things rightly, Sunnah, prophetic judgment.\n\nTorah and Gospel — he will know both: Torah confirmed before him, Gospel revealed to him — solves dispute Jews Christians claiming own law exclusive. Isa knows both, messenger bridging.\n\nHe will be messenger to Children Israel — yet his knowledge includes both scriptures, showing continuity: same chain of chosen families descendants one another (34).\n\nTeaching from Allah directly not school — Isa speaking wisdom as child, no human teacher.\n\nVerse also honours knowledge: Allah teaches whom wills wisdom (2:269), here teaches Isa four: writing, wisdom, Torah, Gospel. Wisdom paired with Books shows Books need wisdom to apply.\n\nFor us: request knowledge as Maryam's son taught — combine literacy, wisdom, knowledge previous revelations.\n\nNext his message miracles.",
  "49": "And as messenger to Children of Israel — I have come with sign from your Lord — I will create for you from clay shape of bird then breathe into it and it becomes bird by Allah permission — heal blind and leper and give life to dead by permission — inform you what you eat and store in houses — in that is sign for you if believers.\n\nIsa's mission: messenger to Banu Israel — not humanity entire like final Messenger — yet signs extraordinary for sceptical people who demanded signs.\n\n\"I create from clay shape of bird\" — akhluqu — using same root as yusawwiru in wombs — form from clay like Adam — then breathe — anfukhu — as Allah breathed into Adam — and it becomes bird bi-idhnillah — by permission — each miracle tagline \"by Allah permission\" — bi-idhni Allah — repeated to crush divinity claim: creator by permission not independent creator.\n\nHealing blind born akmah and leper abras — diseases doctors helpless, giving life dead — ihya — all by permission.\n\nAnd informing what they eat and store — what you ate lunch hidden house — knowledge unseen sign.\n\n\"In that is sign if believers\" — if you want to believe.\n\nAll miracles tied to what disbelievers valued: creation like shaping? He creates bird; provision without account? He knows stored food; healing diseases? etc.\n\nPattern: shaping wombs as wills (6), provision without account (37), nothing hidden (5), life death merging (27) — all demonstrated via Isa but as signs not as lordship.\n\nNext second part confirm Torah and legalize some forbidden.",
  "50": "And confirming what before me of Torah and making lawful for you some of what was forbidden to you — and I have come with sign from Lord — so be mindful of Allah and obey me.\n\nWa musaddiqan lima bayna yadayya min at-Tawrat — confirming Torah before — same role Quran confirming before — same family.\n\nWa li-uhilla lakum ba'da alladhi hurrima alaykum — to make lawful some of what forbidden to you — Torah restrictions due to hard hearts, Bani Israel forbidden some good fat of animals etc as punishment (4:160). Isa comes easing, as earlier abrogation better or similar (2:106).\n\nHe says \"I have come with sign from your Lord\" — ayah bayyinah repeated for emphasis.\n\n\"Fattaqu Allaha wa ati'uni\" — So fear Allah and obey me — same call all prophets: fear Allah, obey messenger. Two wings: taqwa to Allah, obedience to messenger (31 follow me Allah will love you).\n\nThis reduces claim Jesus came to abolish law entirely; he confirms core, eases some burdens.\n\nFor believer, obedience to messenger teaching remains condition taqwa.\n\nNext verse succinct tawhid.",
  "51": "Indeed Allah is my Lord and your Lord — so worship Him — that is straight path. Inna Allaha Rabbi wa Rabbukum fa'buduh — same tawhid testimony earlier Allah witnesses no god except Him (18) — Isa himself says: Allah my Lord and your Lord.\n\nFa'buduh — worship Him alone — hadha sirat mustaqim — this straight path — same straight path Fatiha asks, same sirat mentioned middle nation.\n\nIsa declares servanthood before lordship — as in cradle he said inni Abdullah. This single verse dismantles later Trinity.\n\nStraight path not complicated: worship Allah alone who is my Lord your Lord, not me nor mother.\n\nThis closes Isa early mission summary; next sense of disbelief among his people.\n\nThus surah from Adam chosen, Imran family, Maryam purified, Yahya chaste, Isa honoured Word, all submit to same Rabb.",
  "52": "But when Isa sensed disbelief from them, he said, Who are my helpers to Allah? The disciples said, We are helpers of Allah — we believed in Allah — bear witness we have submitted.\n\nFa-lamma ahassa Isa minhum al-kufra — when sensed disbelief — after bringing signs bringing clear proofs, some still refused.\n\nQala man ansari ila Allah — Who helpers to Allah? Not just helpers to me but to Allah — ila Allah — towards Allah — struggle for His cause.\n\nQala al-hawariyyun — disciples — hawari — purest white, companions closest — nahnu ansar Allah — we helpers Allah — amanna billah — we believed — washhad bi-anna muslimun — bear witness we have submitted — muslimun.\n\nSame submission as Ibrahim (2:131), as Ya'qub sons (2:133).\n\nHawariyyun become model for Ansar of Muhammad — who also said we helpers Allah. Their answer amanna is same as believers 16 amanna faghfir.\n\nThis shows even when many disbelieve, Allah keeps group helpers — not majority but sincere minority suffices.\n\nNext their dua shows characteristics helpers.",
  "53": "Our Lord, we believed in what You revealed and followed the messenger — so write us among witnesses.\n\nRabbana amanna bima anzalta wattaba'na ar-rasul — We believed in what You revealed — Injil — and followed messenger — Isa.\n\nFaktubna ma'a ash-shahidin — write us among witnesses — shahidin — those who testify truth as Allah testified (18). They ask to be written among ulu al-ilm witnessing.\n\nDua simple but profound: faith in revelation + following messenger = counted among witnesses. Same as earlier following Muhammad makes Allah love you (31). Following is proof belief.\n\nHawariyyun did not ask wealth, long life; asked to be written among witnesses — desire to be recorded in high assembly as bearing truth.\n\nThis matches earlier dua rasikhun grant us mercy, gather us, and muttaqin forgive and protect from Fire. All duas revolve around belonging to truthful record.\n\nAfter hawariyyun duas, disbelievers plot.",
  "54": "They plotted and Allah planned — Allah is best of planners. Wa makaru wa makara Allah — they plotted — makr — secret scheme, conspiracy to kill Isa, to crucify. Allah also planned — makara Allah — in Arabic makr for Allah means counter-plan, perfect plan that foils evil plan without blame.\n\nWallahu khayru al-makirin — Allah best of planners — ayya plan that protects beloved never fails. Their plan: kill Isa. Allah plan: raise Isa, cast likeness on another? Narrations diverse but outcome Isa protected.\n\nThis principle repeats in Badr, in Uhud: disbelievers plan horror (2:214) cast terror (3:151) but best planner ensures outcome for believers if patient.\n\nFor believer feeling surrounded plotting — work colleagues, family pressure — reminder best planner watches, nothing hidden (5).\n\nAfter plan, Allah speaks to Isa directly elevation.",
  "55": "When Allah said, O Isa, I will take you and raise you to Me, purify you from those disbelieved, and make those who follow you above those who disbelieved until Day of Resurrection — then to Me is your return, I will judge between you what you differed about.\n\nIni mutawaffika wa rafi'uka ilayya — I will take you — tawaffa — take full, not necessarily cause death, take soul body — wa raise you to Me — raf' — elevation place honour. Wa mutahhiruka min alladhina kafaru — purify you from those disbelieved — remove from entourage of insults, accusations, plans.\n\nWaja'ilu alladhina ittaba'uka fawqa alladhina kafaru ila yawm qiyamah — make your followers above disbelievers till Day — historical: hawariyyun and later Muslims who believed in Isa as servant not god, and those Christians who stayed true before distortion, were above; and will be above Day of judgment.\n\nThumma ilayya marji'ukum — to Me return — same as to Allah destination earlier (28).\n\nFa-ah kumu baynakum fi-ma kuntum fihi takhtalifun — I will judge between you what you differed — as earlier Allah will judge between those differed (2:113). Isa's nature major dispute — deity or servant — judgment returned to Allah.\n\nThis verse establishes second coming? Raised, not killed, purified, followers above.\n\nFor believer, comfort: if you follow Isa truly — worship Allah is my Lord your Lord (51) — you above disbelievers, not below. Despite mockery.\n\nNext consequence two groups.",
  "56": "As for those who disbelieved, I will punish them with a severe punishment in this world and the Hereafter, and they will have no helpers. Fa-amma alladhina kafaru fa-u'adhdhibuhum adhaban shadidan — severe in world — what does severe in world mean for one who rejected Isa after clear signs? Disgrace, scattering, living under fear, as happened to those who plotted against Isa and later claimed victory while actually losing. And severe in Hereafter — Fire that does not tire, as described earlier fuel of Fire is people and stones (2:24), not metaphor.\n\nWa ma lahum min nasirin — they will have no helpers — no wealth children that they thought would avail (10), no Taghut guardians they took instead of Allah who promised to bring them from light to darkness (2:257), no sons or tribe that they relied upon. The same phrase repeats three times in this surah alone — no helpers (22, 56, 181) — because loneliness is the destiny of kufr after clarity.\n\nThis verse balances mercy for believers earlier: those who believed and did righteous deeds paid in full (57). For disbelievers, punishment severe, no helpers. Both sides paid full.\n\nThe verse also refutes Christian claim that Isa will intercede unconditionally for all who claim him while rejecting tawhid. Isa himself will disown such claimants, as his true followers are above disbelievers until Day (55). Help comes only by Allah's permission (2:255), and for those who insisted on shirk, permission not granted.\n\nFor believer, reminder that alliance choice matters: helpers in this world may be many — followers, likes — but on Day, helper is only valid if helper was righteous and permission granted.",
  "57": "And as for those who believed and did righteous deeds, He will pay them their wages in full, and Allah does not like wrongdoers.\n\nFa-amma alladhina amanu wa amilu salihat fa-yuwaffihim ujurahum — pay wages full — yuwaffi — complete without loss — as earlier every soul paid in full what earned (25, 30) but here positive full.\n\nWallahu la yuhibbu az-zalimin — Allah does not like wrongdoers — as earlier not love transgressors, not love corruption. Those who claim love Isa but wrong by deifying him or killing prophets are zalimin.\n\nThis pair 56-57 mirrors earlier bifurcation after introducing Islam Way (19) — believers vs concealers. Reward full.\n\nNext Quran says We recite this to you as signs and wise reminder.",
  "58": "That We recite to you is from signs and wise reminder. Dhalika natluhu... min al-ayat wa dhikr al-hakim — That which We recite — Quran telling Maryam Zakariya Isa stories — is from ayat — signs — and dhikr hakim — wise reminder — or reminder that is wise — contains wisdom.\n\nNatluhu — We recite — shows Quran not Prophet composition but recited to him from Allah.\n\nIt is ayat — signs pointing to tawhid, to power shapes wombs, provides without account, and dhikr hakim — reminder that is wise — collects.\n\nThis verse transition to example Isa like Adam — pivotal logic.\n\nIt reassures Prophet that stories not folklore but ayat.\n\nFor us: these stories are reminder wise — not entertainment; extract wisdom — tawhid, patience, trust.\n\nNext striking comparison Isa Adam.",
  "59": "Indeed example of Isa before Allah is like example of Adam — He created him from dust then said to him Be and he was.\n\nInna mathala Isa indaAllahi ka-mathali Adam — example Isa in sight Allah like Adam — both created without usual father. Adam from dust — turab — no mother father; Isa from mother no father; which more miraculous? Adam more, as no parents.\n\nKhalaqahu min turab thumma qala lahu kun fa-yakun — created from dust then said Be and he was — kun — same word used for heavens earth (2:117) and for Yahya and Isa creation.\n\nIf Adam being created without parents not made god, why Isa made god when created without father? Argument destroys divinity claim logically.\n\nSame kun shows Hayy Qayyum creates as wills (6) — shapes wombs as wills — can create from dust, from womb barren, from virgin.\n\nThus surah returns to opening: Allah is who shapes in wombs as wills.\n\nFor doubter who stumbles at virgin birth, answer: Be.\n\nNext: this truth from Lord so not among doubters.",
  "60": "The truth is from your Lord, so do not be among doubters. Al-haqqu min Rabbik — same as earlier 2:147 — truth from Lord. Not from desires, not from People Book claims, not from discussion Isa. From Rabb.\n\nFa la takun min al-mumtareen — do not be among those who doubt — mumtarin — waverers. After evidence Alif Lam Mim unknown left to Allah, muhkam clear tawhid evident, Isa example like Adam evidence, no room doubt.\n\nProphet addressed but through to ummah: after clear, doubt is deviation heart which earlier duas asked to prevent (8).\n\nIf truth from Lord, then response is acceptance, not argument.\n\nPrepares for mubahala challenge next — those who still dispute after full knowledge.\n\nSo sequence: stories, wisdom, example Adam, now truth declaration.\n\nNext invitation to mutual imprecation for those insisting dispute.",
  "61": "Then whoever argues with you about him after knowledge came to you, say, Come let's call our sons and your sons, our women and your women, ourselves and yourselves, then humbly pray and place curse of Allah upon liars.\n\nFa-man hajjaka fihi min ba'di ma ja'aka min al-ilm — whoever argues about Isa after knowledge came — ilm — what was just described about his birth like Adam, his statement my Lord your Lord, etc.\n\nFa-qul ta'aw na'du abna'ana wa abna'akum wa nisa'ana wa nisa'akum wa anfusana... — Come call sons, women, selves — bring closest family — then nabtahil — humbly pray — with earnest supplication — and place curse Allah upon liars — la'nah.\n\nThis is mubahala — mutual invocation — supreme form debate when arguments exhausted and one party stubborn after knowledge. Prophet did with Najran Christians who came debating Isa divinity. He called Hasan Husayn Fatima Ali? He called family. They refused mubahala fearing curse.\n\nNabtahil root bahalah — humble, earnest, open.\n\nWhy family? Because liar would not risk family being cursed if confident lie; bringing family shows full conviction truth.\n\nThis verse shows how serious claiming Isa god after knowledge is — not polite difference but falsehood earning curse.\n\nIt also shows Prophet family status.\n\nAfter they declined, common terms invited next — which is our next verse after declaration true narrative.",
  "62": "Indeed this is true story, and there is no god except Allah — and Allah is the Mighty, All-Wise. Inna hadha la-huwa al-qasas al-haqq — indeed this is true story — true narrative — not myth, not borrowed.\n\nWa ma min ilahin illa Allah — and no god except Allah — tawhid returns — after story Isa.\n\nWa inna Allaha la-huwa al-Aziz al-Hakim — indeed Allah He is Mighty Wise — Aziz Hakim same as shaping wombs (6) — Mighty to create Isa without father, Wise placement.\n\nQasas al-haqq — true story includes: wife Imran dedication, Zakariya old age Yahya, Maryam purification, Isa cradle speech, miracles by permission, raised.\n\nWhy remind true story? Because People of Book had many stories mixed falsehood: said Isa killed, said Maryam impure, said Allah poor we rich (181). Truth story separates.\n\nAnd declaration no god except Allah after story final verdict: Isa not god; only Allah god.\n\nNext: if they turn away, Allah knows corruptors.",
  "63": "If they turn away, then Allah is Knowing of the corruptors. Fa-in tawallaw — if turn away after mubahala invitation, after true story — qasas al-haqq — that Isa example like Adam, after witness that no god except Allah, after Mighty Wise names.\n\nFa-inna Allaha Alimun bil-mufsidin — Allah Knowing of corruptors — mufsidin — those who spread fasad claiming reform (2:11-12). Turning away after clarity is not neutral academic difference; it is ifsad — corrupting Book by mixing falsehood (71), twisting tongues (78), killing prophets and justice-orderers (21), concealing clear covenant for small price (77).\n\nAlimun bil-mufsidin — Knowing — same as nothing hidden (5), knows what conceals in chests greater than what appears on mouths (118). So turning away not hidden from Him.\n\nThe severity not for compulsion — no compulsion in religion (2:256) — invitation common word remains open. But if after fair invitation and true story they still turn, then quality shifts from difference to corruption.\n\nThis is pivot to common word (64) — invitation to even term. After warning of corruptors, Quran offers way back: come to word even between us.\n\nSo verse serves as hinge.",
  "64": "Say, O People of the Book, come to common word between us and you — that we worship none but Allah, associate none with Him, and not take one another as lords besides Allah — but if they turn away, say, Bear witness we have submitted.\n\nTa'alaw ila kalimatin sawa baynana wa baynakum — Come to word even common — kalimah sawâ — even, equitable, middle.\n\nWhat? Alla na'buda illa Allah wa la nushrika bihi shay'an wa la yattakhidha ba'duna ba'dan arbaban min duni Allah — three clauses: worship none but Allah, associate none with Him, not take one another as lords besides Allah — i.e., no priesthood that legislates halal haram overriding Allah, no saint worship, no clergy lordship.\n\nThis is summary Islam Way (19) and tawhid witness (18) and Isa's own statement Allah my Lord your Lord (51).\n\nFa-in tawallaw faqulu ishadu bi-anna muslimun — if turn away, say bear witness we have submitted — muslimun.\n\nNotice progression: from absolute submission face (20), to Islam Way (19), to common word invitation. Not starting with details hajj but with tawhid core.\n\nCommon word still relevant today interfaith dialogue: begin with agreeable equitable foundation — worship One, no partners, no human lords. Many differences can be discussed after agreement on this.\n\nIf they turn away after fair invitation, bear witness you submitted — you cannot do more than invite; result with Allah.\n\nNext addresses Ibrahim argument.",
  "65": "O People of Book, why argue about Ibrahim when Torah and Gospel not revealed till after him? Will you not reason? Ya Ahl al-Kitab lima tuhajjuna fi Ibrahim wa ma unzilat at-Tawratu wal-Injilu illa min ba'dih — Why argue Ibrahim Jew or Christian while Torah Gospel revealed after him centuries? How could Jew legally defined after Musa be before Musa? How Christian after Isa?\n\nAfa-la ta'qilun — will you not use reason — ya'qilun again as earlier those who do not reason livestock.\n\nIbrahim hanif before those labels — earlier 2:135 — his religion submission.\n\nArgument about Ibrahim in Madinah intense: each claimed him. Quran returns to timeline to expose anachronism.\n\nReasoning simple historical: cannot be Jew Christian if those books after him. So what was he? Answer next 67.\n\nThis teaches method debunking using timeline, not just text.\n\nModern similar claims anachronistic: project modern labels onto earlier prophets. Quran asks reason.\n\nNext broader argument.",
  "66": "Here you are — you argued about what you have some knowledge of, but why argue about what you have no knowledge of? Allah knows and you do not know.\n\nHa antum ha'ulai hajajtum fi-ma lakum bihi ilm — You argued about what you have some knowledge — about Musa, Isa maybe — Torah Gospel you have some knowledge though distorted. But why argue about ma laysa lakum bihi ilm — about which no knowledge — Ibrahim before books, details of unseen.\n\nArgument about things no knowledge is speculation.\n\nWallahu ya'lamu wa antum la ta'lamun — Allah knows and you do not know — same phrase as 2:216 Allah knows you do not know about dislike love.\n\nCure: return to Knower, submit where knowledge ends as firm knowledge people said we believe all from Lord (7).\n\nPeople of Book argued Ibrahim from desire, not knowledge, as earlier deviant hearts follow mutashabih seeking discord (7). Same pattern.\n\nNext clarifies Ibrahim.",
  "67": "Ibrahim was not Jew nor Christian, but he was upright, a Muslim, and not among polytheists. Ma kana Ibrahim Yahudiyyan wa la Nasraniyyan — Ibrahim neither Jew nor Christian — labels later.\n\nWa lakin kana hanifan musliman — but upright — hanif — turning away crookedness to straightness — musliman — submitted — same as aslamtu submission (3:20).\n\nWa ma kana min al-mushrikin — not among polytheists — strong negation. Though father idol maker, he never joined.\n\nHanif Muslim definition important: not tribal but quality.\n\nThis verse centre for common word — tawhid.\n\nIt also answers why argue about Ibrahim — true allegiance not label but way — way is hanif Muslim — turning toward Allah fully, not associating.\n\nFor Muslims who claim Ibrahim by lineage only, same rebuke: are you hanif Muslim?",
  "68": "Indeed closest people to Ibrahim are those who followed him, this Prophet, and those who believed — Allah is Guardian of believers.\n\nInna awla an-nasi bi-Ibrahim lalladhina ittaba'uh — closest — awla — most worthy friend ally to Ibrahim are those who followed him — ittaba'uh — not those who merely descend.\n\nWa hadha an-Nabiyyu walladhina amanu — and this Prophet — Muhammad — and those who believed.\n\nWallahu Waliyy al-mu'minin — Allah Guardian of believers — as earlier Allah Guardian believers brings darkness light (2:257). So closeness to Ibrahim determined by following not blood, and Allah guardians those followers.\n\nThis closes argument Ibrahim lineage. Best claim not Jews Christians as inherited, but followers of his millah including final Prophet and believers.\n\nChain: if follow Ibrahim, follow his way which is Islam Way (19) common word (64) and Muhammad. Thus invitation not abandonment Ibrahim but true adherence.\n\nNext wishes of People Book to mislead.",
  "69": "A group of People of Book wish they could mislead you, but they mislead only themselves while they perceive not. Waddat ta'ifatun min Ahli al-Kitab law yudillunakum — group wishes to mislead you believers from Islam to their faith (as 2:109 envy wish turn back after belief).\n\nWa ma yudilluna illa anfusahum wa ma yash'urun — they mislead only themselves — not perceiving — because misleading after knowledge increases own deviation, Allah increases disease (2:10).\n\nWishes not real ability; Allah made believers middle nation witnesses (2:143). So attempts fail except self-harm.\n\nSame as Satan threatened poverty orders immorality but does not force; those who follow mislead themselves.\n\nNext verses question why reject signs, mix truth falsehood.",
  "70": "O People of the Book, why do you disbelieve in Allah's signs while you bear witness to their truth? Ya Ahl al-Kitab lima takfuruna bi-ayatillah wa antum tashhadun — Why disbelieve while you witness?\n\nTashhadun carries two layers: you bear witness within your own books — description of Muhammad in Torah, prophethood Isa as servant, tawhid — and you bear witness with your own eyes when sign came — Isa's miracles by permission, change of qibla, Badr help.\n\nKufr after shahadah worse than ignorance — knowledge increases accountability.\n\nThis question repeats later verbatim at verse 98, framing entire discussion about concealing, mixing, twisting. Same question after explaining first House Bakkah blessed — why disbelieve signs while Allah Witness over what you do? So it appears twice intentionally.\n\nFor teacher today: when you know sign — knew riba war with Allah, knew hijab, knew prayer — and conceal or disbelieve, grief greater because you witnessed.\n\nThe verse does not answer for them; it leaves question hanging for self-reflection, which is more piercing than statement.\n\nNext verse asks why clothe truth with falsehood while knowing — deeper layer: disbelief not only passive rejection but active mixing.",
  "71": "O People of Book, why do you clothe truth with falsehood and hide truth while you know? Why talbis — mixing truth falsehood as garment mixing — and conceal truth while know. Two crimes: lacing truth with falsehood so people cannot separate, and kitman — concealing remaining truth you know — both while know.\n\nClothe truth with falsehood example: quoting Torah about Ibrahim but inserting claim Jew, or saying Uzayr son Allah, or saying Isa god, mixing real reverence for Isa with exaggeration, or inserting laws not from Allah, or saying Fire few days (24).\n\nHide truth while know — hide description Muhammad, hide ayah riba, hide testimony.\n\n\"While you know\" — aggravates.\n\nEarlier same phrase (2:42) do not mix truth falsehood conceal while know. Same censure repeated because same behaviour.\n\nMixing more dangerous than open denial because borrows authority truth it mixed into, ordinary person cannot separate.\n\nFor teachers today: selective quotation, verse without context, religious language attached to whatever audience wants, hiding inconvenient half. Test simple: does person walk closer to what Allah actually said or closer to what suits me?",
  "72": "A group of People of Book said, Believe at beginning of day in what was revealed to believers and disbelieve at its end, so perhaps they will return —.\n\nPlot: some scholars said let's pretend enter Islam morning, leave evening, so that onlookers think Muslims faith unstable, maybe they will doubt and return. Believing beginning day rejecting end — technique confusion.\n\nLa'allahum yarji'un — so they may return — goal turn believers back after faith (69).\n\nTactic manipulative conversion: feigned interest then loud apostasy to create scandal. Used today via media: person claims ex-Muslim reveals inner faults, morning belief evening rejection to cause doubt.\n\nQuran exposes plan so believers not shaken. True faith not shaken by theatrics.\n\nNext verse they said only trust co-religionists.",
  "73": "And do not trust except who follows your religion — Say, guidance is Allah's guidance — lest someone given like what you were given, or they argue with you before Lord — Say, bounty is in Allah's hand giving to whom wills, Allah Vast Knowing.\n\nThey said privately: do not trust except fellow Jews; keep plan between us.\n\nThen Quran says: Say guidance is Allah guidance — true huda not tribal. Also fear lest others given like what you were given — i.e., revelation given to Arabs like Torah given to you — so envy drives concealment. Or they argue with you before Lord — they fear Muslims will use Torah against them on Day.\n\nSay bounty is in Allah hand giving whom wills — earlier (2:105) Allah chooses mercy whom wills — bounty not limited you. Allah Wasi' Alim — Vast Knowing — bounty vast, knows who truly deserves.\n\nBounty includes prophethood, guidance, provision. Envy that others receive closes door not open.\n\nLesson for Muslim: likewise do not restrict trust to kin only rejecting truth elsewhere; guidance Allah's.\n\nNext verse He chooses mercy.",
  "74": "He chooses for His mercy whom He wills — Allah is Possessor of great bounty. Yakhtassu bi-rahmatihi man yasha — He singles out for mercy whom wills — mercy includes nubuwwah, Quran, Islam, guidance.\n\nWallahu dhu al-fadli al-azim — Owner great bounty — same closing as 2:105. No one's envy diminishes.\n\nAfter plot morning evening, reminder that choice belongs Allah, not plot.\n\nMaryam chosen (42), Zakariya given Yahya despite old age — all choosing.\n\nSo if Allah chooses Muhammad from Isma'il line, no tribal vote abrogates.\n\nFor believer: ask for mercy from Owner great bounty, not from gatekeepers who trust only own.\n\nNext about trustworthiness with wealth.",
  "75": "Among People of Book is one who if you entrust him with qintar — large heap — will return it, and among them is one who if entrusted with dinar will not return unless you stand demanding.\n\nQintar — huge sum — some among People Book trustworthy despite theological error: return heap if entrusted. Example Abdullah ibn Salam? Others betrayal for dinar small — will not return unless standing demanding — qaim — pestering.\n\nWhy difference? Because they say, There is no blame on us regarding unlettered — ummiyyin — Arabs. Claim: covenant only within our community, taking from gentiles permissible — deception using religion to justify betrayal.\n\nThey say about Allah lie while they know — yakdhibun — lie attribution.\n\nThis verse balances: Quran not blanket condemn all People Book; acknowledges upright among them (as later 113-115 upright community recite at night). Some trustworthy despite difference. Others treacherous justifying.\n\n\"There is no blame on us regarding unlettered\" same logic as earlier riba rationalization trade like riba — religion twisted.\n\nFor Muslim dealing today: evaluate person not by label but amanah.\n\nNext about covenant.",
  "76": "No — whoever fulfills covenant and is mindful — then Allah loves the mindful. Bala — No — correction to claim no blame regarding unlettered.\n\nMan awfa bi-ahdihi wattaqa — whoever fulfills covenant and is mindful — taqa — keeps promise, avoids betrayal. Fa inna Allaha yuhibbu al-muttaqin — Allah loves mindful.\n\nCovenant includes contracts with people and with Allah: not betray even if other person unlettered, even if other disbeliever.\n\nAllah loves muttaqin — repeated loves — loves doers good (2:195), loves those mindful. Loves opposite not loving wrongdoers etc.\n\nSo trustworthiness standard faith: fulfil covenant, be mindful.\n\nNext those who exchange covenant small price.",
  "77": "Those who exchange Allah's covenant and their oaths for small price — they have no share in Hereafter, Allah will not speak to them nor look at them on Day, nor purify them — painful punishment.\n\nYashtaru — exchange — covenant Allah and oaths — ayman — for small price — thamanan qalilan — same as 2:41, 2:174 — sell religion small worldly gain: bribes judges (2:188), twisting Book, oath false to steal property.\n\nNo share Hereafter — la khalaq — no portion.\n\nLa yukallimuhum Allahu — will not speak to them — same as 2:174 Allah will not speak to them — silence most terrifying — no merciful speech, no purification tazkiya.\n\nPainful punishment.\n\nThis verse severe for perjury, false oath to take property: Prophet said whoever swears false oath to take Muslim's property will meet Allah angry.\n\nLinks to trust: betrayal for dinar small but consequence huge.\n\nOpposite those who fulfil covenant Allah loves — these no share.\n\nNext group distorts Book with tongues.",
  "78": "Among them is group who twist Book with their tongues so you think it is from Book but not from Book, and they say It is from Allah but not from Allah — they say lie about Allah while know.\n\nYalwuna alsinatahum bil-kitab — twist tongues with Book — ta'wil mispronunciation, adding words, changing meaning, quoting out context to make you think from Book — like earlier mixing truth falsehood.\n\nThey say \"It is from Allah\" but not from Allah — deliberate attribution.\n\nYaqluluna al-kadhiba 'ala Allah wa hum ya'lamun — say lie about Allah while know — same phrase as 75.\n\nThis is third form concealment: earlier hiding, mixing, now twisting recitation.\n\nExamples: recite verse about permission but twist to make it sound prohibition, or add commentary as if Quran.\n\nToday similar: quoting hadith fabricated, twisting translation, mistranslating to support desire, saying \"Islam says\" while no source.\n\nQuran exposes technique so believers ask proof (2:111).\n\nNext not for human given Book to say be worshippers of me.",
  "79": "It is not for a human whom Allah gave Book and wisdom and prophethood to say to people, Be servants to me besides Allah — but be rabbani — devoted to Lord — because you teach Book and because you study.\n\nMa kana libasharin — not for human — whom Allah gave Kitab, hukm (wisdom judgment), nubuwwah — to say be worshippers of me besides Allah — be servants to me. No prophet says worship me.\n\nBut be rabbaniyyin — rabbani — devoted to Lord, learned, teaching others to be devoted — bima kuntum tu'allimuna al-kitab wa bima kuntum tadrusun — because you teach Book and study.\n\nRabbaniyyin — one who nurtures people with small knowledge before large, teaches for Allah.\n\nIsa never said worship me; he said Allah my Lord your Lord worship Him (51). Muhammad never said worship me; he said be servants Allah.\n\nThis verse refutes deification of Isa, Uzayr, saints, also refutes clergy who want followers worship them as lords besides Allah (common word 64 warned not take one another as lords).\n\nTeaching Book and studying leads to rabnaniyyah, not to claiming lordship.\n\nNext not order angels prophets as lords.",
  "80": "Nor would he order you to take angels and prophets as lords — would he order you to disbelieve after you have submitted? Wa la ya'murakum an tattakhidhu al-malaikata wan-nabiyyina arbaban — Nor order angels prophets as lords — as polytheists took angels daughters, as some took Isa as lord, as some took saints.\n\nAya'murukum bil-kufri ba'da idh antum muslimun — would he order disbelief after you have become Muslims? Prophet inviting to kufr impossible.\n\nThus deification of Isa not from Isa but from followers twisting (78). Isa's true call rabnaniyyah, worship Lord alone, not angel lordship.\n\nConnects to common word (64) not take one another as lords besides Allah — that includes not taking Isa as lord, not taking scholars as lawgivers overriding halal haram.\n\nIf someone calls to worship himself or angels prophets as lords, he is not true rabbani.\n\nNext covenant prophets to believe final messenger.",
  "81": "And when Allah took covenant of prophets — If I give you Book and wisdom then messenger comes to you confirming what with you — you must believe in him and help him — He said, Do you affirm and take My covenant on that? They said, We affirm — He said, So bear witness and I am with you among witnesses.\n\nMithaq prophets: When Allah gave any prophet Book and wisdom, then messenger confirming what with them comes — you must believe and help — tu'minunna bihi wa tan-surunna.\n\nThis is covenant for final Prophet Muhammad, confirming previous. Each prophet told community to believe final messenger if appears, and prophets themselves affirmed.\n\nAlastu biraddikum? They said aqrarna — we affirm. Allah said fashhadu — bear witness — wa ana ma'akum min ash-shahidin — I am with you witnesses.\n\nThis covenant explains why People Book knew him as sons (2:146) — prophets told them.\n\nIt also shows prophets unity — chain descendants one another (34) cooperating not competing.\n\nIf prophets must believe final messenger, how much more their followers?\n\nThis covenant makes turning away clear breach.\n\nNext anyone seeks other than Islam Way.",
  "82": "So whoever turns away after this — they are the defiantly disobedient. Fa-man tawalla ba'da dhalika fa-ula'ika hum al-fasiqun — After what? After covenant of prophets (81) that they must believe and help final messenger confirming what with them.\n\nTawalla — turns away — after affirming.\n\nFa-ula'ika hum al-fasiqun — they are fasiqun — defiantly disobedient, stepping outside — fisq — same root as those who exchange covenant small price (77), who twist Book.\n\nFisq here not minor sin but breach of primordial covenant binding all prophets. To reject Muhammad after prophets covenant is to step outside lineage chosen families descendants one another (34), outside Islam Way (19).\n\nProphets themselves bore witness — fashhadu wa ana ma'akum min ash-shahidin — Allah with them among witnesses. So turning away after such witnessed covenant carries weight.\n\nFor People of Book who claimed to follow Musa Isa, this covenant says your own prophets already pledged to believe help final messenger. Turning away therefore not loyalty to Musa Isa but disobedience to them.\n\nIt also tells Muslims: covenant not only for past; you also pledged when you said amanna? Have you helped messenger by following?\n\nNext rhetorical: Do they seek other than Allah's way?",
  "83": "Do they seek other than Allah's way while to Him has submitted whoever is in heavens and earth — willingly or unwillingly — and to Him they will be returned? Afa-ghayra dini Allah yabghun — Do they seek other than Allah's way — deen Allah — while to Him submitted all in heavens earth — taw'an wa karhan — willingly or unwillingly — angels willingly, disbeliever unwillingly body submits to laws death, etc.\n\nWa ilayhi yurja'un — to Him returned — as earlier to Allah destination (28) and matters returned (109). If everything submits to Him willingly or not, why seek other deen?\n\nThis verse after covenant shows Islam Way is not just human religion among options but cosmic deen — everything already Muslim in sense submitting to natural laws He placed. Child in womb shaped as wills submits, sun rises east submits. Only human heart tries not submit. Seeking other than deen contradicts cosmic submission.\n\nFor believer, comfort: your submission joins universal submission; you are not alone.\n\nNext commanding to declare belief in all prophets.",
  "84": "Say, We believe in Allah and what was revealed to us and what was revealed to Ibrahim, Isma'il, Ishaq, Ya'qub and tribes, and what was given to Musa, Isa and prophets from their Lord — we make no distinction between any of them — to Him we have submitted.\n\nSame charter as 2:136 — We believe in Allah and what revealed to us and what revealed to Ibrahim etc — la nufarriqu bayna ahad minhum — no distinction between any of them — wa nahnu lahu muslimun — to Him submitted.\n\nRepetition in Al-Imran after covenant reinforces unity chain.\n\nIf we make no distinction, why do Jews distinguish rejecting Isa Muhammad, Christians distinguish rejecting Muhammad? That distinction breaks covenant.\n\nOur Way is to accept all without distinction.\n\nThis verse Prophet taught to recite morning.\n\nNext whoever seeks other than Islam Way.",
  "85": "And whoever seeks other than Islam as way — it will never be accepted from him — in Hereafter he will be among losers. Wa man yabtaghi ghayra al-Islam dinan fa-lan yuqbala minhu — whoever seeks other than Islam as deen — after it introduced as only Way with Allah (19) and after common word tawhid — never accepted.\n\nWa huwa fil-akhirati min al-khasirin — among losers — same word khasir with wife Imran fear? Losers like those traded guidance error no profit.\n\nThis does not contradict there being some among People Book who truly believed before Muhammad and were rewarded (2:62) — those followed their prophet sincerely before final; after final came, seeking other than Islam is loss.\n\nVerse makes exclusivity not tribal but truth-based — Islam submission to Allah alone — that was way of Ibrahim hanif muslem, Isa saying Allah my Lord your Lord, etc.\n\nAcceptance criterion submission, not label.\n\nNext about those who disbelieved after belief.",
  "86": "How shall Allah guide people who disbelieved after having believed and witnessed messenger is true and clear proofs came to them? Allah does not guide wrongdoing people. Kayfa yahdi Allahu qawman kafaru ba'da imanihim — How guide people who disbelieved after belief and witnessing messenger true and proofs came? Question rhetorical showing enormity.\n\nWashahidu — they witnessed messenger true — like knowing him as sons — then turned.\n\nWallahu la yahdi al-qawma az-zalimin — Allah does not guide wrongdoing people — same closing as earlier wrongdoers conceal etc.\n\nThese likely apostates or People Book who recognized then rejected after knowledge — deliberate kufr after iman.\n\nNext consequence curse.",
  "87": "Those — their recompense is that the curse of Allah, angels, and all humanity is upon them — abiding therein — punishment not lightened nor given respite. Ula'ika jaza'uhum anna alayhim la'nat Allah wal-malaikati wan-nasi ajma'in — those who disbelieved after belief and witnessed messenger true and proofs came — their recompense curse Allah, angels, all people.\n\nCurse — la'nah — expulsion from mercy. Curse Allah alone severe; adding angels and all people shows consensus cosmic.\n\nKhalidina fiha la yukhaffafu anhum al-adhab wa la hum yunzarun — abiding therein, punishment not lightened, nor given respite — same as (2:162) for those die disbelievers, same as (2:162) abiding curse punishment not lightened.\n\nRecompense matches: they cursed truth after knowing — said Fire few days, said Allah poor, said Isa god — so curse returns.\n\nLa yukhaffafu — no lightening — human imprisonment has parole; this has none.\n\nWa la hum yunzarun — nor respite — no delay to prepare.\n\nRepeats earlier to show severity apostasy after clear.\n\nBut immediate exception next verse opens door: except those who repent after and correct.\n\nMercy still after curse warning.",
  "88": "Except those who repent after that and correct — indeed Allah is Forgiving, Merciful. Illa alladhina tabu min ba'di dhalika wa aslahu — Except those who repent after that apostasy and correct — islah — fix what corrupted.\n\nRepentance here not just feeling regret; taba includes return, and aslahu includes correcting: if hid description Muhammad, make clear; if killed prophets legacy, revive justice; if exchanged covenant small price, return rights.\n\nFa-inna Allaha Ghafur Rahim — Forgiving, Merciful — same closing as many verses after severe warnings (2:225 forgiveness for unintentional oaths, 2:173 forgiving merciful for necessity). Allah's names Ghafur Rahim always after opening door back.\n\nThis shows difference between those who disbelieve after belief then increase disbelief whose repentance never accepted (89) because they increase until death forced, vs those who repent soon and correct — accepted.\n\nConnects to earlier (2:160) except those repent correct clarify — same triad: repent, correct, clarify.\n\nSo even after worst category — disbelieve after belief and witnessing messenger true — if person returns quickly and fixes, forgiveness.\n\nEncouragement for anyone who left Islam or disguised truth for worldly gain — way back exists: repent and correct.\n\nNext category those increased disbelief.",
  "89": "Indeed those who disbelieved after belief then increased in disbelief — their repentance will never be accepted — they are astray. Those kafaru ba'da imanihim thumma izdadu kufran — disbelieved after belief then increased — added mockery, plot morning evening, killing prophets legacy. Lan tuqbala tawbatuhum — repentance never accepted — likely means when death comes, or repentance not sincere but to hide.\n\nWa ula'ika hum ad-dallun — astray.\n\nDifference from previous verse where repentance accepted: previous repented before death sincerely correcting; these increased disbelief until death or until repentance forced by seeing punishment, not sincere.\n\nThus Quran distinguishes.\n\nNext die disbelievers.",
  "90": "Those who disbelieved and died as disbelievers — never would be accepted from any of them even earth full of gold as ransom — painful punishment and no helpers. Inna alladhina kafaru wa matu wa hum kuffar fa-lan yuqbala min ahadihim mil'u al-ardi dhahaban wa law iftada bihi — Those disbelieved and died disbelievers — matu wa hum kuffar — final state dies upon kufr — never accepted from any even earth full gold as ransom.\n\nMil'u al-ardi dhahaban — earth full gold — imagination largest wealth (14 heaped gold silver). If offered as fidya — ransom — to escape Fire, not accepted.\n\nUla'ika lahum adhabun alim wa ma lahum min nasirin — Painful punishment no helpers — as earlier no helpers (22,56).\n\nGold cannot purchase iman after death, whereas spending what you love before death (91) attains birr, purchases Gardens.\n\nEarlier no ransom accepted (2:48,123), no soul avail another, no bargaining Day (2:254). Here gold earth's worth — still no.\n\nThis verse closes section about turning away after covenant and after belief.\n\nIt makes believer value spending beloved now before earth full gold worthless.\n\nNext verse attains birr by spending beloved — opposite trade.\n\nFor rich who withholds bounty thinking good, reminder: withheld gold will become collar (185) not ransom.",
  "91": "You will never attain righteousness until you spend from what you love — whatever you spend — Allah knows it. Lan tanalu al-birra hatta tunfiqu mimma tuhibbun — You will never attain birr — righteousness — until spend from what love. Birr earlier defined not faces east west but faith spending despite love (2:177). Now attainment condition: spend what love.\n\nMimma tuhibbun — from what you love — beloved wealth, beloved child dedication, beloved time.\n\nWa ma tunfiqu min shay'in fa-inna Allaha bihi Alim — whatever spend Allah knows — Alim reward.\n\nStory of Abu Talha had beloved garden Bayruha opposite mosque, when verse revealed gave it for Allah. Such spending is birr.\n\nThis verse after warnings about those who exchange covenant small price, who hide Book small price — opposite: spend beloved for Allah to attain birr.\n\nIt also bridges to story about food forbidden to Israel — Israel (Ya'qub) loved certain food and forbade himself? Actually next verse about food.\n\nInvitation: check beloved what hard to give?\n\nNext food before Torah.",
  "92": "All food was lawful to Children of Israel except what Israel forbade for himself before Torah revealed — Say bring Torah and recite it if truthful. Kullu at-ta'am kana hillan li-Bani Isra'il illa ma harrama Isra'il ala nafsih — All food lawful to Children Israel except what Israel — Ya'qub — forbade for himself before Torah. He had sciatica, avoided camel meat milk vowed.\n\nYews claim camel meat forbidden by Allah since Ibrahim, but actually not — only Ya'qub forbade himself due to illness before Torah. Torah came later.\n\nQul fa'tu bit-Tawrat fatluha in kuntum sadiqin — Bring Torah recite if truthful — challenge. Torah does not forbid foods they claimed forbidden now. Their claim fabrication about Allah.\n\nProve tying to earlier mixing concealing — invented prohibitions ascribing to Allah.\n\nIt also shows dietary laws evolving — similar abrogation concept.\n\nNext whoever fabricates lie after.",
  "93": "So whoever fabricates lie about Allah after that — they are wrongdoers. Fa-man iftara ala Allahi al-kadhiba min ba'di dhalika fa-ula'ika hum az-zalimun — fabrication after proof brought — bringing Torah would expose. Those who invent lie about Allah after truth — zalimun — wrongdoers, because lie about Allah corrupts deen (common word). Same as those twist tongues, claim from Allah while not (78). Wrongdoers not loved.\n\nFabrication includes saying Fire few days, claiming exclusive paradise, claiming camel meat forbidden by Allah, claiming Isa god, claiming Allah poor we rich (181).\n\nAfter challenge to bring Torah, warning terrible.\n\nNext says Allah has spoken truth so follow Ibrahim hanif.",
  "94": "Say, Allah has spoken truth — so follow religion of Ibrahim, upright — he was not among polytheists. Qul sadaqa Allahu — Say Allah has spoken truth — sadaqa — truthful. Allah is as-Sadiq — truthful in statement, promise. After challenge bring Torah recite if truthful (93) to prove food claim, Jew claim refuted — Allah truthful, they fabricating.\n\nFattabi'u millata Ibrahim hanifa — Follow millah Ibrahim hanif — upright turning from crooked to straight — hanif — as earlier (67) Ibrahim not Jew Christian but hanif Muslim.\n\nWa ma kana min al-mushrikin — Not among polytheists — as earlier father idol maker but never joined.\n\nIf Allah spoke truth — sadaqa — and Ibrahim hanif Muslim not among polytheists, then following him is following truthful.\n\nMillah Ibrahim includes Tawhid, spending beloved (Ibrahim willingness sacrifice son), building House Bakkah, du'a accept from us (2:127), submitting (3:20).\n\nSo command not abstract follow but follow lived way.\n\nAfter refuting invented prohibitions and lies, way forward is not new invention but return to hanif Ibrahim.\n\nNext first House placed for humanity at Bakkah blessed guidance.",
  "95": "Indeed first House placed for humanity is the one at Bakkah — blessed and guidance for worlds. Inna awwala baytin wudi'a lin-nas lalladhi bi-Bakkata — first House placed for humanity — House — Bayt — al-Ka'bah — at Bakkah — same as Makkah — older name Bakkah — meaning crowding.\n\nMubarakan wa hudan lil-alamin — blessed and guidance for worlds — blessed — barakah — because worship there multiplied, provision fruits brought due dua Ibrahim (2:126), guidance for worlds because first tawhid centre, all prophets faced? Place where submission started.\n\nConnection Ibrahim hanif — he raised foundations House (2:127) — so House link.\n\nFirst House not first building but first placed for humanity purpose worship — humanity first purpose worship (51:56).\n\nBlessed guidance contrasts those who mixed truth falsehood — House pure guidance.\n\nNext ayah containing clear signs.\n\nFor believer, longing first House — craving qibla earlier answered (2:144) — is longing first House.\n\nNext clear signs station Ibrahim.",
  "96": "In it are clear signs — standing place of Ibrahim — whoever enters it is safe — pilgrimage to House duty for Allah on people who can afford way — whoever disbelieves — Allah Free of need from worlds. Fihi ayatun bayyinat — in it clear signs — including Maqam Ibrahim — footprints stone, water Zamzam, safety.\n\nWa man dakhalahu kana aminan — whoever enters safe — historic: even pagan who committed murder could not be harmed inside Haram; sanctuary secure.\n\nWa lillahi ala an-nasi hijju al-bayt man istata'a ilayhi sabila — Hajj duty upon who can afford way — istita'ah — capability body wealth.\n\nWa man kafara fa-inna Allaha Ghaniyyun an al-alamin — whoever disbelieves — denies Hajj obligation — Allah Ghani free need worlds — as earlier Self-Sufficient does not need charity (2:263). Hajj benefits pilgrim not Allah.\n\nFirst House blessed guidance; entering safe; Hajj duty; clear signs.\n\nYet People Book dispute about it — next verse why disbelieve signs.\n\nPilgrimage duty connects provision taqwa best provision (2:197) and spending beloved (92).\n\nQuran mentions first House after discussion Ibrahim to prove Ibrahim connection to Ka'bah not Temple alone — common heritage.\n\nNext rebuke People Book reject signs.",
  "97": "Say, O People of Book, why do you disbelieve in Allah's signs while Allah is Witness over what you do? Repeated question same as 70 — Ya Ahl al-Kitab lima takfuruna bi-ayatillah Wallahu Shahidun ala ma ta'malun — why disbelieve signs while Allah Witness what you do.\n\nSigns here includes first House at Bakkah blessed guidance worlds (95) clear signs station Ibrahim within it (96) safety entering, Hajj duty (95-96). These were known to People Book — Ibrahim raised foundations with Isma'il, first House.\n\nShahid ala ma ta'malun — Witness over what you do — includes concealment covenant not making clear (192), casting behind backs small price, killing prophets, twisting tongues.\n\nRepetition deliberate: after describing first House, asks why disbelieve despite witness? Bakkah House is sign they cannot deny Ibrahim connection, yet they turn.\n\nWitness name comforts believers: your Hajj, your facing qibla, your holding rope — witnessed.\n\nFor those hiding, warning: witness also sees hiding.\n\nSecond occurrence after first House emphasizes universal: disbelief not due lack signs but despite witness.\n\nNext why avert believers from path seeking crookedness while witnesses.",
  "98": "O People of Book, why do you avert from Allah's path those who believe — seeking it crooked while you are witnesses? Why repel?\n\nYa Ahl al-Kitab lima tasudduna an sabili Allah man amana tabghunaha iwajan wa antum shuhada — Why avert from Allah's path those who believe seeking crookedness while you witnesses?\n\nTasudduna an sabili Allah — averting — sadd — blocking — as earlier averting people from Allah path and disbelieving and Sacred Mosque and expelling its people greater with Allah (2:217). Now same blocking but through doubt: morning-evening plot (72), claiming only trust co-religionists, mixing truth falsehood (71).\n\nTabghunaha iwajan — seek it crooked — want straight path Islam to appear crooked — i'waj — bent — by adding conditions (offering consumed by fire), by claiming Ibrahim Jew Christian, by claiming Isa god.\n\nWa antum shuhada — while you are witnesses — again shuhada — you witness that path straight, as you know him as sons, know true story qasas al-haqq.\n\nWa ma Allahu bi-ghafilin amma ta'malun — Allah not unaware what you do — closing similar to witness name.\n\nAfter repeated why disbelieve signs (70,97), now why avert others seeking crooked while witnesses — escalation from self disbelief to active missionary of doubt.\n\nFor believers, if they obey such party among given Scripture, they will be turned back after belief into disbelievers (99) — next verse.\n\nSo warning double.",
  "99": "O you who believe, if you obey a party among those given Scripture, they will turn you back into disbelievers after having believed. Ya ayyuha alladhina amanu in tuti'u fariqan min alladhina utu al-Kitab yaruddukum ba'da imanikum kafirin — if obey group among People Book they will turn you back after belief.\n\nYaruddukum — turn back — same as wish mislead.\n\nObeying here meaning following their desires, accepting their twist, doubting due to their claims.\n\nSame warning as 2:109 many among People Book wish turn you back out of envy after truth clear.\n\nPrescription: do not obey those who wish mislead; obey Allah Messenger (32).\n\nNext how can you disbelieve while...",
  "100": "And how can you disbelieve while Allah's verses recited to you and among you is His Messenger? Whoever holds fast to Allah has been guided to straight path. Wa kayfa takfuruna wa antum tutla alaykum ayatullah... — How can you disbelieve while verses recited and among you Messenger? At time revelation ongoing.\n\nWa man ya'tasim billah fa-qad hudiya ila sirat mustaqim — whoever holds fast to Allah guided straight path.\n\nI'tisam — holding fast rope — same as hold rope Allah (next verse) — rope Allah.\n\nWith verses recited and Messenger present, disbelief contradiction.\n\nFor us verses still recited though Messenger not among physically, his Sunnah present, his seerah present, Quran still recited — same question applies.\n\nHolding fast to Allah — reliance, dhikr, dua earlier rasikhun — guides straight path earlier described as worship Allah my Lord your Lord (51).\n\nNext verse command fear hold rope together.",
  "101": "O you who believe, fear Allah as He should be feared, and do not die except while you are in submission. Ittaqullah haqqa tuqatih — fear Allah as He should be feared — haqqa — rightful due — not slight mindfulness but true taqwa: obey not disobeyed, remembered not forgotten, thanked not ungrateful as companions interpreted. Yet Allah does not burden beyond capacity (2:286) — so haqqa tuqatih means as much as you are able, with effort, with sincerity.\n\nWa la tamutunna illa wa antum muslimun — do not die except while Muslims — same as Ya'qub advice to sons (2:132) and Ibrahim (2:132). Death cannot be scheduled, so live in submission at all times so however death finds, finds Muslim. No one controls time death, so directive means maintain Islam continuously.\n\nAfter verse how can you disbelieve while verses recited and Messenger among you (100), now fear as should be feared, and do not die except submission — linking taqwa and final state.\n\nTaqwa here preceded holding rope together (next) — taqwa individual, rope communal.\n\nFor us today recited verses still, though Messenger not physically, his rope still — Quran Sunnah — fear as should be feared asks continuous return.\n\nNext hold firm to rope Allah together.",
  "102": "And hold fast to rope of Allah all together and do not become divided — remember favour of Allah upon you — when you were enemies and He joined hearts and you became brothers by His favour — and you were on edge of Fire pit and He saved you — thus Allah makes clear signs so you may be guided.\n\nWa'tasimu bi-habli Allah jami'an wa la tafarraqu — Hold fast rope Allah together — Habl Allah — rope — Quran, Islam, covenant — strong rope extended from heaven earth if held, you not fall. Jami'an — all together — communal.\n\nReminder favour: when you were enemies — Aws Khazraj centuries war — joined hearts, became brothers by His favour — ni'mah — Islam. And were on edge pit Fire — shafa hufratin min an-nar — disbelief, tribal vengeance leading Fire, and He saved.\n\nThat favour experienced Madinah firsthand. Before Islam tribal feud, after Islam brotherhood.\n\nThus Allah makes clear signs so you may be guided — yubayyin — as before makes clear verses so you may understand (2:242).\n\nThis verse after fear how should be feared — individual taqwa plus collective rope prevents division.\n\nModern ummah divided along national, racial, sectarian — rope one but hands many divided. Return rope together.\n\nNext collective duty invite good.",
  "103": "And let there be among you an ummah inviting to good, ordering what is right and forbidding what is wrong — they are successful. Waltakun minkum ummatun yad'una ila al-khayr wa ya'muruna bil-ma'ruf wa yanhawna an al-munkar — Let there be among you group calling to good — khayr — Islam, and ordering ma'ruf — known right — forbidding munkar — rejected wrong.\n\nUmmah within ummah? Scholars two readings: from among you there should be group whose job dawah — specialists; or you all should be ummah calling. Both true: collective duty but specialised group needed.\n\nWa ula'ika hum al-muflihun — they successful — falah same as farmers earlier (2:5) — success because enjoining right forbidding wrong preserves community like rope.\n\nAfter holding rope together, active maintenance: call good, forbid wrong prevents rope fraying.\n\nThis verse is foundation hisbah, dawah.\n\nFor individual, at least invite family to good, forbid in gentle way.\n\nNext do not be like those divided after clear proofs.",
  "104": "And do not be like those who became divided and differed after clear proofs came to them — they will have tremendous punishment. Wa la takunu kalladhina tafarraqu wakhtalafu min ba'di ma ja'ahum al-bayyinat — Do not be like those divided differed after bayyinat came — refers to People Book differed out of baghy after knowledge (19), and also others.\n\nWa ula'ika lahum adhabun azim — tremendous punishment — because division after knowledge caused great harm, led to killing prophets, twisting Book.\n\nAfter command hold rope together and invite good, warning what happens if not: become like divided — success replaced punishment.\n\nDivide after clear proofs worst — proofs were meant to unite, using them to divide perverse.\n\nToday Muslims divide after Quran Sunnah clear — using fiqh minor differences to cause hate, using tribal pride — same pattern.\n\nNext describes Day white faces black faces.",
  "105": "On a Day some faces will become white and some black — as for those blackened faces — Did you disbelieve after having believed? Then taste punishment for disbelief.\n\nYawma tabyaddu wujuhun wa taswaddu wujuh — Day Faces white and black — white — bright honor joy — black — shame gloom.\n\nFa-amma alladhina iswaddat wujuhuhum — those blackened — asked Did you disbelieve after belief? — akafartum ba'da imanikum — turning back after Islam.\n\nFa-dhuqu al-adhaba bima kuntum takfurun — taste punishment for disbelief — taste — immediate.\n\nWhite vs black faces result of inner heart — those with deviation following mutashabih seeking discord earlier (7) faces darken; those who remembered Allah standing sitting lying reflecting — faces whiten.\n\nAfter division warning, Day when division manifests physically on faces.\n\nFor us self-check: which gathering would whiten face?\n\nNext those white faces.",
  "106": "As for those whose faces whitened — in mercy of Allah — they will abide therein forever. Wa amma alladhina ibyaddat wujuhuhum fa-fi rahmatillah — in mercy Allah — Rahmah — first mercy asked by rasikhun (8) grant mercy from Yourself — now mercy as space they abide.\n\nHum fiha khalidun — abiding forever — as earlier khulud for no fear grieve (2:112 etc).\n\nMercy as location, not just attribute. Inside mercy.\n\nWhite faces due to tawhid, holding rope, inviting good, not dividing after clear proofs, spending beloved (92), etc.\n\nBlack faces fuel Fire — previously wealth children fuel Fire (10). White faces in mercy.\n\nAfter this awaits — these are verses Allah We recite in truth — next verse.\n\nThus encouragement hold rope to be among white faces.",
  "107": "These are verses of Allah — We recite them to you in truth — Allah wants no injustice for worlds. Tilka ayatullah natluha alayka bil-haqq — These verses — signs — We recite you truth — as earlier recite signs wise reminder (58). Truth — haqq — from Lord.\n\nWa ma Allahu yuridu zulman lil-alamin — Allah wants no injustice for worlds — la yuridu — Does not want injustice. So punishment white/black faces not injustice but justice — no one wronged (25, 2:281). Allocation by earning.\n\nIf Allah wants no injustice, then holding rope, fearing as should be feared, spending beloved — all just commands for mercy, not to oppress.\n\nThis verse closes section about unity and Faces Day before moving to best nation.\n\nIt also mirrors opening: Nothing hidden, shaping wombs as wills, precise foundation — all by Truth.\n\nAfter establishing justice, next verse declares best nation.",
  "108": "You were best nation produced for humanity — you enjoin right and forbid wrong and believe in Allah — if People of Book had believed it would be better — among them believers but most defiantly disobedient.\n\nKuntum khayra ummatin ukhrijat lin-nas — You were best nation produced for humanity — khayra ummah — best — not by lineage but by role: produced — ukhrijat — for humanity — for people benefit, not for self pride. Why best? Ta'muruna bil-ma'ruf wa tanhawna an al-munkar wa tu'minuna billah — enjoin right forbid wrong believe Allah — same as earlier letting be among you ummah inviting good (103). Bestness conditional on carrying out.\n\nWa law amana Ahlu al-Kitab lakana khayran lahum — If People Book believed, better for them — invitation remains.\n\nMinhum al-mu'minun wa aktharuhum al-fasiqun — Among them believers but most fasiqun defiantly disobedient — as earlier among them trustworthy and untrustworthy.\n\nThis verse after white faces mercy shows path: best nation not by claim exclusive Paradise (2:111) but by serving humanity enjoining right.\n\nKhayr Ummah produced for humanity — humanity includes non-Muslims — you serve them by inviting good.\n\nIf enjoining/forbidding/belief stops, bestness claim stops — as earlier preference removed from wrongdoers (2:124 covenant not include wrongdoers).\n\nNext discusses harm People Book can do.",
  "109": "They will never harm you except little annoyance — if they fight you they will turn backs then not helped. Lan yadurrukum illa adha — They will never harm you except adha — little annoyance — hurtful words, mockery, brief.\n\nWa in yuqatilukum yuwallukum al-adbar — If fight you, turn backs — flee — thumma la yunsarun — then not helped — no divine help because wrongdoers.\n\nEarlier thought conspiracies morning evening cause return (72), but only adha — not root harm if holding rope.\n\nHistorical: Jewish tribes attempted fighting, turned backs, expelled.\n\nFor believers fearing conspiracy, comfort: harm limited annoyance if hold rope fear as should.\n\nNext describes disgrace struck upon them.",
  "110": "Disgrace struck upon them wherever found unless with rope from Allah and rope from people — they incurred wrath from Allah and poverty struck — because they disbelieved in signs Allah and killed prophets unjustly — that because they disobeyed and transgressed.\n\nDuribat alayhim adh-dhillah — disgrace struck — wherever found — ill feeling humiliation history.\n\nIlla bi-hablin min Allah wa hablin min an-nas — unless with rope from Allah and rope from people — i.e., unless under covenant protection: rope from Allah — promise that some will be protected if repent? Or rope from people — treaty with Muslims or others granting security. Without such rope, disgrace.\n\nWa ba'u bi-ghadabin min Allah wa duribat alayhim al-maskanah — incurred wrath and poverty struck — misknah — neediness inner.\n\nDhalika bi-annahum kanu yakfuruna bi-ayatillah wa yaqtuluna al-anbiya bi-ghayri haqq — because disbelieved signs and killed prophets without right — referring earlier 21.\n\nDhalika bima asaw wa kanu ya'tadun — because disobeyed and transgressed — asaw ya'tadun — sin transgression.\n\nRope from Allah appears again — same root as hold rope Allah together (102). Only rope saves from disgrace.\n\nNext exception upright among People Book.",
  "111": "They are not all same — among People Book is upright community reciting verses Allah in night hours and they prostrate.\n\nLaysu sawa'an — not all same — justice — as earlier some trustworthy with qintar some betray dinar (75). Among People Book upright ummah — qaimah — standing reciting — yatluna ayat Allah ana al-layl — reciting verses Allah in night hours, prostrating.\n\nThis likely refers to Abdullah ibn Salam and those who entered Islam, or Christians who remained sincere night worship before Quran, or generally believers among People Book who truly followed.\n\nThey recite ana al-layl — hours night — same time mustaghfirin bil-ashar seeking forgiveness before dawn (17). Devotion night praised.\n\nWa hum yasjudun — prostrate — action.\n\nQuran does not blanket condemn — distinguishes — as earlier not all same.\n\nThese community will be described believing etc.\n\nModel for Muslim night recitation — standing reading — as Maryam in mihrab provision.\n\nNext qualities of that upright community.",
  "112": "They believe in Allah and Last Day, enjoin right and forbid wrong, race in good deeds — they are among righteous. Yu'minuna billahi wal-yawmi al-akhir wa ya'muruna bil-ma'ruf wa yanhawna an al-munkar wa yusari'una fil-khayrat — Believe Allah Last Day enjoin right forbid wrong race good deeds — same definition best nation (108) and invitation (103). So upright among People Book share same qualities best nation — racing — yusari'una — sprint.\n\nWa ula'ika min as-salihin — among righteous — salihin — as earlier Yahya, Isa, Maryam among salihin.\n\nRacing good deeds includes spending beloved (91) night recitation, dawn istighfar.\n\nThus righteousness not label but action.\n\nNext nothing good lost.",
  "113": "And whatever good they do will never be unacknowledged — Allah is Knowing of mindful. Wa ma yaf'alu min khayrin fa-lan yukfaruh — Whatever good they do will never be denied — yukfar — from kufr meaning cover — will not be covered — will be recognized.\n\nWallahu Alimun bil-muttaqin — Allah Knowing of mindful — muttaqin — same as best provision taqwa.\n\nGood deeds of upright among People Book not wasted despite majority fasiq; individually counted.\n\nSame principle: whatever good you spend Allah knows it (92).\n\nEncouragement minority doing right within large corrupt community — good not unacknowledged.\n\nNext wealth children not avail disbelievers.",
  "114": "Indeed those who disbelieved — neither wealth nor children will avail them against Allah at all — they are companions of Fire forever. Same as earlier (10) and similar 116 — Inna alladhina kafaru lan tughniya anhum amwaluhum wa la awladuhum minAllahi shay'an — wealth children will not avail.\n\nWa ula'ika Ashab an-Nar hum fiha khalidun — companions Fire forever — khalidun — abiding, as earlier fuel Fire (10) and recompense curse abiding (87).\n\nRepetition third time in this surah alone: 10, 114, 116 — to hammer love of beautified desires — women, children, heaped gold silver, horses, cattle, tilth (14) — will not avail if not coupled taqwa.\n\nAfter describing upright community among People Book whose good never unacknowledged (113), Allah Knowing of mindful, contrast: disbelievers wealth not avail.\n\nThis framing teaches: good of mindful preserved, wealth of disbeliever not avail.\n\nEconomy reminder: what you spend from beloved (91) for Allah counted; what you hoard of beautified for self not avail.\n\nNext example spending disbelievers like wind frost.\n\nFor modern who accumulates heaps thinking security, verse says lan tughniya — will not enrich, not avail.\n\nAnd companionship Fire forever vs companionship mercy (106) — white faces in mercy.",
  "115": "Example of what they spend in this worldly life is like wind containing frost that struck tilth of people who wronged themselves and destroyed it — Allah did not wrong them but they wronged themselves.\n\nMathalu ma yunfiquna fi hadhihi al-hayat... — Example what they spend in worldly life — disbelievers spending to show off, to block path, etc — like wind frost — rih fiha sirr — cold freezing wind that struck harth — tilth — field of people who wronged themselves — drought?\n\nAllah did not wrong them but they wronged themselves — as earlier (2:57) they wronged selves not Allah.\n\nSpending without faith like farming after wronging self then wind destroys — no harvest.\n\nEarlier gardens parables for believers yield double; here disbeliever spending yields destruction.\n\nConnects to provision taqwa best provision — spending without taqwa waste.\n\nWarns believer also spending to be seen riya' like this wind.\n\nNext not take inner circle from outside.",
  "116": "O you who believe, do not take as inner circle those outside yourselves — they will not spare you any ruin — they wish what distresses you — hatred appeared from mouths — what chests conceal greater — We made clear signs if you use reason.\n\nYa ayyuha alladhina amanu la tattakhidhu bitanatan min dunikum — Do not take inner circle — bitanah — intimate confidant lining garment — from outside yourselves — those outside — disbelievers, hypocrites, those who wish harm.\n\nLa ya'lunakum khabala — They will not spare you any ruin — spare no effort to cause khabal — ruin, confusion.\n\nWaddu ma anittum — Wish what distresses you — anittum — hardship.\n\nQad badat al-baghda'u min afwahihim wa ma tukhfi suduruhum akbar — Hatred appeared from mouths, what chests conceal greater — slip of tongue reveals, deeper hatred bigger.\n\nQad bayyanna lakum al-ayat in kuntum ta'qilun — Made clear signs if use reason — ya'qilun.\n\nSimilar to earlier not take disbelievers as awliya instead of believers (28) and not take bitanah outside. Inner alliance matters.\n\nHistorical: hypocrites in Madinah leaking secrets to Jews.\n\nFor today: choosing advisors, close circle: does he spare effort ruin you? Wish distress? Hatred appears mouths? What hearts conceal greater? Reason sign.\n\nNext describes you love them they not love you.",
  "117": "Here you are — you love them but they do not love you — you believe in all the Book while they do not believe — when meet you say we believe but when alone bite fingertips from rage — Say die in your rage — Allah Knowing what is in chests.\n\nHa antum ula'i tuhibbunahum wa la yuhibbunakum — You love them but they not love you — believers naturally want good for all, love guidance, but they not love you.\n\nTu'minuna bil-kitabi kullih — you believe in all the Book — all revelations including Torah Gospel before — they don't believe in your Book — asymmetry.\n\nWa idha laqukum qalu amanna wa idha khalaw addu alaykum al-anamila min al-ghayz — When meet say we believe but alone bite fingertips from rage — ghayz — intense anger seeing unity.\n\nQul mutu bi-ghayzikum — Say die in rage — command contempt for rage, its fire consumes owner.\n\nInnAllaha Alimun bi-dhati as-sudur — Knowing what is in chests — same as earlier conceal reveal knows (29). Knows biting rage hidden.\n\nThis verse personalizes bitanah warning: love unreciprocated, belief inclusive vs exclusive, rage biting.\n\nNext whether good touches you grieves them etc.",
  "118": "If good touches you it grieves them, and if harm afflicts you they rejoice — but if you are patient and mindful their plot will not harm you at all — Allah encompassing what they do.\n\nIn tamsaskum hasanatun tasu'hum — If goodness — victory, provision, unity — touches you it grieves them — tasu'hum — makes them sad.\n\nWa in tusibkum sayyi'atun yafrahu biha — If evil — defeat, loss — afflicts they rejoice.\n\nWa in tasbiru wa tattaqu la yadurrukum kayduhum shay'an — But if patient and mindful plot will not harm at all — sabr taqwa again shield.\n\nInnAllaha bima ya'maluna muhit — Allah encompassing what they do — muhit — surrounds, as earlier (2:19) Allah encompasses disbelievers. So plot within His encompass; cannot escape.\n\nThis prepares for Uhud story: good at Badr grieved them, harm at Uhud rejoiced, need sabr taqwa for plot not harm.\n\nLinks to earlier sabr taqwa prevents harm (3:120? Actually 3:120?) Yes.\n\nSoon Uhud example patience tested.\n\nNext morning you went to place believers for battle.",
  "119": "And when you left in morning from your family to place believers in positions for battle — Allah Hearing, Knowing — and two groups among you thought of failing — Allah was their Guardian — in Allah believers put trust.\n\nWa idh ghadawta min ahlika tubawwi'u al-mu'minina maqa'ida lil-qital — Morning you left family to place believers positions battle — ghadawta — early morning — tubawwi'u — placing, arranging ranks. This is Uhud — Prophet left morning Madinah arranged army.\n\nWallahu Sami'un Alim — Hearing Knowing — heard consultation, knows inner thoughts.\n\nIdh hammat ta'ifatani minkum an tafshala — Two groups among you thought failing — cowardice — Bani Salamah and Harithah slipped due whisper Satan — wa Allahu Waliyyuhuma — Allah their Guardian — protected from actually failing, brought back.\n\nWa ala Allahi falyatawakkali al-mu'minun — In Allah believers put trust — tawakkul — after arranging positions, trust.\n\nSecond group failure thought shows even sincere can waver, but Allah guardians.\n\nThis begins Uhud detailed narrative — lesson planning plus tawakkul plus Allah hearing knowing inner whisper.\n\nNext recalls Badr help while weak.",
  "120": "Allah had already helped you at Badr while you were weak — so be mindful of Allah so you may be grateful.\n\nWa laqad nasarakum Allahu bi-Badrin wa antum adhillah — Helped at Badr while weak — adhillah — few, poorly equipped — 313 vs 1000 — as earlier sign two groups (13). Help came with patience.\n\nFattaqu Allaha la'allakum tashkurun — Be mindful so you may be grateful — taqwa leads shukr.\n\nBadr victory not due numbers but taqwa shukr; Uhud lesson: when taqwa weakened dispute, defeat came.\n\nShukr tied to previous verse remember favour when enemies and He joined hearts — brotherhood favour.\n\nBadr reminder before detailing Uhud slip.\n\nNext angels three thousand.",
  "121": "When you said to believers, Will it not be enough that your Lord supports you with three thousand angels sent down? Indeed if you are patient and mindful and they come upon you suddenly, your Lord will support with five thousand angels marked.\n\nIdh taqulu lil-mu'minina a-lan yakfiyakum an yumiddakum Rabbukum bi-thalathati alafin — Will it not enough Lord supports with three thousand angels sent? To comfort before battle.\n\nConditions: if patient mindful — as earlier condition if you are patient mindful plot no harm — and they come upon you suddenly immediate, Lord support with five thousand marked — musawwamin — marked horses.\n\nAngels support at Badr and Uhud? At Badr angels came; at Uhud because archers disobeyed condition patience not kept fully, support withheld? Some say.\n\nKey: angelic help conditional on sabr taqwa.\n\nVictory not angels themselves but good tidings to reassure hearts.\n\nNext verse: victory only from Allah.",
  "122": "And Allah made it only as good tidings for you and to reassure your hearts — victory is only from Allah, Mighty, All-Wise.\n\nWa ma ja'alahu Allahu illa bushra lakum wa li-tatma'inna qulubukum — Made it only as bushra — good tidings for you and reassure hearts — litatma'inna — tranquility as earlier Sakina in Tabut (2:248).\n\nWa ma an-nasru illa min indi Allahi al-Azizi al-Hakim — Victory only from Allah Mighty Wise — not angels independent, not numbers — only from Him.\n\nAziz Hakim — Mighty Wise — Mighty to give victory despite weakness, Wise to give it when conditions sabr taqwa met, to withhold wisdom to purify.\n\nReassurance after fear of failing two groups, fear of not enough angels — victory source single: Allah.\n\nFor us: seeking help from means — money, influence — without Allah, not victory. Means are bushra to reassure hearts but victory from Him alone.\n\nThus lessons Uhud still not about military strategy only but tawhid tawakkul.\n\nNext to cut off disbelievers.",
  "123": "It is to cut off a portion of disbelievers or suppress them so they turn back disappointed. Li-yaqta'a tarafan min alladhina kafaru aw yakbitahum fa-yanqalibu kha'ibin — Purpose of help — sending angels, reassuring hearts, victory only from Allah Mighty Wise — to cut off portion disbelievers — taraf — edge, leaders — or suppress — yakbit — disgrace — so turn back disappointed — kha'ibin.\n\nAt Badr edge cut — leaders like Abu Jahl killed; at Uhud though Muslims wounded, Quraysh's ultimate goal to wipe Islam failed, they turned back disappointed not achieving eradication.\n\nYakbit — suppress — same root as disgrace struck (110).\n\nFanqalibu kha'ibin — turn back failed — as earlier those who plot morning-evening wishing you return hoped you return failed, they turn back failed.\n\nDivine help cuts off aggression so it does not grow.\n\nFrom believer perspective, even wound at Uhud contributed to cutting off — because disbelievers exposed excess, hypocrites exposed.\n\nNext verse you have no say matter — up to Allah turn mercy or punish.",
  "124": "You have no say in matter — it is up to Allah to turn to them in mercy or punish them — they are wrongdoers. Laysa laka min al-amri shay'un — You have no say in matter — Prophet told — authority belongs Allah.\n\nAw yatuba alayhim aw yu'adhdhibahum fa-innahum zalimun — He may turn to them mercy or punish, they wrongdoers.\n\nRevealed when Prophet prayed against some Quraysh leaders who wounded him at Uhud, saying how can people succeed who wounded Prophet? Allah says say not yours.\n\nLesson: calling to Allah even against those who harmed, not personal vengeance; guidance belongs Allah. Some of those same leaders later became Muslims like Khalid ibn Walid.\n\nAfter Uhud injury Prophet bloodied, this instruction shows prophetic character restraint.\n\nNext to Allah belongs heavens earth forgives whom wills punishes whom wills.",
  "125": "To Allah belongs whatever in heavens and whatever on earth — He forgives whom He wills and punishes whom He wills — Allah is Forgiving, Merciful. Wa lillahi ma fis-samawati wa ma fil-ard yaghfiru liman yasha wa yu'adhdhibu man yasha — To Allah belongs heavens earth — He forgives whom wills punishes whom wills — same as near end Baqarah (2:284) He forgives whom wills punishes whom wills.\n\nWallahu Ghafur Rahim — Forgiving Merciful — mercy dominates even after battle.\n\nForgives whom wills includes those who fought you then later believe; punishes whom wills includes persistent wrongdoers.\n\nProperty heavens earth indicates authority to forgive punish.\n\nFollowing forgiveness mercy, next prohibition riba.",
  "126": "O you who believe, do not consume riba multiplied many times — fear Allah so you may be successful. Ya ayyuha alladhina amanu la ta'kulu ar-riba ad'afan muda'afah — Do not consume riba multiplied many times — ad'af muda'afah — doubled multiplied — riba of Jahiliyyah where debt doubled each time not paid.\n\nWattaqu Allaha la'allakum tuflihun — Fear Allah so you may be successful — falah — as earlier best nation success tied to enjoining right.\n\nRiba consumption warned earlier sternly (2:275 war with Allah). Here within Uhud context: craving increase wealth via riba leads to cowardice? Some link: army left for worldly eagerness — archers left for spoils similar to riba greed multiplication.\n\nGuarding Fire next.",
  "127": "Guard yourselves against Fire prepared for disbelievers. Wattaqu an-nara allati u'iddat lil-kafirin — Guard against Fire prepared for disbelievers — same as 2:24 — fuel people stones prepared for disbelievers — and here after riba prohibition (126) multiplied many times.\n\nWattaqu — fear — same root taqwa best provision, haqqa tuqatih, rope.\n\nFire prepared — u'iddat — already exists ready, as earlier Paradise prepared for mindful (129). Two prepared abodes: prepared for disbelievers vs prepared for muttaqin.\n\nRiba leads to Fire prepared for disbelievers though prohibition addressed to believers — stern: consuming riba behaviour disbelievers can drag into their prepared abode if persists (as 2:275 war).\n\nGuarding Fire via leaving riba, holding rope, spending ease hardship, restraining anger, pardoning, remembering seeking forgiveness not persisting.\n\nAfter guarding Fire, next obey Allah and Messenger so mercy.\n\nLink to earlier guard yourselves Day no soul avail another (2:48) — guard Fire by taqwa.\n\nPractical: every riba transaction seems small multiplication but destination is prepared Fire.\n\nSo verse after riba not abstract; immediate consequence.",
  "128": "Obey Allah and the Messenger that you may be shown mercy. Wa ati'u Allaha war-Rasula la'allakum turhamun — Obey Allah and Messenger so you may be shown mercy — turhamun — mercy.\n\nObedience includes not consuming riba, not taking bitanah outside, not following plot morning evening, obeying archers order etc.\n\nLa'allakum turhamun — so may be shown mercy — mercy earlier asked grant mercy from Yourself (8), ridwan better than gardens (15), mercy of Allah white faces in mercy forever (106).\n\nMercy not automatic; linked obedience.\n\nAfter Uhud where obedience to Messenger command (archers stay at mountain) broken leading loss, command to obey still central.\n\nIt also precedes race to forgiveness and Paradise vast prepared for mindful (129). Mercy leads to forgiveness race.\n\nSo sequence: guard Fire prepared for disbelievers (127) — obey Allah Messenger so mercy (128) — hasten forgiveness Paradise prepared for mindful (129). Two prepared abodes, path to mercy abode via obedience.\n\nNext hasten forgiveness.\n\nFor believer struggling with riba debt, obedience path to mercy.",
  "129": "And hasten to forgiveness from Lord and Garden vast as heavens and earth — prepared for mindful. Wa sari'u ila maghfiratin min Rabbikum... Race to forgiveness and Garden width heavens earth prepared for muttaqin.\n\nSari'u — hasten — race — similar to race to good deeds (2:148) and race to forgiveness. Speed toward forgiveness, not toward riba multiplication.\n\nGarden vast heavens earth — width as vast — as earlier Paradise for muttaqin (15) gardens under rivers.\n\nU'iddat lil-muttaqin — prepared for mindful — opposite Fire prepared for disbelievers (127). Choice: two prepared abodes.\n\nWho are muttaqin? Next verses describe.\n\nFor Uhud injured, hastening forgiveness better than grieving loss.\n\nParadise vastness also indicates not narrow tribal paradise few days — vast for all mindful.\n\nNext description muttaqin.",
  "130": "Those who spend in ease and hardship, restrain anger, pardon people — Allah loves doers of good. Alladhina yunfiquna fis-sarra'i wa-ddarra'i — spend prosperity and adversity — sara' ease darra' hardship — spending despite love beloved (92) both conditions — not only when easy — generous even hardship.\n\nWal-kazimina al-ghayza — restrain anger — kazm — holding, swallowing — ghayz same as biting fingertips rage (117) — muttaqin swallow anger.\n\nWal-afina an an-nas — pardon people — not only swallow but pardon.\n\nWallahu yuhibbu al-muhsinin — Allah loves doers good — muhsinin — ihsan.\n\nThis is portrait muttaqin prepared Garden: spending, restraining anger, pardoning.\n\nAt Uhud anger was present after defeat, desire revenge; verse prescribes restraint pardon.\n\nAfter spending in ease hardship links to earlier spending in Allah path grain (2:261) — best provision taqwa.\n\nNext upon committing evil deed remember Allah seek forgiveness.",
  "131": "And those who when they commit immorality or wrong themselves — remember Allah and seek forgiveness for their sins — and who can forgive sins except Allah — and do not persist knowingly.\n\nWalladhina idha fa'alu fahishatan aw zalamu anfusahum dhakaru Allaha fastaghfaru li-dhunubihim — Those when commit fahishah — immorality — or wrong selves — lesser sins — remember Allah and seek forgiveness.\n\nWa man yaghfiru adh-dhunuba illa Allah — Who forgives sins except Allah — rhetorical none.\n\nWa lam yusirru ala ma fa'alu wa hum ya'lamun — And do not persist knowingly — not insist while knowing.\n\nThis continues muttaqin: not perfect sinless — they commit — but remember, seek forgiveness, not persist knowingly.\n\nEarlier after sad, devotion — spending, restraining anger, pardoning — now they themselves sin and respond with dhikr and istighfar, not arrogance taking sin as in sin (2:206).\n\nFahishah includes adultery, riba consumption, etc. Wrong selves includes neglect.\n\nRemembering Allah dhakaru — same as remember Allah standing sitting lying (191).\n\nSins forgiven by none except Allah — so direction of istighfar solely to Him, not intermediaries.\n\nNot persist knowingly — israr — insisting while knowing haram — differs from slip then repent. Istighfar must accompany leaving.\n\nThis completes circle taqwa: fall, remember, ask, not persist.\n\nNext reward forgiveness Gardens.",
  "132": "Those — their reward is forgiveness from Lord and Gardens beneath rivers flowing forever — excellent reward for workers.\n\nUla'ika jaza'uhum maghfiratun min Rabbihim wa jannatun... — Reward forgiveness from Lord and Gardens rivers flow — staying forever — khalidina fiha.\n\nWa ni'ma ajru al-amilin — Excellent reward for workers — for those who work — not wishers.\n\nForgiveness first then Gardens — because entry Paradise depends forgiveness more than deeds — as earlier those who say Our Lord we believed so forgive (16).\n\nAmilin — workers — includes patience, spending hardship, restraining anger, pardoning, remembering seeking forgiveness not persisting — active.\n\nEarlier best nation enjoin right forbid wrong believe (108), best provision taqwa (2:197), now excellent reward workers.\n\nFor Uhud companions who committed mistake archer disobedience, reminder: if remember seek forgiveness not persist, reward still forgiveness Gardens.\n\nLink to hasten forgiveness (129) — those hastening get this.\n\nNext travel see fate deniers.",
  "133": "There have been patterns before you — travel through earth and see how was end of deniers. Qad khalat min qablikum sunan fa-siru fil-ardi fanzuru kayfa kana aqibatu al-mukadhdhibin — Patterns — sunan — Allah's ways dealing with nations who deny — have passed before you — like Pharaoh, Ad. Travel through earth see end deniers — ruins, stories.\n\nFa-siru — travel — not only physical travel to ruins but travel reflection stories Quran recounts (Pharaoh, Talut, etc).\n\nEnd deniers visible: disgrace struck upon them (110), abiding Fire, if plot not harm patient mindful (118) but deniers end ruined.\n\nAfter Uhud where some thought victory lost, reminder sunan: days alternate victory defeat among people (140) to distinguish believers.\n\nTravel seeing fate gives perspective beyond immediate defeat.\n\nNext this is clear statement.",
  "134": "This is clear statement to humanity — guidance and admonition for mindful. Hadha bayanu lin-nas wa huda wa maw'izatun lil-muttaqin — This — Quran, or this passage about sunan and reward — is bayan — clear statement — to humanity — lin-nas — guidance — huda — and admonition — maw'izah — for muttaqin.\n\nBayan for all, but huda maw'izah specifically muttaqin because they benefit, as earlier Book guidance for muttaqin (2:2) and Furqan made clear for people sure faith (2:118).\n\nClear statement includes previous patterns, description muttaqin, warning not consume riba etc.\n\nSo after commands fear as should be feared hold rope hasten forgiveness, this passage summarised as bayan — exposition.\n\nFor mindful, it becomes huda.\n\nNext do not falter grieve you will have upper hand if believers.",
  "135": "Do not weaken and do not grieve — you will be uppermost if you are true believers. Wa la tahinu wa la tahzanu wa antum al-a'lawna in kuntum mu'minina — Do not weaken — wahin — lose heart — wa la tahzanu — grieve — after Uhud wounds — antum al-a'lawna — you uppermost — if true believers.\n\nUppermost not necessarily immediate battle win but final predominance deen, rank with Allah.\n\nCondition: in kuntum mu'minina — if true believers — belief includes patience, spending hardship, restraint anger, remembering seeking forgiveness — qualities just listed.\n\nWeakening grief natural after injury death of 70 companions including Hamza. Quran acknowledges grief but commands not let consume.\n\nEarlier best nation (108) but uppermost conditional belief true.\n\nThis verse was soothing for survivors bleeding.\n\nFor today personal defeat — business loss, family dispute — same: do not weaken grieve, you uppermost if believers.\n\nNext if you suffered injury they suffered similarly.",
  "136": "If wound touches you, wound like it touched other people — We alternate days among people — so Allah may know those who believed and take from you martyrs — Allah does not like wrongdoers.\n\nIn yamsaskum qarhun fa-qad massa al-qawma qarhun mithluh — If wound injury touches you, similar touched other people — at Badr they suffered wounds; at Uhud you suffered. Balance.\n\nWa tilka al-ayyamu nudaawiluha bayna an-nas — We alternate days among people — yaum victory, yaum defeat — Sunna alternating — wisdom.\n\nLi-ya'lama Allahu alladhina amanu wa yattakhidha minkum shuhada — So Allah may know — i.e., make known, distinguish — those who believed and take from you martyrs — martyrs — shuhada — witnesses over peoples, also killed in path.\n\nWallahu la yuhibbu az-zalimin — Allah not love wrongdoers — wrongdoers here may include archers disobeyed order or hypocrites.\n\nAlternation not random: to test, to select martyrs — honour not punishment — Hamza martyrdom raised rank.\n\nMartyrs taken from you — meaning death in His path honour.\n\nNext and to purify believers destroy disbelievers.\n\nIf you have suffered, others similar — normalizes.\n\nNext entering Paradise without proving.",
  "137": "And to purify believers and wipe out disbelievers. Wa li-yumahhisa Allahu alladhina amanu wa yamhaqa al-kafirin — Purpose alternating days: purify believers — yumahhis — cleanse sins via trial as fire purifies gold — and wipe out — yamhaq — disbelievers — as earlier Allah destroys riba and grows charities (2:276) — yamhaq.\n\nPurification via wounds forgiveness: sins forgiven through suffering.\n\nWipe out disbelievers via their joy at harm leading excess until destroyed.\n\nTwo opposite effects same event: same battle purifies believer, destroys disbeliever via arrogance.\n\nFor us trials serve purification.\n\nNext do you think enter Paradise without Allah proving.",
  "138": "Or do you think you will enter Paradise without Allah making evident those who strove among you and making evident the patient? Am hasibtum an tadkhulu al-jannata wa lamma ya'lami Allahu alladhina jahadu minkum wa ya'lama as-sabirin — Think enter Paradise without Allah proving those who strove and patient?\n\nHasibtum — thought — as earlier (2:214) think enter Paradise without trials as those before? Same theme. Paradise not cheap.\n\nAlladhina jahadu — those who strove — jihad includes battle, but also striving against anger, spending hardship.\n\nAs-sabirin — patient — as earlier patient mindful plot not harm.\n\nAllah already knows, but making evident — ya'lami — to manifest knowledge in reality to creation.\n\nSo Uhud was revealing who strives, who patient.\n\nFor us: desire Paradise requires striving patient, not just claim love Allah.\n\nNext you wished for martyrdom before encountering.",
  "139": "You had certainly wished for death before you encountered it — now you saw it with own eyes. Wa laqad kuntum tamannawna al-mawta min qabli an talqawhu fa-qad ra'aytumuhu wa antum tanzurun — You wished death — martyrdom — before meeting — many companions before Uhud wished martyrdom like at Badr who missed Badr said if granted battle would show truth. Now you saw it with eyes — ra'aytumuhu wa antum tanzurun — seeing battlefield death face to face.\n\nTammanni before differs from reality — 70 dead, blood.\n\nReminder to be careful wishing test: wishing martyrdom good, but must be ready for patience when death appears not romantic.\n\nIt also comforts those who wished and then fled? Some archers wished then weakened. Seeing reveals truth.\n\nNext Prophet is only messenger messengers passed before.",
  "140": "Muhammad is not but a messenger — messengers passed before him — if he dies or is killed will you turn back on heels? Whoever turns back does not harm Allah at all — Allah will reward grateful.\n\nWa ma Muhammadun illa rasulun qad khalat min qablihi ar-rusul — Muhammad not but messenger, messengers passed before — Ibrahim, Nuh, Musa, Isa raised — all died or raised — mortality of messengers sunnah.\n\nAfa-in mata aw qutila inqalabtum ala a'qabikum — If dies or killed will you turn back on heels? At Uhud rumor spread Prophet killed, some threw weapons saying if died religion ended.\n\nInqalab ala a'qab — turn back heels — apostasy or giving up deen.\n\nWa man yanqalib... fa-lan yadurra Allaha shay'an — Whoever turns back does not harm Allah at all — Allah Ghani (96) free need.\n\nWa sa-yajzi Allahu ash-shakirin — Allah will reward grateful — shakirin — those who stay grateful after calamity, not turn back.\n\nThis verse pivotal: Islam not tied to person even greatest person; tied to Hayy Qayyum ever-living. Messenger delivers then goes; message remains.\n\nFor Abu Bakr after Prophet actual death, recited this verse to calm Umar and ummah.\n\nLesson: love Messenger by following message, not by making Islam depend on his physical presence.\n\nNext no soul dies without Allah Will.",
  "141": "No soul dies except by Allah's permission at written term — whoever desires worldly gain We give it to him, and whoever desires Hereafter gain We give it to him — and We will reward grateful.\n\nWa ma kana li-nafsin an tamuta illa bi-idhni Allahi kitaban mu'ajjalan — No soul dies except by permission Allah at written term — ajal mu'ajjal — fixed book time — not random. Age, place, manner written.\n\nIf no soul dies except permission, then fearing death on battlefield irrational; death comes at written term regardless staying home — same as earlier those fled homes thousands fearing death said die then gave life (2:243).\n\nWa man yurid thawaba ad-dunya nu'tihi minha — Who desires worldly gain give it — sara' adversity spending etc worldly gain limited — same as one who says give us in world has no share hereafter (2:200).\n\nWa man yurid thawaba al-akhirah nu'tihi — Who desires hereafter gain give — both provided but proportion?\n\nWa sa-najzi ash-shakirin — Reward grateful — same ending as previous.\n\nFor archers who left hill for spoils worldly gain — they desired world, got world but lost.\n\nFor believer, intention directs outcome — want dunya get dunya, want akhira reward get.\n\nNext many devotees fought alongside prophets never faltered.",
  "142": "How many prophets fought and along with them many devoted men — they never faltered for what afflicted them in Allah's path, nor weakened, nor gave in — Allah loves the patient.\n\nWa ka-a min nabiyyin qatala ma'ahu ribbiyuna kathir — How many prophets fought accompanied many devoted men — ribbiyyun — learned pious devotees — kathir — many.\n\nFa-ma wahanu lima asabahum fi sabili Allah wa ma da'ufu wa mastakanu — They never faltered for what afflicted them in Allah's path, nor weakened, nor gave in — three verbs: wahanu — lose heart, da'ufu — become weak physically, istakanu — give in surrender humbly to enemy.\n\nWallahu yuhibbu as-sabirin — Allah loves patient — same as loves doers good.\n\nThese devoted men example for Uhud companions: many prophets faced similar loss but devotees stayed.\n\nComparison: at Uhud some faltered after affliction — this verse gives model of not faltering.\n\nFor us: when project da'wah faces setback, prophetic companions did not falter weaken give in — keep.\n\nNext their only word dua forgiving excess firm steps victory.",
  "143": "They said nothing but — Our Lord forgive us our sins and excess in our affair, make firm our feet, and grant victory over disbelieving people.\n\nWa ma kana qawlahum illa an qalu Rabbanaghfir lana dhunubana wa israfana fi amrina wa thabbit aqdamana wansurna ala al-qawmi al-kafirin — Their only word facing affliction was dua — not blame prophet, not blame each other, not say why.\n\nForgive sins and excess in affair — israfana — excess — even righteous see excess — restrain.\n\nThabbit aqdamana — make firm feet — as earlier Dua Talut army pour patience make firm steps (2:250). Same phrase.\n\nWansurna ala qawmi kafirin — grant victory over disbelievers — similar Dua at Badr.\n\nThis dua after describes not faltering: they combined not faltering outward with seeking forgiveness inward.\n\nLessons Uhud: archers after partial victory disputed about command (152) about booty, weakened — instead should have said this dua.\n\nFor us today after failure, not blame analysis only but forgiveness firmness victory dua.\n\nNext Allah gave reward world excellent reward hereafter.",
  "144": "So Allah gave them reward of world and excellent reward of Hereafter — Allah loves doers of good. Fa-atahumu Allahu thawaba ad-dunya wa husna thawabi al-akhirah — So Allah gave them reward world — victory, honour, provision — and excellent reward hereafter — Paradise.\n\nWallahu yuhibbu al-muhsinin — Loves doers good — muhsinin — as earlier loves patient, loves doers good (134). Ihsan includes du'a forgiveness firmness seeking victory not personal.\n\nAfter Uhud setback, reminder that those who follow pattern — no faltering, du'a forgiveness, firmness — get both rewards.\n\nFor companions who slipped, door still open if follow same.\n\nNext if yield to disbelievers dragged back losers.",
  "145": "O you who believe, if you obey those who disbelieved they will turn you back on heels and you will become losers. Ya ayyuha alladhina amanu in tuti'u alladhina kafaru yaruddukum ala a'qabikum fa-tanqalibu khasirin — If obey disbelievers — follow advice, plot, desire — they will turn you back on heels after belief and become losers — khasirin — same as losers earlier who traded belief disbelief and wish you return (69, 99).\n\nObedience here includes taking bitanah outside (118) loving them though they not love you, listening morning evening plot.\n\nLoss not only battle but deen.\n\nNext but Allah your Guardian best Helper.",
  "146": "But Allah is your Guardian and He is best Helper. Bal Allahu Mawlakum wa Huwa khayru an-nasirin — But Allah your Mawla — Guardian, Protector, Ally — and best Helper — nasirin.\n\nIf obey disbelievers turn back losers, but if Allah Guardian best Helper, obedience to Him brings success.\n\nMawla same root as Wali — earlier Allah Guardian believers brings darkness light (2:257).\n\nBest Helper — khayru an-nasirin — not just helper but best. So no need other awliya.\n\nThis verse after warning obeying disbelievers leads loss — reminder true Waliyy.\n\nAfter defeat, need to know true Protector still Allah, not vanished.\n\nNext cast horror hearts disbelievers associating.",
  "147": "We will cast horror into hearts of disbelievers because they associated with Allah what He gave no authority for — refuge Fire — evil lodging wrongdoers.\n\nSa-nulqi fi qulubi alladhina kafaru ar-ru'ba bima ashraku billahi ma lam yunazzil bihi sultanan — We will cast terror — ru'b — into hearts disbelievers because they associated partners with Allah what He gave no authority.\n\nWa ma'wahum an-nar wa bi'sa mathwa az-zalimin — Refuge Fire evil lodging wrongdoers.\n\nAt Uhud initially Muslims fled horror into disbelievers? Actually after initial Muslim setback, later Allah cast terror into Quraysh so they left not finishing.\n\nRoot: shirk brings inner horror — though seem powerful, hearts unstable — as earlier they saw double number (13) and slipped. Tawhid brings tranquility — Sakina.\n\nMathwa — lodging — same as mihad evil resting place (12).\n\nSo obedience to disbelievers brings loss, but Allah best Helper will cast horror into their hearts — no need take them as bitanah.\n\nNext Allah fulfilled promise when swept them away.",
  "148": "And Allah had fulfilled His promise when you were sweeping them away by His permission — until when you faltered and disputed about order and disobeyed after He showed you what you love — He turned you from them to test you — He has pardoned you — Allah Possessor bounty for believers.\n\nWa laqad sadaqakum Allahu wa'dah — Allah fulfilled promise — at start Uhud you were sweeping away Quraysh — tahussunahum — cutting, sweeping — by His permission — idhnihi — victory from Him alone.\n\nHatta idha fashiltum wa tanaza'tum fil-amri wa asaytum min ba'di ma arakum ma tuhibbun — Until when you faltered and disputed about order and disobeyed after He showed you what you love — what you love — booty, victory. Archers disputed: we should go collect spoils? Leader said stay. Dispute, disobedience — after seeing love.\n\nSarafakum anhum li-yabtaliyakum — He turned you from them to test you — test.\n\nWa laqad afa ankum — He pardoned you — kept forgiveness after mercy.\n\nWallahu dhu fadlin ala al-mu'minin — Owner bounty for believers — fadl — includes pardon.\n\nLesson clear: promise fulfilled first phase, then faltering dispute disobedience after seeing what love caused turn. Test revealed.\n\nFor us: many victories near, then love of what we love — money, fame — causes dispute disobedience, turn.\n\nBut pardoned, possessor bounty.\n\nNext when you were running far away not looking while Messenger calling from behind.",
  "149": "When you were climbing far away not looking at anyone, while Messenger was calling you from behind — so He repaid you distress with distress so you would not grieve over what slipped nor what struck you — Allah is Aware of what you do.\n\nIdh tus'iduna wa la talwuna ala ahad war-Rasulu yad'ukum fi ukhraakum — You were climbing — tus'iduna — running uphill far away not looking at anyone — panic — while Messenger calling from behind — Prophet calling \"To me servants Allah! I am Messenger!\" — Companions running past.\n\nFa-athabakum ghamman bi-ghammin li-kay la tahzanu ala ma fatakum wa la ma asabakum — So He repaid you distress with distress — first distress — loss 70 brothers, rumour Prophet death, second distress — being called back ashamed — so you would not grieve over what slipped and what struck — purpose: larger distress made smaller seem small, training not to grieve over ghanimah slipped (booty) nor wound struck.\n\nWallahu Khabirun bima ta'malun — Allah Aware what you do — including running, calling, disobedience.\n\nImagery vivid: army running up mountain, Prophet behind calling, distress upon distress. Yet within it mercy — so you would not grieve... Allah teaches to reframe grief: what you lost less than what you still have, and second distress covers first.\n\nNext after distress He sent down serenity.",
  "150": "Then after distress He sent down security — drowsiness overcoming group of you, while other group — anxious for themselves — thought about Allah other than truth — thought of ignorance — saying, Is there anything for us in this matter? Say, matter all belongs to Allah — they conceal in chests what they not reveal saying If there was anything for us we would not have been killed here — Say if you had been in houses those destined to be killed would have gone forth to places they were to be slain — Allah may test what in your chests and purify what in hearts — Allah Knowing what is in chests.\n\nThumma anzala alaykum min ba'di al-ghammi amanatan nu'asan yaghsha ta'ifatan minkum — After distress He sent security drowsiness — nu'as — slumber overcoming group — those sincere believers like Abu Talha said sword fell from hand due sleep — serenity proof Allah with patient.\n\nWa ta'ifatun qad ahammat-hum anfusuhum yazunnuna billahi ghayra al-haqq zanna al-jahiliyyah — Other group anxious for themselves thought about Allah other than truth thought ignorance — thought Islam ended, promise false.\n\nYaquluna hal lana min al-amri min shay — Is there anything for us in this matter? Doubting share.\n\nQul inna al-amra kullahu lillah — Matter all belongs to Allah — same as dominion Owner (26).\n\nYukhfuna fi anfusihim ma la yubduna — Conceal in chests not reveal.\n\nLaw kana lana... ma qutilna ha-huna — If there was anything for us not killed here — blame.\n\nQul law kuntum fi buyutikum la-baraza alladhina kutiba alayhim al-qatlu ila madaji'ihim — Say if in houses those destined killed would have gone forth to places slain — ajal written permission earlier (141) — written term — no escape.\n\nLi-yabtaliya Allahu ma fi sudurikum wa li-yumahhisa ma fi qulubikum — Allah test what in chests purify what hearts — same as purify believers wipe disbelievers (137).\n\nWallahu Alimun bi-dhati as-sudur — Knowing what in chests — same as knows conceal reveal (29).\n\nVerse exposes two reactions distress: believers given serenity via drowsiness; anxious group thoughts ignorance.",
  "151": "The surah now declares a specific form of divine aid that will be granted against the enemy, linking their spiritual crime to their psychological punishment. “We will cast horror into the hearts of the disbelievers.\n\n” The word “horror” (ru‘b) is an intense, overwhelming fear that destabilizes the mind and paralyzes action. This was a miraculous phenomenon witnessed at several battles, where the disbelievers, despite their superior numbers and equipment, were seized by unexplained terror and fled. At Badr, the Muslims were few and poorly armed, yet the Quraysh were filled with dread. At Uhud, although the Muslims suffered losses, the Quraysh army, under Abu Sufyan, did not press their advantage to annihilate the remaining Muslims in Medina; instead, they withdrew. Many reports indicate that Allah cast such fear into their hearts that they decided to return to Mecca, fearing a counterattack.\n\nThe verse then explains the cause of this divine action: “for associating false gods with Allah—a practice He has never authorized. ” Their crime is shirk, the association of partners with Allah in worship, which is the ultimate injustice. Because they committed this atrocity without any divine sanction, Allah punished them with internal terror.\n\nThe verse then shifts to the ultimate punishment: “The Fire will be their home—what an evil place for the wrongdoers to stay!” The casting of horror in this world is a mere foretaste of the eternal terror and suffering that awaits them.\n\nThe phrase “what an evil place for the wrongdoers to stay” (bi’sa mathwa al-zalimin) emphasizes the wretchedness of their final abode. For the believers, this verse served as a powerful reassurance. The enemy that seemed so formidable was, in reality, spiritually and psychologically vulnerable. Their false gods could not protect them from the fear that Allah casts directly into their hearts. This knowledge emboldened the believers and diminished their own fear. For the contemporary believer, this verse teaches that the power of falsehood is inherently fragile. Those who oppose the truth may appear strong, but their hearts are often filled with insecurity and terror, even if they do not show it. The believer, armed with faith, has a serenity that the disbeliever cannot possess.\n\nThe verse also reinforces the gravity of shirk and its dire consequences in both worlds.",
  "152": "This verse is the heart of the Uhud narrative, providing a detailed analysis of why the battle turned from initial victory to painful loss. “Indeed, Allah fulfilled His promise to you when you initially swept them away by His Will.” The battle began exactly as promised. The Muslims, despite being smaller in number, were overwhelming the Quraysh. The enemy was fleeing, and the Muslims were collecting spoils. Allah’s promise of victory was true and was being fulfilled.\n\nThe verse then lists the human failures that reversed the situation: “then your courage weakened and you disputed about the command and disobeyed.” The weakening of courage (fashiltum) refers to the loss of resolve when some fighters saw the spoils and lost focus. The dispute (tanaza‘tum) was among the archers whom the Prophet had stationed on the hill with explicit orders not to leave their post under any circumstances. When they saw the spoils, most of them argued that they should join the collection, despite their leader Abdullah ibn Jubayr’s reminders. The disobedience (‘asaytum) was their actual abandonment of the post. This happened “after Allah had brought victory within your reach,” meaning the triumph was virtually in their hands. Then the verse diagnoses the underlying motives: “Some of you were after worldly gain while others desired a heavenly reward.” The division of intentions weakened the unity of action. Those who desired the spoils left their post; those who sought the Hereafter stayed or fought. The result: “He denied you victory over them as a test. ” The withdrawal of the initial victory was a trial, to teach the believers the consequences of disobedience and divided intentions.\n\nYet the verse does not end with condemnation: “yet He has pardoned you. And Allah is Gracious to the believers.” Despite the grave error, Allah’s mercy enveloped them. The defeat was not a total annihilation; it was a disciplinary lesson, and forgiveness was granted. This verse is a masterclass in divine education. It shows that success depends on obedience and unity of purpose. It also reveals the immense grace of Allah, who turns even failures into opportunities for growth and then pardons His servants.\n\nFor the believer, it is a timeless lesson in self-accountability. When setbacks occur, one must look at one’s own actions and intentions, correct them, and then seek Allah’s forgiveness, trusting in His graciousness.",
  "153": "The surah paints a vivid and painful picture of the chaos that ensued when the tide turned. “Remember when you were running far away in panic—not looking at anyone—while the Messenger was calling to you from behind!” The verb “running far away” (tus‘idun) suggests climbing and fleeing upward, scattered across the mountain slopes.\n\nThe phrase “not looking at anyone” (la talwuna ‘ala ahad) conveys the single-minded panic that erased all concern for comrades or the Prophet. Meanwhile, the Prophet Muhammad, with a small band of steadfast companions, was calling out, “To me, O servants of Allah! I am the Messenger of Allah!” He was trying to rally them, but the fleeing was so widespread that his voice was ignored or unheard by many. This moment exposed the depth of the human panic instinct when faith wavers.\n\nThe verse then states: “So Allah rewarded your disobedience with distress upon distress.” The “distress” (ghamm) refers to the grief, fear, and confusion that overwhelmed them.\n\nThe first distress was the defeat and the rumour of the Prophet’s death; the second distress was the realization of their own failure and the loss of the battle. This accumulation of distress was a direct consequence of their earlier disobedience.\n\nThe verse then offers a balm: “Now, do not grieve over the victory you were denied or the injury you suffered.” After the lesson is delivered, Allah consoles them. The lost victory and the physical and emotional injuries should not be a source of prolonged despair. The divine pedagogy is complete; what remains is to learn and move forward. “And Allah is All-Aware of what you do” reminds them that their inner state, their repentance, and their future efforts are all fully known to Allah.\n\nFor the believer, this verse is a stark reminder of the consequences of disobedience to the Messenger. It also shows the incredible mercy of Allah, who after describing their humiliating flight, tells them not to grieve. The past cannot be changed, but the future can be rebuilt.\n\nThe image of the Prophet calling to his fleeing companions is one of the most touching in the Quran, demonstrating his unwavering commitment to his ummah. It also serves as a call to every believer to heed the call of the Messenger in their own lives, not to flee from the responsibilities of faith when the battle—whether literal or metaphorical—becomes intense.",
  "154": "The verse describes the contrasting psychological states of two groups after the battle. “Then after distress, He sent down serenity in the form of drowsiness overcoming some of you.” The “some” were the sincere believers. After the extreme terror and exhaustion of the battle, Allah granted them a miraculous calmness manifesting as a light sleep or drowsiness (nu‘as). This was a sign of divine security (sakinah). In a state of fear, sleep normally flees, but the sincere were given this gift as a reassurance.\n\nIn contrast, “others were disturbed by evil thoughts about Allah—the thoughts of pre-Islamic ignorance.” These “others” were the hypocrites and those with weak faith. Their minds were filled with doubts about Allah’s promise, questioning whether the Prophet was truly a messenger, whether Allah had abandoned them, and whether the whole endeavor was a mistake. Their thought pattern was that of the pre-Islamic era (al-jahiliyyah), which lacked firm trust in divine decree. They asked, “Do we have a say in the matter?” This was a rhetorical question expressing their feeling that they had been dragged into a disastrous situation without any real control or consultation. The Prophet is instructed to answer: “All matters are destined by Allah.” Victory and defeat, life and death, all are under Allah’s complete control. Then the verse reveals their hidden whispers: “They conceal in their hearts what they do not reveal to you. They say to themselves, ‘If we had any say in the matter, none of us would have come to die here.’” These were the hypocrites who believed that if they had been in charge, they would have avoided the battle altogether and thus prevented the deaths. This reveals a total lack of faith in qadr. The Prophet is commanded to respond: “Even if you were to remain in your homes, those among you who were destined to be killed would have met the same fate.\n\n” This is the exact argument made earlier about death’s appointed time. The purpose of all this is explained: “Through this, Allah tests what is within you and purifies what is in your hearts. ” The trial at Uhud separated the sincere, who received serenity, from the hypocrites, who were exposed. And the sincere were also purified of their own inner impurities.\n\nThe verse ends, “And Allah knows best what is hidden in the heart.” For the believer, this verse is a profound study of the effects of faith and doubt under pressure. It teaches that true iman brings divine peace, even in the midst of catastrophe, while weak faith and hypocrisy breed confusion and blame. The believer learns to recognize the peace of faith as a sign, and to reject the doubts of jahiliyyah that question divine decree when things go wrong.",
  "155": "The verse addresses the painful reality of those believers who genuinely had faith but were overcome by panic and fled from the battlefield. “Indeed, those believers who fled on the day when the two armies met were made to slip by Satan because of their misdeeds.\n\n” The phrase “were made to slip” (istazallahum) indicates that Satan caused them to stumble and fall into the error of fleeing. However, the verse does not absolve them of responsibility; Satan was able to influence them “because of their misdeeds” (bima kasabu). Their prior sins or errors—such as disobeying the Prophet’s command, arguing over the spoils, or having mixed intentions—created a vulnerability that Satan exploited. This teaches that sins weaken the spiritual immune system, making a person susceptible to greater failures. The flight of these believers was not an act of outright disbelief or hypocrisy; it was a moment of weakness that they deeply regretted.\n\nThe verse then offers the balm of divine mercy: “But Allah has pardoned them. Surely Allah is All-Forgiving, Most Forbearing.\n\n” The word “pardoned” (‘afa) is a complete and gracious forgiveness, wiping away the sin and its consequences. The combination of the divine names “All-Forgiving” (Ghafur) and “Most Forbearing” (Halim) is significant. Ghafur indicates that Allah covers and erases the sin, while Halim indicates that He does not hasten punishment but gives respite and is gentle in His correction. The flight of these believers could have merited severe punishment, but Allah’s forbearance and forgiveness encompassed them. This verse was a source of immense relief for those companions, like Uthman ibn Affan and others, who had fled in the confusion and later felt overwhelming guilt. It taught the community that while sins have consequences, the door of repentance is always open, and Allah’s mercy is vast enough to cover even the grave error of fleeing from battle.\n\nFor the believer today, this verse is a powerful reminder that no matter how great the fall, if it is followed by sincere regret and amendment, Allah’s forgiveness is near. It also warns against the incremental danger of small misdeeds, which can pave the way for larger failures. The verse balances justice with mercy, showing that Satan’s role does not negate human accountability, but Allah’s forgiveness can erase the stain of even major sins.",
  "156": "The surah now addresses a specific form of erroneous thinking that was spreading among some of the weaker believers and the hypocrites after Uhud. “O believers! Do not be like the unfaithful who say about their brothers who travel throughout the land or engage in battle, ‘If they had stayed with us, they would not have died or been killed.’” The “unfaithful” (kafaru) refers to the hypocrites or outright disbelievers. When news of casualties came, whether from a trading journey or from the battlefield, they would claim that the deaths could have been avoided if the deceased had only stayed home. This “if only” (law) thinking is a rejection of divine decree and a path to endless, useless regret.\n\nThe verse reveals the divine punishment for this attitude: “Allah makes such thinking a cause of agony in their hearts.” The constant dwelling on hypothetical alternatives that contradict Allah’s decree creates a permanent state of grief, anxiety, and despair. The heart that does not submit to qadr is left to torment itself with scenarios that can never be.\n\nThe verse then provides the correct creedal anchor: “It is Allah who gives life and causes death.” Life and death are exclusively in Allah’s hands. The time, place, and manner of death are fixed by His decree. Whether a person travels, fights, or stays home, they will die at their appointed time. This belief liberates the heart from the tyranny of “what if. ” The verse concludes, “And Allah is All-Seeing of what you do.” He observes the reactions, the words, and the hidden thoughts of both the faithful and the unfaithful. For the believers, this verse is a call to sound theology and mental health. The “if only” mentality is a spiritual disease that the Prophet explicitly forbade: “If something befalls you, do not say, ‘If only I had done such and such,’ but say, ‘Qaddar Allahu wa ma sha’a fa‘al (Allah decreed and what He wills He does),’ for ‘if only’ opens the door to Satan’s work.” The believer accepts what has happened and moves forward, trusting that Allah’s decree is always ultimately good, even when it involves loss.\n\nThe verse also warns against the company of those who spread this toxic mindset.",
  "157": "The verse continues the consolation for the losses suffered at Uhud, redirecting the believers’ attention from the pain of death to the immeasurable gain that comes with it for the sincere. “Should you be martyred or die in the cause of Allah, then His forgiveness and mercy are far better than whatever wealth those who stay behind accumulate.\n\n” The phrase “in the cause of Allah” (fi sabil Allah) is the crucial qualifier. When a believer’s life ends while they are striving in the path of Allah—whether by martyrdom in battle or by a natural death during a journey for His sake—the outcome is not loss but supreme profit. The verse lists two things that await such a person: “His forgiveness and mercy.” Forgiveness wipes away all sins, and mercy encompasses all forms of divine pleasure, honour, and bliss. This forgiveness and mercy are described as “far better” (khayr) than all the worldly possessions that the people who stayed behind are busy accumulating. The contrast is deliberate. Those who refrained from battle and clung to their lives and wealth may enjoy temporary material gains, but they miss out on the eternal riches. The verse is not condemning lawful wealth, but it is putting it in its proper, inferior place relative to the rewards of the Hereafter. This verse was a direct comfort to the families of the seventy martyrs of Uhud, including Hamza ibn Abd al-Muttalib, the beloved uncle of the Prophet whose body was mutilated. It assured them that their loved ones had not lost anything, but had gained something that no amount of gold or land could match.\n\nThe verse also serves as a motivation for future sacrifice. It removes the fear of death by framing it as a transaction where one trades the temporary, mixed blessings of this world for the pure, eternal blessings of Allah’s forgiveness and mercy.\n\nFor the believer today, this verse is a powerful antidote to the materialism that makes one cling to life at the expense of duty. It reframes death in the path of duty—whether it be in defending the oppressed, speaking truth to power, or any other form of striving for Allah’s cause—as a gateway to the greatest imaginable good. The believer learns to view the sacrifices demanded by faith not as losses but as investments with an infinite return.",
  "158": "This concise verse delivers a profound and all-encompassing reminder about the ultimate destiny of every human being. “Whether you die or are martyred—all of you will be gathered before Allah.” It addresses the reality that death is inevitable for everyone, regardless of the manner in which it occurs. The distinction between “die” (muttum) and “are martyred” (qutiltum) covers the two primary ways a believer might depart this life: a natural death or a violent death in the path of Allah. Both lead to the same final destination: the gathering before Allah on the Day of Judgment.\n\nThe word “gathered” (tuhsharun) refers to the great assembly (hashr) where every soul from the first to the last will be brought forth to stand before their Lord for accountability. This reminder serves several purposes in the context of Uhud. First, it neutralises the fear of death that had caused some to flee. Since everyone will eventually die and be gathered before Allah, the only thing that matters is the state in which one arrives at that gathering. The person who dies in bed and the person who dies on the battlefield will both stand in the same court; the difference will be in the deeds they bring.\n\nTherefore, the one who dies as a martyr has secured a better standing. Second, it consoles those who lost loved ones. The deceased are not lost forever; they have merely preceded the living to the gathering place. The separation is temporary. Third, it warns those who cling to life at all costs, thinking they can escape death. No escape is possible; the only choice is how to invest the time before the inevitable gathering.\n\nFor the believer, this verse is a constant reminder of the transience of this world and the certainty of the Hereafter. It instills a mindset of preparation. Every morning and evening, the believer is aware that they are moving closer to the day when they will be gathered before Allah. This awareness shapes priorities, decisions, and conduct.\n\nThe verse also simplifies complex fears. Rather than worrying about the particular cause of death, the believer focuses on the state of their soul when death arrives. The gathering is the great equaliser; all will be there, and all will be judged justly. The believer therefore lives with the gathering in mind, striving to be among those who are gathered with honour and mercy.",
  "159": "This verse turns from the soldiers to the leader, addressing the Prophet Muhammad directly and, through him, all leaders and guides. It highlights a crucial quality that preserved the Muslim community after the disaster at Uhud. “It is out of Allah’s mercy that you, O Prophet, have been lenient with them.\n\n” The word “lenient” (linta) means gentle, soft, and approachable. The Prophet, despite the enormous pain he suffered—wounded, having lost his uncle and many companions, and having been disobeyed—did not react with harshness or fury. This leniency was not merely a personal trait; it was a direct gift of Allah’s mercy. It was divinely placed in his heart to save the community.\n\nThe verse then explains the consequence of the opposite behaviour: “Had you been cruel or hard-hearted, they would have certainly abandoned you. ” If the Prophet had been harsh (fazz) and hard-hearted (ghaliz al-qalb), the companions, already filled with guilt and grief, would have been crushed. They would have scattered, leaving the mission in ruins. This reveals a timeless leadership principle: harshness repels, gentleness attracts. The Prophet’s gentleness after their grave error was what allowed the community to heal and rebound.\n\nThe verse then issues a series of commands that form a comprehensive guide for leadership: “So pardon them, ask Allah’s forgiveness for them, and consult with them in conducting matters.” Pardoning (‘fu) addresses the personal right of the leader to be angry; he should forgive. Seeking Allah’s forgiveness (istaghfir) addresses their spiritual need; the leader intercedes for them. Consultation (shawirhum) addresses their collective dignity and the practical need for diverse input.\n\nThis command to consult was given even after the consultation before Uhud had led to a result that some might have considered a mistake, teaching that consultation remains a duty regardless of outcomes. The next step is “Once you make a decision, put your trust in Allah.” After consultation, a firm decision is made, and then reliance (tawakkul) is placed on Allah, not on the decision itself.\n\nThe verse ends with “Surely Allah loves those who trust in Him. ” This is the reward for the leader who embodies these qualities: divine love. For the believer, this verse is a comprehensive manual for any position of responsibility, whether in a family, an organisation, or a community. It balances mercy, forgiveness, spiritual care, inclusiveness, decisiveness, and ultimate reliance on Allah. It teaches that strength is in gentleness, and success is from Allah, not from mere human planning.",
  "160": "The surah closes this section of the Uhud narrative with the ultimate declaration of reliance on Allah, drawing the logical conclusion from all that has been said about victory and defeat. “If Allah helps you, none can defeat you.\n\n” This is the absolute statement of divine omnipotence in the context of human struggle. The Arabic “yansurkum” (helps you) covers all forms of divine aid—angels, psychological serenity, strategic advantage, or the casting of fear into the enemy. When this help is present, no human force, no matter how vast, can overcome the one whom Allah aids. The converse is equally absolute: “But if He denies you help, then who else can help you?\n\n” The word “yakhdhulkum” (denies you help) implies abandonment and withdrawal of support. If Allah leaves a people to their own devices, there is no power in the universe that can assist them. No army, no wealth, no technology, no alliance can substitute for the absence of divine help. This rhetorical question—“who else can help you?”—has an implied answer of absolute negation: no one. This truth is the cornerstone of Islamic theology regarding all human affairs, not just warfare. It ties together the lessons of Badr and Uhud. At Badr, Allah’s help came, and the outnumbered Muslims triumphed. At Uhud, when the believers’ own actions caused a withdrawal of some aspects of that help, they tasted defeat.\n\nYet even in that defeat, Allah’s ultimate help did not abandon them; the enemy withdrew. The verse then issues the natural command: “So in Allah let the believers put their trust. ” Tawakkul, or trust, is the practical application of this knowledge. It means to rely completely on Allah after doing everything within one’s power, with the heart at peace knowing that the outcome is in the best of hands. This verse is a powerful spiritual anchor.\n\nFor the believer today, in any struggle—whether it be personal, professional, or communal—the principle remains unchanged. Success comes only from Allah, and no human effort can succeed without His will. The believer does their utmost, then rests their heart on Allah, knowing that if He aids, no obstacle is insurmountable, and if He withholds, no amount of striving will force success. This cultivates a profound humility, a reduction of anxiety, and a fearless determination. The verse is a declaration of independence from all worldly powers and a declaration of total dependence on the Lord of all powers.",
  "161": "Those who fled on day two crowds met — Satan made them slip due to some of what they earned — but Allah pardoned them — Allah Forgiving, Forbearing. Inna alladhina tawallaw minkum yawma iltaqa al-jam'an innama istazallahum ash-Shaytanu bi-ba'di ma kasabu — Those fled day crowds met — Satan made slip due to some what earned — earlier errors, worldly desires, allowed Satan foothold.\n\nWa laqad afa Allahu anhum — But Allah pardoned them — pardon after slip.\n\nInnAllaha Ghafur Halim — Forgiving, Forbearing — Halim — not hastening punishment, giving time to return.\n\nThis verse comforts those who fled: slip due to some earned, but pardon possible, Allah Forgiving Forbearing.\n\nIt also shows cause: Satan slip due to some earned — sins open door — as earlier Satan threatens poverty orders immorality (2:268).\n\nLinks to earlier no helpers vs now pardoned.\n\nAfter pardon, warning not be like unfaithful saying about brothers if stayed not killed.",
  "162": "O you who believe, do not be like those who disbelieved and said about their brothers when they travelled or went to battle, If they stayed with us not died nor killed — so Allah makes that regret in hearts — Allah gives life and causes death — Allah Seeing what you do.\n\nYa ayyuha alladhina amanu la takunu kalladhina kafaru wa qalu li-ikhwanihim idha darabu fil-ardi aw kanu ghuzzan law kanu indana ma matu wa ma qutilu — Do not be like disbelievers said about brothers when travelled or battle — if stayed with us not died nor killed.\n\nLi-yaj'ala Allahu dhalika hasratan fi qulubihim — So Allah makes that regret in hearts — statement becomes hasrah — regret.\n\nWallahu yuhyi wa yumit — Allah gives life causes death — same as Ibrahim argument (40) — not staying home gives life nor travel causes death; life death His hand (2:258).\n\nWallahu bima ta'maluna Basir — Seeing what you do — travel, battle, saying.\n\nThis verse addresses what-if mentality: if only had not gone... had stayed... Such thought regret, shirk? Because attributes life death to staying, not Allah.\n\nQadar belief: even if in houses those destined killed would go forth places slain (150). So staying wouldn't have prevented.\n\nFor believers, leave what-if, trust written term (141).\n\nNext if martyred die in Allah path forgiveness mercy better than they accumulate.",
  "163": "And if you are killed in Allah's path or die — forgiveness and mercy from Allah are better than what they accumulate. Wa la-in qutiltum fi sabili Allah aw muttum la-maghfiratun min Allahi wa rahmatun khayrun mimma yajma'un — If killed in Allah path or die — any death — maghfirah rahmat from Allah better than what they accumulate — wealth, property, worldly life beautified earlier.\n\nAccumulation — yajma'un — same as heaped treasures gold silver (14) — beautified desires.\n\nComparison: forgiveness mercy vs world entire accumulation — forgiveness mercy better.\n\nEven those who stayed accumulating wealth think better, but true better is maghfirah rahmat.\n\nThis reorients definition better — earlier better than desires is Gardens (15) and ridwan; here forgiveness mercy better than accumulation.\n\nNext whether you die or killed all will be gathered before Allah.",
  "164": "And whether you die or are killed — to Allah you will be gathered. Wa la-in muttum aw qutiltum la-ila Allahi tuhsharun — Whether die natural or martyred killed — to Allah gathered — hashr — same root as numbered days your gathering to Him (2:203).\n\nGathering inevitable regardless mode death.\n\nEarlier those fled homes thousands fear death said die then gave life (2:243) — fleeing not prevent gathering.\n\nLink to earlier Day soul finds good present and wishes evil far — gathering for that.\n\nSo if gathering to Allah inevitable, best ensure forgiveness mercy better than accumulation goes with you, not just accumulation that stays.\n\nNext mercy lenient with them.",
  "165": "So by mercy from Allah you were lenient with them — had you been harsh hard-hearted they would have dispersed from around you — so pardon them, seek forgiveness for them, consult them in matter — when you decide put trust in Allah — Allah loves those who trust.\n\nFa-bima rahmatin min Allahi linta lahum — By mercy from Allah you were lenient — lin — soft — with them — after disobedience archers, fleeing, dispute — Prophet could have been harsh, but mercy.\n\nWa law kunta fazzan ghaliza al-qalb lanfaddu min hawlik — Had harsh hard-hearted dispersed from around you — fazz — harsh speech, ghaliz qalb — hard heart.\n\nFa'fu anhum wastaghfir lahum wa shawirhum fil-amr — So pardon them, seek forgiveness for them, consult them in matter — three steps after leniency: pardon personal wrong to you, seek forgiveness from Allah for their sin, consult them in future affairs — despite they messed consultation previously? Yes consult again — restores confidence.\n\nFa-idha azamta fa-tawakkal ala Allah — When decide put trust Allah.\n\nInnAllaha yuhibbu al-mutawakkiliin — Allah loves those who trust.\n\nThis verse cornerstone prophetic leadership: mercy leniency even after major mistake, pardon, istighfar, shura, then tawakkul.\n\nModel for any leader family: harshness scatters, leniency gathers.\n\nNote pardon seek forgiveness consult are traits muttaqin — pardon people (130), seek forgiveness (131), spend etc.\n\nMawlid? Actually leadership mercy.\n\nNext if Allah helps none can defeat.",
  "166": "If Allah helps you, no one can overcome you — if He forsakes you, who can help you after — in Allah believers put trust. In yansurkum Allahu fa-la ghaliba lakum wa in yakhdhulkum fa-man dha alladhi yansurukum min ba'dih — If Allah helps you no overcomer, if He forsakes who can help after.\n\nWa ala Allahi falyatawakkali al-mu'minun — In Allah believers put trust — tawakkul — same as previous when decide trust.\n\nAfter Uhud where help seemed delayed due to disobedience, reminder help overcomer condition: help from Allah alone.\n\nVictory only from Allah Mighty Wise (122).\n\nSo no need take disbelievers as inner circle for help; if Allah helps none overcomes; if forsakes no inner circle helps.\n\nTawakkul returns many times.\n\nNext not appropriate prophet withhold spoils.",
  "167": "It is not for a prophet to embezzle — whoever embezzles will bring what he embezzled Day of Resurrection — then every soul paid in full what it earned, they will not be wronged.\n\nWa ma kana li-nabiyyin an yaghulla — Not for prophet to embezzle — ghullul — withhold spoils — or betray. Some accusation at Badr about missing red velvet? Maybe hypocrites accused Prophet withheld? This clears.\n\nWa man yaghlul ya'ti bima ghalla yawma al-qiyamah — Who embezzles will bring what embezzled Day — carrying on neck camel, horse, etc.\n\nThumma tuwaffa kullu nafsin ma kasabat wa hum la yuzlamun — Then every soul paid full what earned not wronged — same as earlier payment full.\n\nEmbezzlement includes withholding trust — amanah — whether war spoils, orphan property, bitanah secrets.\n\nProphet trustworthy — Amin — cannot ghulul.\n\nFor believers, warning: taking small from public wealth will come carrying Day.\n\nNext are those seeking Allah pleasure like wrath?",
  "168": "Is one who follows Allah's pleasure like one who draws wrath from Allah — refuge Hell — evil destination. Afa-man ittaba'a ridwana Allah ka-man ba'a bi-sakhatin min Allah wa ma'wahu Jahannam wa bi'sa al-masir — Is follower of ridwan like drawer of wrath?\n\nRidwan earlier better than gardens (15) and gardens described ridwanun min Allah.\n\nFollowing ridwan means following Messenger (31) Allah will love you.\n\nDrawing wrath — ba'a bi-sakhat — like those incurred wrath (110), wronged themselves.\n\nMa'wahu Jahannam — refuge Hell, evil destination — similar evil lodging wrongdoers (147).\n\nQuestion rhetorical obviously not equal.\n\nAfter ghulul, two paths: seek pleasure vs deserve wrath.\n\nFor Uhud: those who obeyed order seeking ridwan vs those who sought booty seeking worldly gain drew wrath.\n\nNext varying degrees in sight Allah.",
  "169": "They have varying degrees with Allah — Allah is Seeing what they do. Hum darajatun inda Allah — They varying degrees with Allah — follower ridwan higher degree than drawer wrath. Not all same — laysu sawa (111).\n\nDegrees — darajat — Paradise levels and Fire depths.\n\nWallahu Basirun bima ya'malun — Seeing what they do — Basir — as earlier Seeing servants (15, 19). Seeing determines degrees.\n\nAfter Uhud, companions not all same: those patient firm remembered, sought forgiveness vs those fashilta disputed.\n\nDegree concept comforts: small difference patience now large degree difference later.\n\nNext favor raising messenger among them.",
  "170": "Certainly Allah favoured believers when He raised among them messenger from themselves reciting verses, purifying them, teaching Book and wisdom — though before they were in clear error.\n\nLaqad manna Allahu ala al-mu'minina idh ba'atha fihim rasulan min anfusihim yatlu alayhim ayatihi wa yuzakkihim wa yu'allimuhum al-Kitaba wal-Hikmata wa in kanu min qablu la-fi dalalin mubin — Allah favoured — manna — gave favour — believers when raised among them messenger from themselves — min anfusihim — from themselves — same language earlier Messenger from yourselves (3:164? actually same). Reciting verses, purifying, teaching Book wisdom — same four tasks from Ibrahim dua (2:129) and earlier verse (2:151). Though before clear error — dalal mubin — Jahiliyyah tribal wars, worship idols, burying daughters.\n\nManna — favour — reminds earlier favour remember when enemies joined hearts brothers (102).\n\nSo after defeat, reminder favour still — Messenger still among you, reciting purifying teaching — even if battle lost, favour not lost.\n\nTeaching Book and wisdom includes explaining why defeat happened — purifying.\n\nThough before clear error — highlights transformation — from error to best nation (108) enjoining good.\n\nNext why when suffered casualties although made enemy suffer twice you protested how could this be.",
  "171": "Why is it when affliction struck you — and you had struck twice as much — you said how can this be? Say, It is from yourselves — Allah has power over all. Awa lamma asabatkum musibatun wa qad asabtum mithlayha qultum anna hadha — When Uhud affliction 70 killed, you had struck twice at Badr 70 killed and 70 captured — you said how can this be? — anna hadha — how?\n\nQul huwa min indi anfusikum — Say it is from yourselves — from your own selves — dispute disobedience love of what you love after He showed you what you love (148).\n\nInnAllaha ala kulli shay'in qadir — Power over all — capable to give victory and test with loss.\n\nAccountability without blaming qadar? Both: Qadar Allah power, but cause from yourselves — disobedience archers.\n\nThis teaches internal locus after calamity: not conspiracy, not \"Allah failed\", but from yourselves — self-reflection.\n\nYet after self-reflection, pardon mercy favours.\n\nNext what suffered day crowds met by permission Allah to distinguish believers.",
  "172": "What struck you on day crowds met was by permission of Allah — to make evident the believers and make evident hypocrites.\n\nWa ma asabakum yawma iltaqa al-jam'ani fa-bi-idhni Allah wa li-ya'lama al-mu'minina wa li-ya'lama alladhina nafaqu — What struck day crowds met — Uhud — was by permission Allah — bi-idhni — not random, permission to distinguish believers and make evident hypocrites — nafaqu.\n\nPermission includes allowing disobedience consequences to manifest.\n\nYa'lama — make known — earlier (138) to make evident those who strove patient.\n\nHypocrites exposed: when told come fight cause Allah or defend, they said if knew fighting we would follow you that day nearer disbelief than belief saying with mouths not in hearts Allah knows what conceal (167+).\n\nUhud filtering: believers distinguished, hypocrites exposed.\n\nNext details hypocrites reply and those sat home saying had listened would not be killed.",
  "173": "When it was said to them, Come fight in Allah's path or defend — they said, If we knew fighting we would follow you — that day they were nearer to disbelief than belief — saying with mouths not in hearts — Allah knows what they conceal.\n\nQiila lahum ta'alaw qatilu fi sabili Allah aw idfa'u — Come fight path Allah or defend — idfa'u — at least defend city, family, not necessarily offencive.\n\nQalu law na'lamu qitalan la-ittaba'nakum — If knew fighting we would follow — claim not real battle, just skirmish you invented.\n\nHum lil-kufri yawma'idhin aqrabu minhum lil-iman — That day nearer disbelief than belief — qarib — close.\n\nYaquluna bi-afwahihim ma laysa fi qulubihim — Say with mouths not in hearts — same as earlier those who say we believe not believers (2:8) and pleasing speech but most quarrelsome opponent (2:204).\n\nWallahu A'lamu bima yaktumun — Allah knows what conceal — same as knows what hearts conceal greater (116).\n\nExpose hypocrisy pattern: refuse help, excuse no real fighting, near kufr, mouths not hearts.\n\nNext those sat home saying about brothers had followed us not killed.",
  "174": "Those who sat and said about brothers, If they obeyed us not killed — Say, ward off death from yourselves if truthful.\n\nAlladhina qalu li-ikhwanihim wa qa'adu law ata'una ma qutilu — Those sat and said about brothers if obeyed us not killed — qa'adu — sat at home not fighting, then said about brothers killed: had followed us stayed home not killed — same as earlier do not be like those disbelieved said about brothers when travelled or fought if stayed not died nor killed (162).\n\nQul fa-idra'u an anfusikum al-mawta in kuntum sadiqin — Say ward off death from yourselves if truthful — challenge: can you prevent own death at appointed time (141)? No soul dies except permission at written term. So staying would not prevent.\n\nIf death written, will go forth to places slain even if in houses (150). So statement false.\n\nAnswer similar: death from Allah permission not from staying.\n\nNext martyrs alive with Lord.",
  "175": "Do not ever think those killed in Allah's path dead — nay alive with Lord provided for — rejoicing in what Allah gave them of bounty and delighting for those not yet joined behind — no fear upon them nor they grieve.\n\nWa la tahsabanna alladhina qutilu fi sabili Allahi amwatan bal ahya'un inda Rabbihim yurzaqun — Do not ever think martyred dead nay alive with Lord provided — same as 2:154 do not say dead rather alive but you perceive not.\n\nYurzaqun — provided — Rizq — same as Maryam provision without account, here martyrs sustenance with Lord.\n\nFarihina bima atahumu Allahu min fadlih — Rejoicing in what Allah gave bounty — fadl — as earlier bounty Owner great bounty (74).\n\nWa yastabshiruna billadhina lam yalhaqu bihim min khalfihim alla khawfun alayhim wa la hum yahzanun — Delighting for those not yet joined behind no fear nor grieve — same phrase no fear grieve for believers earlier (2:112 etc). Martyrs joyful not only for self but for comrades coming.\n\nThis verse after sat home saying if obeyed not killed: they think dead ended; reality alive rejoicing. So sitting claim \"not killed\" misses honour: killed alive better.\n\nFor families grieving Uhud 70, comfort: alive with Lord provided, no fear grief.\n\nNext joyful receiving grace bounty Allah does not deny reward believers.",
  "176": "They are rejoicing in favour and bounty from Allah, and Allah does not waste reward of believers. Yastabshiruna bi-ni'matin min Allahi wa fadlin wa anna Allaha la yudi'u ajra al-mu'minina — Rejoicing favour bounty and that Allah does not waste reward believers.\n\nYastabshiruna — rejoicing — as earlier yastabshiruna billadhina lam yalhaqu... — delighting for those not yet joined — now rejoicing favour bounty.\n\nNi'mah fadl — favour, bounty — same two words repeated as return with favour bounty (179) after Hamra al-Asad, same as bounty Owner great bounty (74).\n\nWa anna Allaha la yudi'u ajra al-mu'minina — Allah does not waste reward believers — la yudi'u — does not allow loss — same as whatever good they do never unacknowledged (113) and will not waste deed any doer male female (195).\n\nMartyrs joy double: personal favour bounty, and principle reward not wasted.\n\nAt Uhud after defeat where reward seemed wasted — 70 dead, wounded — assurance reward not wasted.\n\nEven response after injury (177) great reward, after warning people gathered (178) faith increased, return favour (179) — all demonstrate not wasting.\n\nFor us, small good done — dawn forgiveness seekers, patient, truthful — not wasted. Martyrs ensure.\n\nNext those responded after injury great reward bridging to Hasbun Allah.",
  "177": "Those who responded to Allah and Messenger after injury befell them — for those who did good among them and were mindful — great reward.\n\nAlladhina istajabu lillahi war-Rasuli min ba'di ma asabahum al-qarh — Those responded to Allah and Messenger after injury befell — qarh — wounds Uhud — next day Prophet called to go after Quraysh to show not defeated — Hamra al-Asad expedition — only those wounded previous day allowed? Some wounded came despite wounds.\n\nLilladhina ahsanu minhum wattaqaw ajrun azim — For those did good among them and were mindful great reward — ajr azim — great.\n\nResponse after injury demonstrates true tawakkul trust (165), sabr patient, enjoining good.\n\nIt shows Islam not only victory celebration but response after injury.\n\nGreat reward despite wounds — as earlier excellent reward workers (132).\n\nNext those warned enemies mobilized.",
  "178": "Those who when people said to them, People gathered against you so fear them, it increased them in faith and they said, Allah sufficient for us, excellent Disposer.\n\nAlladhina qala lahum an-nasu inna an-nasa qad jama'u lakum fakhshawhum fa-zadahum imanan wa qalu hasbun Allahu wa ni'ma al-Wakil — Those when people said people gathered against you so fear them — warning — Abu Sufyan threatened return?\n\nFa-zadahum imanan — increased them in faith — not fear — faith increased — Iman can increase as earlier those who believe.\n\nWa qalu hasbun Allahu wa ni'ma al-Wakil — Said Allah sufficient for us excellent Disposer — Hasbun Allah — enough — Wakil — disposer affairs.\n\nThis dua after distress serenity drowsiness — trust.\n\nHasbun Allah phrase used by Ibrahim when thrown fire, Muhammad when plotted.\n\nIncreased faith after warning sign firm hearts.\n\nNext they returned with favour grace no harm touching.",
  "179": "So they returned with favour from Allah and bounty — no harm touched them — they followed pleasure of Allah — Allah Owner great bounty.\n\nFanqalabu bi-ni'matin min Allahi wa fadlin lam yamsashum su'un wattaba'u ridwana Allah Wallahu dhu fadlin azim — Returned with ni'mah fadl no harm touched — as earlier warded off distress with distress so not grieve (149), now no harm.\n\nWattaba'u ridwana Allah — Followed pleasure Allah — ridwan earlier better than gardens (15) — price return.\n\nWallahu dhu fadlin azim — Owner great bounty — same closing earlier.\n\nHamra al-Asad expedition: they went out despite wounds, Quraysh already left fearing; returned with favour bounty no harm.\n\nObedience after injury following ridwan results favour bounty no harm.\n\nLesson: Hasbun Allah path returns favour bounty even when outnumbered.\n\nNext that warning only Satan trying prompt fear followers so fear Me.",
  "180": "Indeed that was Satan trying to make you fear his allies — so do not fear them, fear Me if you are believers. Innama dhalikum ash-Shaytanu yukhawwifu awliya'ah — That was Satan trying make you fear his allies — awliya' — supporters — Satan frightens via allies rumours.\n\nFa-la takhafuhum wa khafuni in kuntum mu'minina — So do not fear them fear Me if believers — khafuni — fear Me — fear Allah alone as earlier Ittaqullah haqqa tuqatih.\n\nIbrahim feared Allah not Nimrud fire, Zakariya asked despite old age fearing Allah, Maryam trusted.\n\nAfter Hasbun Allah, command not fear allies Satan.\n\nSatan's strategy earlier threatens poverty (2:268), orders immorality, now tries prompt fear followers.\n\nCure fear Me if believers — iman includes fear.\n\nNext do not grieve those race to disbelieve.",
  "181": "Do not grieve over those who rush to disbelief — they will not harm Allah at all — Allah wants not assign them share Hereafter — they will have great punishment.\n\nWa la yahzunka alladhina yusari'una fil-kufr — Do not grieve over those rush to disbelief — yusari'una — race as earlier race good deeds (103) but race to kufr — hypocrites rushing?\n\nInnahum lan yadurru Allaha shay'an — Not harm Allah at all.\n\nYuridu Allahu alla yaj'ala lahum hazzan fil-akhirah — Allah wants not assign them share Hereafter — hazz — portion — no share.\n\nWa lahum adhabun azim — Great punishment.\n\nAfter command not fear allies, not grieve rushers disbelief.\n\nRushing to disbelief includes morning evening plot (72), twisting Book, etc.\n\nThey not harm Allah because Allah Ghani free need (96, 125).\n\nNo share Hereafter similar to no share for those exchange covenant small price (77).\n\nNext those trade belief for disbelief never harm Allah.",
  "182": "Those who purchased disbelief with belief will never harm Allah at all — they will have painful punishment. Inna alladhina ishtaru al-kufra bil-iman lan yadurru Allaha shay'an wa lahum adhabun alim — Purchased disbelief with belief — ishtaru — trade as earlier traded guidance error — 175 traded guidance error and forgiveness punishment.\n\nTrade is staggering: belief in hand given to take disbelief — as earlier those sold souls for magic (2:102) miserable price.\n\nNever harm Allah.\n\nPainful punishment alim — as earlier painful for disbelievers fuel Fire.\n\nThis mirrors verse 181 race to disbelief; now purchase.\n\nNext disbelievers think living longer good.",
  "183": "Those who disbelieve should not think that We extend their time good for them — We only extend so they increase in sin — they will have humiliating punishment. Wa la yahsabanna alladhina kafaru annama numli lahum khayrun li-anfusihim — Disbelievers think extension time granted good for them — imla — giving rope.\n\nInnama numli lahum li-yazdadu ithma — We only extend so increase sin — more time more sins accumulation.\n\nWa lahum adhabun muhin — Humiliating punishment — muhin — humiliating — as disgrace struck (110) humiliating.\n\nExtension is not honour but rope for sinner to increase sin as earlier Satan threatens? Actually mercy delay gives chance repent but if persist accumulates.\n\nFor believers extension used for repentance correct (88) — crown.\n\nToday some think long life prosperity sign Allah pleased, but could be imla.\n\nNext Allah would not leave believers condition until distinguished.",
  "184": "Allah would not leave believers in state you are in until He distinguishes bad from good — Allah would not inform you of unseen — but Allah chooses from messengers whom He wills — so believe in Allah and His messengers — if you believe and are mindful you will have great reward.\n\nMa kana Allahu li-yadhara al-mu'minina ala ma antum alayhi hatta yamiza al-khabitha min at-tayyib — Allah would not leave believers in state you are — mixed believers hypocrites — until He distinguishes bad from good — khabith from tayyib — via tests like Uhud, bitanah exposure, morning evening plot.\n\nWa ma kana Allahu li-yutli'akum ala al-ghayb — Allah would not inform you directly of unseen — i.e., who hypocrite in hearts? That's ghayb He keeps. But through tests He makes evident.\n\nWa lakinna Allaha yajtabi min rusulihi man yasha — But Allah chooses from messengers whom wills — to give some unseen news as earlier casting pens unseen (44) news unseen revealed to you.\n\nFa-aminu billahi wa rusulih — So believe in Allah messengers — belief includes accepting these tests distinguish.\n\nWa in tu'minu wa tattaqu fa-lakum ajrun azim — If believe mindful great reward — ajr azim — same as those responded after injury (177).\n\nThis verse explains wisdom Uhud: not chaos but filtering khabith tayyib.\n\nAllah would not leave mixed; must filter.\n\nNext do not withhold Allah bounties think good.",
  "185": "Those who withhold what Allah gave them of His bounty should not think it is good for them — rather bad — they will be collared with what they withheld on Day — to Allah belongs inheritance heavens earth — Allah Aware of what you do.\n\nWa la yahsabanna alladhina yabkhaluna bima atahumu Allahu min fadlih huwa khayran lahum — Those withhold — yabkhaluna — stingy — what Allah gave of bounty think good for them — rather bad.\n\nSayutawwaquna ma bakhilu bihi yawma al-qiyamah — They will be collared with what withheld Day — tawq — collar around neck — as earlier embezzler brings what embezzled (167) and spending beloved (91) opposite withholding.\n\nWa lillahi mirathu as-samawati wal-ard — To Allah inheritance heavens earth — mirath — all wealth ultimately returns Him — so withholding temporary.\n\nWallahu bima ta'maluna Khabir — Aware what you do — as earlier Allah Aware, Hearing Knowing.\n\nThis verse about bukhl — stinginess — connects to spending beloved, spending ease hardship (130), and not think extension time good (183). Withholding not good.\n\nIncludes withholding zakah, withholding knowledge hiding Book (187), withholding support.\n\nBad not good.\n\nNext Allah heard those said Allah poor we rich.",
  "186": "Allah has certainly heard saying of those who said, Allah is poor and we are rich — We will record what they said and killing prophets without right — and We will say, Taste punishment of burning.\n\nLaqad sami'a Allahu qawla alladhina qalu inna Allaha faqirun wa nahnu aghniya — Allah certainly heard those who said Allah poor we rich — Jews said after verses about lending good loan to Allah (2:245) mocked: Allah poor needs loan we rich. Mocking.\n\nSa-naktubu ma qalu wa qatlahum al-anbiya bi-ghayri haqq — We will record what they said and killing prophets without right — link speech killing — same crime as earlier 21 killing prophets unjustly and ordering justice.\n\nWa naqulu dhuqu adhab al-hariq — Say taste punishment burning — hariq — burning.\n\nAllah Heard — Sami'a — as earlier Allah Hearing Knowing (119) around arrangements, now hears slur.\n\nRecorded — sa-naktubu — same as We will record what they said.\n\nTaste punishment burning — as earlier fuel Fire, severe punishment.\n\nThis shows mocking sacred things not small — saying Allah poor — serious.\n\nIt follows verse about stinginess — they said Allah poor we rich because told spend from beloved — stinginess leads to slander.\n\nNext this is for what hands sent forth.",
  "187": "That is for what your hands sent forth — Allah is never unjust to servants. Dhalika bima qaddamat aydikum wa anna Allaha laysa bi-zallamin lil-abid — That — taste burning — for what hands sent forth — qaddamat — same as whatever good you send forth find with Allah (2:110) — but this evil they sent forth.\n\nWa anna Allaha laysa bi-zallamin lil-abid — Allah never unjust to servants — not zulm, punishment justice.\n\nRepeats principle every soul paid full not wronged (25).\n\nFor stingy mockers, what hands sent forth includes saying Allah poor, killing prophets, withholding bounty — collared.\n\nFor believers, what hands sent forth includes spending beloved, restraining anger, pardoning, remembering seeking forgiveness — gardens.\n\nJustice ensures no injustice.\n\nNext those say Allah commanded not believe messenger unless brings offering consumed by fire.",
  "188": "Those who said, Allah instructed us not to believe in any messenger unless he brings offering consumed by fire — Say, messengers before me came with clear proofs and with what you said — why did you kill them if truthful?\n\nAlladhina qalu inna Allaha ahida ilayna alla nu'mina li-rasulin hatta ya'tiyana bi-qurbanin ta'kuluhu an-nar — Those said Allah instructed us not believe messenger unless brings qurban offering consumed by fire — Fire eating offering sign true prophet in earlier times? They demand same.\n\nQul qad ja'akum rusulun min qabli bil-bayyinat wa billadhi qultum fa-lima qataltumuhum in kuntum sadiqin — Say messengers before me came with clear proofs and with that you said — why killed if truthful? — Exposes lie: previous prophets brought that sign and still killed.\n\nSo condition excuse, not genuine.\n\nSimilar to those who said if only Allah would speak to us or sign come (2:118) hearts alike.\n\nIt shows excuse after excuse after knowledge — after sign, kill messenger.\n\nFor us, condition setting for faith — if only seen sign would believe — often false; after sign new excuse.\n\nNext if rejected so were messengers before came clear proofs divine Books enlightening Scriptures.",
  "189": "If they deny you, messengers before you were denied who came with clear proofs, written ordinances, and enlightening Scripture. Fa-in kadhdhabuka fa-qad kudhdhiba rusulun min qablika ja'u bil-bayyinat waz-zuburi wal-kitabi al-munir — If they deny you — Prophet — messengers before denied who came with bayyinat, zubur — written ordinances, and kitab munir — enlightening Scripture.\n\nBayyinat — clear proofs — zubur — originally Psalms? Written pieces — kitabi munir — illuminating Book.\n\nThree levels revelation: clear signs, written laws, enlightening scripture — all brought before.\n\nSo rejection not new, not personal to you.\n\nConsolation: you are among messengers (2:252) pattern same.\n\nNext every soul taste death full reward Day Judgment whoever spared Fire admitted Paradise success.",
  "190": "Every soul will taste death — you will only be paid in full on Day of Resurrection — whoever is drawn away from Fire and admitted to Paradise has succeeded — worldly life is only enjoyment of delusion.\n\nKullu nafsin dha'iqatu al-mawt — Every soul taste death — dhaiqah — taste — sample before full? Death taste brief, then eternal.\n\nWa innama tuwaffawna ujurakum yawma al-qiyamah — You will only be paid full Day Resurrection — tuwaffawna — full payment (25) — in worldly life partial.\n\nFa-man zuhziha an an-nar wa udkhila al-jannata fa-qad faza — Whoever drawn away — zuhziha — pulled away gently inch by inch from Fire and admitted Paradise has succeeded — fawz — real success — unlike success they defined beautified desires (14).\n\nWa ma al-hayatu ad-dunya illa mata'u al-ghurur — Worldly life only enjoyment delusion — mata' al-ghurur — deluding enjoyment, as earlier brief enjoyment then Hell evil rest (197).\n\nThis verse after rejection messengers: messengers died, deniers die, every soul tastes death, full payment later, real success not this world.\n\nIt also comforts Uhud losses: tasted death but full pay later; spared Fire admitted Paradise has succeeded — martyrs 70 succeeded.\n\nFor us attachment world delusion.\n\nNext you will be tested wealth selves hear many hurtful words.",
  "191": "You will surely be tested in wealth and selves — you will hear many hurtful words from those given Book before you and from polytheists — but if you are patient and mindful — that is from matters requiring resolve.\n\nLa-tublawunna fi amwalikum wa anfusikum wa la-tasma'unna min alladhina utu al-Kitaba min qablikum wa min alladhina ashraku adhan kathiran — You will certainly be tested in wealth — loss like Uhud spoils, spending beloved — and selves — injury death — and hear many hurtful adhan kathiran — many hurtful words from People Book before and polytheists — like Allah poor we rich, Fire few days, mocking.\n\nWa in tasbiru wa tattaqu fa-inna dhalika min azmi al-umur — If patient mindful that from matters requiring resolve — azm al-umur — firm determination.\n\nSame patient mindful condition that prevents plot harm (118), brings five thousand angels (121), ensures help.\n\nTesting wealth selves hurtful words is Sunnah after every lesson, not anomaly.\n\nIt ties earlier: spend from what love (92) test wealth, wrestle patient, hear hurtful words from same groups plotting morning evening.\n\nMatters requiring resolve — azm — same as earlier best provision taqwa includes resolve.\n\nNext covenant those given Book to make known not hide yet cast behind backs small price.",
  "192": "And when Allah took covenant from those given Book — you must make it clear to people and not hide it — but they cast it behind backs and sold it for small price — evil is what they purchased.\n\nWa idh akhadha Allahu mithaqa alladhina utu al-Kitaba la-tubayyinunnahu lin-nasi wa la taktumunah — When Allah took covenant from those given Book you must make clear to people not hide it — bayyin — clear and not hide — kitman earlier banned (2:159,2:174).\n\nFa-nabadhuhu wara'a zuhurihim washtaraw bihi thamanan qalilan — But cast it behind backs and sold for small price — same phrase as People Book cast Book Allah behind backs as if did not know (2:101) — nabadh behind backs — casting behind.\n\nFa-bi'sa ma yashtarun — Evil what they purchased — same as miserable price sold souls (2:102).\n\nBayyin not hide covenant serious for scholars — hiding description Muhammad, hiding Ayat riba, hiding provision.\n\nSmall price — worldly benefit — as earlier small price (77).\n\nEvil purchase leads to thinking those rejoice misdeeds will escape? Next verse.\n\nFor us today scholars influencers hiding truth small price — likes — evil purchase.",
  "193": "Do not think those who rejoice in what they did and love to be praised for what they did not do — will escape punishment — they will have painful punishment.\n\nLa tahsabanna alladhina yafrahuna bima ataw wa yuhibbuna an yuhmadu bima lam yaf'alu — Do not think those who rejoice what they did — e.g., casting behind backs, plotting, yet rejoice — and love praised what did not do — love credit for knowledge charity they did not give — will escape.\n\nWa la tahsabanna... bi-mafazatin min al-adhab wa lahum adhabun alim — Not in escape from punishment, painful.\n\nYafrahuna bima ataw — rejoice what they did — opposite those who rejoice grace bounty from Allah (176) — these rejoice misdeed.\n\nYuhibbuna an yuhmadu bima lam yaf'alu — love praised what did not do — like claiming we believe while concealing, claiming guidance.\n\nThis applies to anyone: posting good deed didn't do, rejoicing plot.\n\nPainful punishment.\n\nNext kingdom heavens earth Allah capable everything.",
  "194": "To Allah belongs kingdom heavens and earth — Allah has power over all. Wa lillahi mulku as-samawati wal-ard Wallahu ala kulli shay'in qadir — To Allah kingdom heavens earth — Mulku — same as Owner dominion gives whom wills (26) — Qadir — power over all — same as earlier Allah has power over all (26, and 2:106).\n\nAfter covenant hiding, reminder kingdom belongs Allah, He capable — can expose hidden, punish, record.\n\nTransition to reflection creation heavens earth.\n\nThis verse bridge to final profound passage about ulu al-albab reflecting.\n\nIt closes law history section before worship reflection.\n\nIf kingdom His, hiding Book for small price foolish — kingdom not theirs.\n\nNext in creation heavens earth... signs for people of reason.",
  "195": "Indeed in creation heavens and earth and alternation night and day — are signs for people of reason.\n\nInna fi khalqi as-samawati wal-ard wakhtilafi al-layli wan-nahar la-ayatin li-uli al-albab — In creation heavens earth and alternation night day — signs for ulu al-albab — people of inner cores — as earlier (7, 190).\n\nSigns include: heavens earth creation as earlier (2:164) creation heavens earth, alternation night day, ships, rain etc — signs for those reason.\n\nUlu al-albab — same as rasikhuna? Those who remember.\n\nKhalq heavens earth — same as Shapes wombs as wills (6) Provider without account (37) Owner dominion merges night day (27).\n\nAlternation night day also earlier merging.\n\nSigns point Hayy Qayyum etc.\n\nNext describes who are ulu al-albab.",
  "196": "Those who remember Allah standing sitting and lying on sides and reflect on creation heavens and earth — Our Lord You did not create this in vain — Glory be to You — protect us from punishment Fire.\n\nAlladhina yadhkuruna Allaha qiyaman wa qu'udan wa ala junubihim wa yatafakkaruna fi khalqi as-samawati wal-ard — Those remember Allah standing sitting lying sides — all states — and reflect creation heavens earth.\n\nRabbana ma khalaqta hadha batilan Subhanaka faqina adhaba an-nar — Our Lord You did not create this without purpose — batilan — false, vain, play — creation purposeful.\n\nSubhanaka — Glory You — above vain.\n\nFaqina adhaba an-nar — Protect us from Fire — same dua muttaqin 16 protect from torment Fire.\n\nDhikr plus fikr — remembrance plus reflection — combine. Remember Allah standing sitting lying — time — reflect creation — space — together.\n\nThey reflect not only as scientists measure but as worshippers asking purpose.\n\nIf creation not vain, then gathering Day no doubt (9) purposeful, paradise best (15).\n\nThis du'a leads to chain supplications next.\n\nFor us: remembrance in all postures — practical: standing queue, sitting bus, lying bed — and reflection sky earth — night sky stars.\n\nNext Our Lord those You commit Fire disgraced.",
  "197": "Our Lord, those You admit to Fire — You have disgraced — wrongdoers will have no helpers. Rabbana innaka man tudkhilu an-nara fa-qad akhzaytah — Our Lord those You admit Fire You have disgraced — akhzaytah — disgrace.\n\nWa ma liz-zalimin min ansar — Wrongdoers will have no helpers — as earlier no helpers (22), no helpers disbelievers (10), fuel Fire.\n\nDisgrace vs honour earlier Tu'izzu man tasha Tudhillu (26) — admitting Fire is ultimate humiliation.\n\nAkhzaytah — disgrace — opposite honoured in world next (45) Isa honoured.\n\nSupplication shows fear disgrace more than pain? Both.\n\nLinks to earlier Fire prepared disbelievers (131) seek protection.\n\nNext Our Lord we heard caller.",
  "198": "Our Lord, we heard caller calling to faith — Believe in your Lord — so we believed — Our Lord forgive us our sins, expiate our evil deeds, and take us in death with righteous.\n\nRabbana innana sami'na munadiyan yunadi lil-imani an aminu bi-Rabbikum fa-amanna — We heard caller calling to faith — Munadi — caller — Muhammad? Or faith itself? Could be Quran caller, or fitrah.\n\nAn aminu bi-Rabbikum fa-amanna — Believe in Lord — so we believed — as earlier 16 we believed so forgive, 53 we believed revelations follow messenger write among witnesses.\n\nRabbana faghfir lana dhunubana wa kaffir anna sayyi'atina wa tawaffana ma'a al-abrar — Forgive sins, expiate evil deeds, take us in death with righteous — abrar — righteous.\n\nDhunu and sayyiat distinction: dhunub major, sayyiat minor? Forgive cover both.\n\nTawaffana ma'a al-abrar — Take us death with righteous — not just among but with — companionship.\n\nTawaffi — same word used for Isa I will take you (55).\n\nRequest join abrar implies desire righteous company.\n\nThis matches 16 forgive protect Fire, 53 write among witnesses, 147 forgive excess firm steps victory — now forgive expiate join righteous.\n\nContinuum supplications of ulu al-albab.\n\nNext grant what promised.",
  "199": "Our Lord, grant us what You promised through messengers and do not disgrace us on Day Resurrection — You never break promise.\n\nRabbana wa atina ma wa'adtana ala rusulika wa la tukhzina yawma al-qiyamah innaka la tukhlifu al-mi'ad — Grant what promised through messengers — paradise, victory, forgiveness — and do not disgrace us Day Resurrection — tukhzina — same root as akhzayt disgrace in Fire (197) — opposite.\n\nInnaka la tukhlifu al-mi'ad — You never break promise — same ending as earlier gathering Day no doubt Allah never breaks promise (9).\n\nMi'ad — appointment Day gathering.\n\nSupplications started (196) You did not create vain protect from Fire (196), disgrace those admitted Fire no helpers (197), heard caller believed forgive expiate take with abrar (198), now grant promised and not disgrace Day.\n\nChain logical: purpose, fear disgrace, faith call, request promised not disgrace.\n\nAll duas of ulu al-albab.\n\nNext Lord responded.",
  "200": "So their Lord answered them — I will not waste deed of any doer among you male or female — you are from one another — those who emigrated, were expelled from homes, were harmed in My path, fought and were killed — I will expiate their evil deeds and admit them Gardens rivers flowing — reward from Allah — Allah with Him excellent reward.\n\nFa-istajaba lahum Rabbuhum — So Lord answered them — immediate response — istajaba — same root as earlier Lord hears supplication near responds (2:186).\n\nAnni la udi'u amala amilin minkum min dhakarin aw untha ba'dukum min ba'd — Will not waste deed of any doer among you male female — you from one another — equal origin (34) descendants one another. No gender hierarchy in reward: male female equal.\n\nAlladhina hajaru wa ukhriju min diyarihim wa udhu fi sabili wa qatalu wa qutilu — Those emigrated — hajaru — as earlier emigrated and strove hope mercy (2:218), expelled homes — ukhriju — harmed in My path — udhu — fought killed — categories covering Uhud muhajirun.\n\nLa-ukaffiranna anhum sayyi'atihim wa la-udkhilannahum jannatin — Will expiate evil deeds admit Gardens — Rivers — as earlier reward forgiveness Gardens (132) excellent reward workers.\n\nThawaban min indi Allah — Reward from Allah — and with Him excellent reward — husn thawabi.\n\nThus divine answer to supplications: promise kept, no deed wasted, male female equal, emigration expulsion harm fighting killing leads to expiation Gardens.\n\nCloses circle opening favour believers raising messenger teaching purifying — now reward.\n\nNext final verses deceived prosperity disbelievers land brief enjoyment etc."
};
